 survey of modern human radial variation; an introduction to archeological and per-historic techniques of investigation regarding the changing physical form of humans. (Same as ANTG 1011).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139041, 530432, 'GEOG', '4018', 2020, 'Urban', 'A geographic approach to the study of urban areas stressing location, historical development, distribution, size, growth and function; emphasis on current urban problems. Prerequisite: GEOG 101-102.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139042, 788794, 'GEOG', '201', 2020, 'Introduction to Archeology', 'Survey of the history and development of archeology as a science, its place in the sciences, and an overview of the important material remains of past human life and activities in selected areas of the world. (Same as ANTG 2001.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139043, 172614, 'FCSC', '4037', 2020, 'Intermediate Studio', 'Individual design projects in a residential and/or commercial setting. Six hours laboratory or equivalent. Prerequisites: 2006, 3037.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139044, 640330, 'H&HP', '4035', 2020, 'Practicum in Physical Education (General)', 'Observation and participation in non-teaching physical education, recreational or health related programs for one semester. Prerequisite: Health and physical education major (general).', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139045, 109444, 'H&HP', '4038', 2020, 'Exercise Physiology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany KINS 437. Emphasis is given to demonstration of physiological responses to exercise testing, as well as other laboratory procedures unique to exercise science. Prerequisite: Credit for or concurrent enrollment in KINS 437. Kinesiology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139046, 926101, 'CJUS', '4015', 2020, 'Juvenile Delinquency and Justice', 'The nature, extent, and causes of juvenile delinquency; factors in its treatment and prevention, including community and agency programs; and analysis of the legal system as it applies to juveniles. (Same as SOCL 4015).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139047, 438860, 'KINS', '447', 2020, 'Community Health Education and Promotion Practicum', 'Provides student the opportunity to participate in a community health education or promotion programs for one semester. Prerequisite: KINS 4041.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139048, 411755, 'LATN', '303', 2020, 'Classical Mythology', 'Tales of the gods, heroes, and great families that have influenced literature, art, and music. (Same as ENGL 3093)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139049, 194376, 'H&HP', '4042', 2020, 'Health and Physical Education Program Development', 'This course is designed to foster the examination, discussion and creation of health physical education program development. Prerequisite: Permission of instructor. Education majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139050, 970598, 'H&HP', '4031', 2020, 'Methods and Materials in Health Education', 'Materials, techniques, and methods of teaching health in schools. Ten (10) hours of classroom observation will be completed during this course. Prerequisite: Must be admitted to teacher education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139051, 792910, 'H&HP', '437', 2020, 'Physiology of Exercise', 'Acute and chronic physiological changes in response to exercise. Emphasis on the practical application of exercise training for health, fitness, and- performance. Prerequisite: Junior standing. Kinesiology majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139052, 514201, 'KINS', '4041', 2020, 'Worksite Health Promotion', 'This course is designed to develop knowledge and awareness of the major issues in the field of worksite health promotiong programming, as well as to enhance the ability of future practitioners to develop the professional techniques necessary to fulfill wellness programming needs within corporate fitness/wellness field. Prerequisites: KINS 2011, 2041 and junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139053, 240201, 'H&HP', '4013', 2020, 'Management of Health, Physical Education, and Recr', 'The purpose and functions of the management process in the instructional and related area programs in todays classroom as well as experiences in those areas outside the normal classroom setting. Federal and state regulations in education, alternative programs, discipline and other current problems are discussed. Ten (10) hours of classroom observation will be completed during this course. Prerequisite: KINS 211 and Junior standing. (Formerly Administration and Health, Physical Education, and Recreation.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139054, 553209, 'H&HP', '417', 2020, 'School and Multicultural Health', 'School and cultural health problems for school aged children and current programs of prevention and protection against disease. Prerequisite: junior standing. Education majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139055, 261290, 'H&HP', '4008', 2020, 'Physical Activity for Students With Special Needs', 'This course examines how physical activities and motor skills can be tasked analyzed and modified to include a wide range of individuals with special needs. Basic knowledge, skills and competencies in Special Education are covered with an emphasis in pedagogical principles.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139056, 553147, 'BIOL', '469', 2020, 'General VIrology Laboratory', 'A laboratory to accompany 4068. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit with \"C\" or better or registration in 4068.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139057, 122274, 'KINS', '355', 2020, 'Lifetime Sports', 'Basic skills, rules, strategies, and teaching procedures of selected individual lifetime sports. Prerequisite: Health and physical education major.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139058, 492451, 'H&HP', '406', 2020, 'Advanced Driver Education', 'Curriculum innovations and instructional devices (with lab). In-depth study of curriculum materials and instructional devices and techniques including simulation, multi-media, driving range, on-street instruction, and motorcycle. Instruction in the use of all forms supplied by the State Department of Education. Prerequisites: KINS 3025 and junior standing.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139059, 163489, 'H&HP', '3033', 2020, 'Activities for Elementary School', 'Materials, techniques and methods of teaching physical education in elementary schools. Sophomore level and above.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139060, 759876, 'H&HP', '3004', 2020, 'Coaching Track and Field', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching track and field. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139061, 890802, 'H&HP', '3003', 2020, 'Coaching Baseball and Softball', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching baseball and softball. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139062, 906730, 'KINS', '335', 2020, 'Team Sports', 'Basic skills, strategies, rules, and teaching procedures of selected team sports. Prerequisite: Health and physical education major.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139063, 906730, 'KINS', '3035', 2020, 'Team Sports', 'Basic skills, strategies, rules, and teaching procedures of selected team sports. Prerequisite: Health and physical education major.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139064, 693551, 'H&HP', '3002', 2020, 'Coaching Basketball', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching basketball. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing. ', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139065, 305606, 'H&HP', '2056', 2020, 'Living With Health', 'Content and theory related to basic health information; critical health issues; improving and maintaining optimal health and wellness. Students with prior credit in Kinesiology 241 are not eligible to receive credit in Kinesiology 256. Cannot be used to satisfy major or minor requirements.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139066, 398321, 'H&HP', '3001', 2020, 'Coaching Football', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching football. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139067, 354444, 'H&HP', '2043', 2020, 'Scuba Diving', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning scuba diving.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139068, 310064, 'H&HP', '2048', 2020, 'Officiating', 'Principles, techniques and practices of officiating with emphasis on rules, rule interpretations and mechanics of basketball and football. Practical experience will be arranged.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139069, 566603, 'H&HP', '2049', 2020, 'Officiating Spring Sports', 'This course is designed to enhance the students ability to understand the basic principles, techniques, and practices of officiating youth sports with emphasis on rules, rule interpretations, and mechanics for Dixie League softball/baseball, FIFA U6-U19 soccer, and USTA tennis.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139070, 146706, 'KINS', '3018', 2020, 'Fitness Assessment Techniques', 'This course is designed to provide the exercise professional with the necessary cognitive and laboratory experiences essential for developing safe and accurate physical fitness testing practices. Prerequisite: KINS 2011. Kinesiology majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139071, 440761, 'H&HP', '2041', 2020, 'Personal and Community Health', 'An orientation course in health which deals with nutrition, stress, exercise, diseases and their prevention.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139072, 394389, 'H&HP', '233', 2020, 'Water Safety Instruction', 'Qualifies individuals to teach and certify American Red Cross Aquatic courses. Prerequisite: 2020.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139073, 487484, 'HLST', '207', 2020, 'Nutrition', 'Application of principles of basic nutrition throughout the life cycle. Emphasis is on the relationship to health and disease.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139074, 209018, 'H&HP', '2001', 2020, 'First Aid Andcpr', 'First aid to the victims of accidents, sudden illness, cardiac or respiratory emergencies. First aid and CPR certification granted to those meeting agency requirements. Two hours laboratory. (Formerly First Aid and Personal Safety.)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139075, 17515, 'H&HP', '161', 2020, 'Weight Training I (Women)', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning weight training. For women only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139076, 981856, 'H&HP', '153', 2020, 'Self Defense I', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning self defense.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139077, 262046, 'KINS', '1045', 2020, 'Basketball', 'Skills, techniques, knowledges of beginning basketball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139078, 257144, 'H&HP', '1038', 2020, 'Racquetball', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning raquetball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139079, 404616, 'KINS', '1014', 2020, 'Jazz Dance I', 'The study of jazz techniques with emphasis on style and rhythmic design.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139080, 845758, 'H&HP', '1017', 2020, 'Softball', 'Skill, techniques, and knowledges of beginning softball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139081, 326487, 'H&HP', '1018', 2020, 'Volleyball', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning volleyball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139082, 515770, 'KINS', '253', 2020, 'Self Defense II', 'Continued instruction and practice in the various aspects of self defense.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139083, 799611, 'H&HP', '1011', 2020, 'Archery', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning archery.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139084, 880246, 'H&HP', '1013', 2020, 'Bowling I', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning bowling.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139085, 864043, 'H&HP', '119', 2020, 'Weight Training I (Men)', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning weight training. For men only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139086, 991249, 'AGRB', '344', 2020, 'Agribusiness Practicum', 'Design, plan, and execute an approved agribusiness enterprise. May be used for elective credit only. May be repeated. (Formerly AGRI 344) Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139088, 835752, 'H&HP', '1006', 2020, 'Tennis I', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning tennis.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139089, 835752, 'H&HP', '106', 2020, 'Tennis I', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning tennis.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139090, 966990, 'H&HP', '109', 2020, 'GOLF I', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning golf.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139091, 504186, 'H&HP', '1008', 2020, 'Soccer', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning soccer.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139092, 698562, 'ACCT', '440', 2020, 'Law for Accountants', 'Specifically for accounting majors. Legal concepts underlying business organizations, contracts, debtor-creditor relationships, government regulation of business, the uniform commercial code, property and professional and legal responsibilities. Can be used as a preparation for the CPA examination. Prerequisite: 4001. F, Sp (Formerly ACCT 440.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139093, 698562, 'ACCT', '4040', 2020, 'Law for Accountants', 'Specifically for accounting majors. Legal concepts underlying business organizations, contracts, debtor-creditor relationships, government regulation of business, the uniform commercial code, property and professional and legal responsibilities. Can be used as a preparation for the CPA examination. Prerequisite: 4001. F, Sp (Formerly ACCT 440.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139094, 652273, 'AGEC', '2003', 2020, 'Agricultural Marketing', 'The principles and methods of marketing agricultural products and the institutions performing the various functions in the marketing of various commodities. Current trends and developments in the agricultural marketing process. (Formerly AGEC 203)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139095, 651376, 'AGRB', '3010', 2020, 'Agricultural Finance', 'Principles of agricultural finance emphasizing costs and returns from capital and credit, various types and sources of credit, development, characteristics and role of agricultural lending institutions. (Formerly AGEC 310) Prerequisite: Minimum grade of &quot;C&quot; in AGRB 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139096, 321995, 'GOVM', '4057', 2020, 'Contemporary Political Thought', 'Political thought of the twentieth century; liberalism, modern totalitarianism, conservatism, Freudianism, existentialism, and democracy.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139097, 695003, 'POLS', '4063', 2020, 'Comparative Politics of Race and Ethnicity', 'International comparative analysis of how political processes both shape and are shaped by racial and ethnic differences, both within and among nation-states. Prerequisite: 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139098, 625620, 'POLS', '464', 2020, 'Internship in Political Science', 'Field experience under the general supervision of a faculty memeber and the direct supervision of a professional in the field, with academic components including a final paper and presentation. (Same as SOCL 4064.)', 3.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139099, 773108, 'AGRB', '311', 2020, 'Agricultural Price Analysis and Forcasting', 'Basic treatment of agricultural price analysis tools. Emphasis is placed on computer software and problem recognition. Course lectures concentrate on local commodities. (Formerly AGEC 311)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139100, 552735, 'AGEC', '3005', 2020, 'Farm Business Records', 'Fundamental principles for assimilation, organization, and analyses of farm records as applied to decision-making processes. Utilization of computers in farm records and accounting will be stressed. (Formerly AGEC 305) Prerequisite: Minimum grades of &quot;C&quot; in AGRB 1001, 2001, and 2003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139101, 651376, 'AGEC', '310', 2020, 'Agricultural Finance', 'Principles of agricultural finance emphasizing costs and returns from capital and credit, various types and sources of credit, development, characteristics and role of agricultural lending institutions. (Formerly AGEC 310) Prerequisite: Minimum grade of &quot;C&quot; in AGRB 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139102, 78034, 'POLS', '4093', 2020, 'Directed Study: Public Administration and Law (Formerly 491B)', 'Directed study and/or research in selected areas of government. Prerequisite: Advanced standing, approval of department head, and permission of the instructor. (Formerly 491B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139103, 725649, 'POLS', '4061', 2020, 'International Political Economy', 'A course focused on the intersection of politics and economies in relations among actors in the international environment. Main topics include: international trade strategies; the political strategies of transnational firms; assessment of international organization; the role of the Uited States in the contemporary global economy. Prerequisite: 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139104, 725649, 'POLS', '461', 2020, 'International Political Economy', 'A course focused on the intersection of politics and economies in relations among actors in the international environment. Main topics include: international trade strategies; the political strategies of transnational firms; assessment of international organization; the role of the Uited States in the contemporary global economy. Prerequisite: 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139105, 83591, 'GOVM', '4041', 2020, 'Comparative Govt and Politics in Latin America', 'A comparative survey of governmental institutions and political processes which characterized the Latin American republics from the colonial period to the present. (Formerly 306.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139106, 795337, 'GOVM', '4053', 2020, 'International Politics', 'The nation-state system, power politics, processes affecting international relations; sources of tension in international politics and possibilities of their peaceful resolution. (Formerly 315.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139107, 961005, 'GOVM', '4029', 2020, 'Women and Politics', 'An examination of the role that women have played in the development of the U.S. political system, including historical analysis of the barriers to womens participation and the impact of politically active women on contemporary issues.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139108, 68286, 'GOVM', '440', 2020, 'Comparative', 'The structure, theory, organization, and methods of control in the governments of the major European powers; recent political trends. Prerequisite: 2001. (Formerly 305.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139109, 531276, 'GOVM', '4023', 2020, 'American Urban Politics', 'An analysis of the structure and functions of contemporary city governments with considerable attention devoted to basic problems. Special emphasis on local government in Louisiana. (Formerly 307.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139110, 693779, 'GOVM', '4020', 2020, 'Louisiana Government and Politics', 'Development and organization of political processes in Louisiana; contemporary problems of Louisiana state and local governments. (Formerly 302.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139111, 547805, 'POLS', '4018', 2020, 'Constitutional Law and Criminal Justice', 'Study of constitutional law and its applicability in the criminal justice system. Prerequisite: POLS 2001. (Same as CJUS 4018) (Formerly GOVM/CJUS 421.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139112, 720669, 'POLS', '4017', 2020, 'Public Administration and Administrative Law', 'Structure and processes of public administration, practices and processes of public administration, practices in personnel, organization and development of administrative law. Prerequisite: POLS 2001. (Formerly 309.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139113, 533147, 'POLS', '4013', 2020, 'Constitutional Law: Governmental Powers', 'A study of the U.S. Constitution through analysis of decisions of the Supreme Court. The cases demonstrate the nature of judicial function, the nature of the federal system, and the scope and character of the process of the national government. Prerequisite: POLS 2001 or approval of department head and permission of the instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139114, 787621, 'POLS', '407', 2020, 'Western Political Theory', 'A study of political theory beginning with Plato and the ancient Greeks and continuing through the Middle Ages, Reformation, and Enlightenment to Marx, Mills and the modern age. The central questions of political thought are explored e.g., what is the good3; what is justice3; how is political authority acquired3; where does sovereignty reside0; and how do we incur obligations3 Prerequisite: POLS 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139115, 964366, 'POLS', '404', 2020, 'Global Environmental Politics', 'Global Environmental Politics analyzes transnational environmental issues, such as climate change, species and habitat loss, water and air pollution, and waste management, from a cross-cultural, multi-disciplined approach with an emphasis on policy development and implementation issues. Prerequisite: POLS 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139116, 234751, 'GOVM', '2006', 2020, 'Introduction to Paralegal Studies', 'Students are introduced to the structure and workings of the law firm, especially the important aspects of law office practices, which include investigation and research techniques. Prerequisite: GOVM 205.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139118, 801432, 'SPCH', '3030', 2020, 'Persuasion', 'A review of general theoretical approaches to persuasion and influence with focus on principles of persuasive communication and application of persuasive strategies. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3030)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139119, 999533, 'CONS', '460E', 2020, 'Directed Study: Special Contracting Methods (Formerly CONS 460E)', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. Directed individual study. Prerequisite: Approval of director. (Formerly CONS 460E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139120, 404616, 'H&HP', '1014', 2020, 'Jazz Dance I', 'The study of jazz techniques with emphasis on style and rhythmic design.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139121, 618202, 'GOVM', '2005', 2020, 'Introduction to Paralegal Studies', 'Students are introduced to the structure and workings of the law firm, especially the important aspects of law office practices, which include investigation and research techniques.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139122, 163450, 'GOVM', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Directed study and/or research in selected areas of government. A. National, State, and Local; B. Public Administration and Law; C. Political Theory; D. International Relations; E. Comparative; F. Political Processes. Prerequisite: Advanced standing, approval of department head, and permission of the instructor.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139123, 565721, 'MLSC', '3044', 2020, 'Directed Study: Blood Banking (Formerly CLSC 338D)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems in blood banking. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338D)', 1.0000, 