and Social Sciences requirements, with the permission of the department head and/or instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139437, 50047, 'PSYC', '4099', 2020, 'Advanced General Psychology', 'The capstone experience for psychology majors, integrating and expanding upon knowledge gained from specialty courses. Prerequisite: 30 hours in psychology.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139438, 44788, 'MLSC', '3047', 2020, 'Directed Study: Toxicology (Formerly CLSC 338H)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems in toxicology. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338H)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139439, 44788, 'CLSC', '338H', 2020, 'Directed Study: Toxicology (Formerly CLSC 338H)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems in toxicology. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338H)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139440, 277033, 'SOCL', '424', 2020, 'Women and Aging', 'Examines the life experiences of women as they age. Emphasis is on sociological influences on perceptions of aging among women and on aging womens roles in society. (Same as GERO 4024)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139441, 977044, 'TOXI', '4043', 2020, 'Industrial Hygiene Laboratory', 'A laboratory dedicated to the practical application of information disseminated in Toxicology 4044. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in 4042. Toxicology majors only. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139442, 977044, 'TOXI', '443', 2020, 'Industrial Hygiene Laboratory', 'A laboratory dedicated to the practical application of information disseminated in Toxicology 4044. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in 4042. Toxicology majors only. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139443, 309289, 'EQSC', '3045', 2020, 'Equine Marketing and Sales', 'Practical concepts and experience in marketing horses, including analysis of pedigrees, evaluation of conformation, production costs, assessing the market, targeting customers, preparing and presenting the horse. One hour lecture and three hours laboratory. Prerequisites: EQSC 201 and 220.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139444, 252993, 'EQSC', '3060', 2020, 'Equine Nutrition and Genetics', 'Principles and practice of equine nutrition and genetics, including digestive systems, digestive disturbances, feeding, heredity, and coat color. Two hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: EQSC 201.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139445, 631810, 'EQSC', '3050', 2020, 'Equine Reproduction', 'Principles of equine reproduction, including the reproductive tracts, breeding cycles, methods of breeding, pregnancy, and foaling; and common equine reproductive management practives. Two hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: EQSC 201. (Formerly EQSC 340 and 341)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139446, 252993, 'EQSC', '360', 2020, 'Equine Nutrition and Genetics', 'Principles and practice of equine nutrition and genetics, including digestive systems, digestive disturbances, feeding, heredity, and coat color. Two hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: EQSC 201.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139447, 790687, 'EQSC', '4001', 2020, 'Equine Enterprises', 'A study and analysis of the various equine enterprises, including business planning, contracts, revenue sources, expenses, and facilities management. Three hours lecture. Prerequisite: EQSC 201.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139448, 790687, 'EQSC', '401', 2020, 'Equine Enterprises', 'A study and analysis of the various equine enterprises, including business planning, contracts, revenue sources, expenses, and facilities management. Three hours lecture. Prerequisite: EQSC 201.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139449, 651538, 'EQSC', '4020', 2020, 'Therapeutic Equitation', 'Individualized instruction on basic horsemanship as it relates to therapeutic horseback riding. Specific areas include safety, equipment, riding, anatomy/conformation, techniques of instruction, and familiarization of rider capabilities, limitations, and disabilities.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139450, 150671, 'HLST', '3001', 2020, 'Healthcare Ethics', 'This course is designed to introduce ethical thinking and concepts regarding healthcare to prepare the student to understand, evaluate, and participate in ethical decision-making. Coursework presents professional codes of ethics using group discussions. Ethic related topics to be included such as genetics, transplant, cloning, etc. Prerequisites: PSYC 2001 or SOCL 1001 or 1002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139451, 335302, 'HLST', '3003', 2020, 'Health Practicum I', 'This is a professional development course, as well as preparation for Health Science Practicum II. Students select an agency and develop personal goals and objectives appropriate to the setting, population, and health issues. Under supervision in an approved agency, students have the opportunity for on-the-job experiences. Students have the opportunity to &quot;shadow&quot; individuals who are performing their jobs on a daily basis. The organization can involve the student in productive activities, which benefit the agency and enhance the student&#39;s learning experience. The practicum is generally performed in the student&#39;s junior year. Prerequisites: College of Health Sciences majors only. ENGL 3021 or BUSN 3005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139452, 465573, 'CLSC', '1003', 2020, 'Principles of Renal Function and Urinalysis', 'The morphology, anatomy and physiology of renal system, and principles of urinalysis. One hour lecture. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139453, 399563, 'AVIA', '3030', 2020, 'Aviation Professionalism', 'Aviation career opportunities and career paths; responsibilities of the aviation professional; professional ethics; decision-making; stress management; substance abuse. (Formerly 330)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139454, 364056, 'EQSC', '2020', 2020, 'Horse Handling Techniques', 'A study of proper horsemanship techniques including handling, riding, training techniques, and basic care. One hour lecture and three hours laboratory.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139455, 364056, 'EQSC', '220', 2020, 'Horse Handling Techniques', 'A study of proper horsemanship techniques including handling, riding, training techniques, and basic care. One hour lecture and three hours laboratory.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139456, 60092, 'HLST', '4005', 2020, 'Principles of Leadership in Healthcare', 'This course will provide an overview of leadership theories to prepare the student for a leadership/management role in healthcare. Prerequisites: junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139457, 596587, 'SPLP', '2002', 2020, 'Speech and Language Science', 'The production, transmission, and perception of acoustic signals in speech communication; and principles of linguistic analysis including phonology, semantics, morphology, syntax and pragmatics. (Formerly SPLP 242)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139458, 57129, 'HLST', '4002', 2020, 'Healthcare Law', 'This course examines healthcare law and the legal system, and the interplay between law and ethics; The course will examine federal mandates and other aspects of patient confidentiality; Students will probe legal issues pertaining to healthcare topics, such as modes and institutions for providing medical care, liabitilty of selected providers, and review of applicable laws, rules, and regulations. Prerequisites: junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139459, 8503921, 'SPLP', '490', 2020, 'Neurophysiological Bases for Communication', 'Principles of anatomy and physiology of the normal neurological system as related to language and speech systems.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139460, 231453, 'CSCI', '1067', 2020, 'Software Applications', 'Work with three major computer application software packages - word processing, spreadsheets, and databases. Not applicable towards a degree in Computer Science or in the College of Business Administration.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139462, 434798, 'CLSC', '475A', 2020, 'Clinical Laboratory Science Problems', 'An introduction to emerging medical technologies and research in: A. Urinalysis; B. Hematology; C. Immunology; D. Blood Bank/Transfusion Medicine; E. Serology; F. Clinical Chemistry; H. Toxicology; I. Microbiology; J. Other associated areas of clinical laboratory science; K. Parasitology; and L. Clinical Laboratory Management. Prerequisite: Completion of three years of preclinical courses. F, Sp, Sum', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139463, 415960, 'SPCH', '491C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Speech Communication (Formerly CMST 491C)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisites: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139464, 415960, 'SPCH', '4091C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Speech Communication (Formerly CMST 491C)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisites: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139466, 933300, 'COMM', '1001', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Communication', 'Focus is on the total range of communication behaviors we engage in within the contexts of intrapersonal, interpersonal, small group, organizational, public speaking, and mass communication.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCOM 1013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139467, 933300, 'CMST', '1001', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Communication', 'Focus is on the total range of communication behaviors we engage in within the contexts of intrapersonal, interpersonal, small group, organizational, public speaking, and mass communication.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCOM 1013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139468, 720962, 'RELG', '321', 2020, 'Religions of the World', '3 credits each (320-321) A systematic analysis of the origins, doctrines, and practices of the major world religions. Particular attention will be given to the philosophical foundations of each religion. (Same as PHIL 320-321)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139469, 605041, 'AGEC', '4022', 2020, 'Community and Rural Development', 'Theory and practical application of economic principles to the problems faced in community and rural development. Rerequisite: AGEC 201 or ECON 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139470, 919477, 'BIOL', '419', 2020, 'Advanced Concepts in Genetic and Molecular Biology', 'An advanced level course in genetics with a focus on DNA structure and function, gene expression, protein function, human genetics, and biotechnology. An emphasis is placed on current topics and emerging biomedical technologies. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in BIOL 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139471, 867179, 'BIOL', '430', 2020, 'DNA Analysis in Molecular Biology', 'A laboratory- based course focused on generating and analyzing DNA data. Methods include introductions, protocols and trouble shooting for PCR, RAPDs, DNA sequencing, alignment and phylogentic analyses. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 3005.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139472, 836271, 'CNST', '1002', 2020, 'CNST 102', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139473, 414715, 'CMST', '311', 2020, 'Argumentation and Debate', 'Argumentation as a method for critical inquiry. Emphasis on debate as argument exemplar with instruction in analysis, reasoning, and use of evidence. Participation in debates. Prerequisite: COMM 2001 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3011)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139474, 33246, 'SPCH', '3035', 2020, 'Nonverbal Communication', 'The process of generating and interpreting messages from such nonverbal sources as space, physical appearance, time, facial expressions, and other nonverbal codes explored for effects on interpersonal relationships. Prerequisite: COMM 1018, 2001 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3035)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139475, 832657, 'MCOM', '452', 2020, 'Digital Cinema', 'Theory and techniques of video production from conception to completion, for a variety of mass communications applications. One hour lecture, four hours studio. Additional course fee. Prerequisite: Senior standing, graduate standing, or consent of instructor. (Formerly MCOM 4052)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139476, 281264, 'CMST', '304', 2020, 'Intercultural Communication', 'An international perspective on communication between members of different cultures. Verbal and nonverbal code systems, social patterns, values, and belief systems examined as they affect the sharing of meaning. Special attention given to Health Care, Business, and Education contexts. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. May not be used as a substitute for a foreign language. (Formerly CMST 4004)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139477, 934543, 'CMST', '3041', 2020, 'Communication and Gender', 'Exploration of how gender and communication interact, how gender influences communication, how gender is communicated, and how communication influences our understandings of gender and what it means to be gendered beings. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3041)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139478, 960977, 'SPCH', '426', 2020, 'Health Communications', 'The study of communication perspectives and skills helpful in providing integrated, coordinated services between various allied health professions. Prerequisite: Junior standing.(Formerly CMST 4026)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139480, 65311, 'CMST', '452', 2020, 'Criticism of Contemporary Communication', 'This course examines various aspects of contemporary communication. Prerequisite: COMM\r\n3030 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4052)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139481, 511210, 'SPCH', '4050', 2020, 'Communciation Theory', 'An analysis and evaluation of predominant communication theories that identify fundamental communicative forces in human action. Prerequisite: COMM 1018, 2010 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4050)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139482, 270642, 'FRNH', '474', 2020, 'Second Language Acquisition', 'The application of second language acquisition theory in the classroom. Prerequisite: Spanish/French 4073.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139483, 896478, 'FRNH', '3021', 2020, 'Independent Reading', 'Directed reading in excerpts of French literature, with continued emphasis on understanding, speaking, reading and writing French. Prerequisite: 2001.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139484, 896478, 'FRNH', '321', 2020, 'Independent Reading', 'Directed reading in excerpts of French literature, with continued emphasis on understanding, speaking, reading and writing French. Prerequisite: 2001.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139485, 417762, 'RADT', '310', 2020, 'Patient Care Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany RADT 3009. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139486, 605041, 'AGRB', '4022', 2020, 'Community and Rural Development', 'Theory and practical application of economic principles to the problems faced in community and rural development. Rerequisite: AGEC 201 or ECON 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139487, 62000, 'AVIA', '4096', 2020, 'Directed Study: Aerospace Research and Development (Formerly AVIA 491E)', 'Directed Study: Aerospace Research and Development. Maximum, 6 cr. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491E)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139488, 62000, 'AVIA', '491E', 2020, 'Directed Study: Aerospace Research and Development (Formerly AVIA 491E)', 'Directed Study: Aerospace Research and Development. Maximum, 6 cr. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491E)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139489, 185592, 'AVIA', '4094', 2020, 'Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Traffic Control (Formerly AVIA 491C)', 'Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Traffic Control. Maximum, 6 cr. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491C)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139490, 550544, 'AHSC', '430C', 2020, 'Interdisciplinary Studies', 'Interdisciplinary education for allied health and related areas. Students will utilize a problem-based learning approach. Prerequisite: 430A for 430B, 430B for 430C, or permission of instructor.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139491, 52513, 'AHSC', '430', 2020, 'Interdisciplinary Studies', '1 credit each. Interdisciplinary education for allied health and related areas. Students will utilize a problem-based learning approach. Prerequisite: 430A for 430B, 430B for 430C, or permission of instuctor.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139492, 89033, 'ART', '4066', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Surrealism in Art (Formerly ART 443G)', 'Seminar in Art History: Surrealism in Art. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443G)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139493, 198923, 'AVIA', '4092', 2020, 'Directed Study: Aviation Course Construction (Formerly AVIA 491A)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Directed Study: Aviation Course Construction. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139494, 768883, 'THEA', '3005', 2020, 'Advanced Theater Production Laboratory', 'Provides practice in the application of technical or performance skills in the execution of a major role or position of significant responsibility in TheatreWorks.ULM productions. Prerequisites: Permission of the Director of the Theater. Not designed to accompany any other course. May be repeated for up to three hours credit. F, Sp, Su', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139495, 626026, 'ARAB', '1003', 2020, 'Study Abroad', 'Application of language skills in a foreign language environment. Students will be involved in a total immersion living situation and will receive a minimum of fifteen clock hours per week in formal languae instruction. May be repeated with permission of the department head.', 3.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139496, 445623, 'ART', '4051', 2020, 'Advanced Printmaking', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Research problems in printmaking; choice of media. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisites: 1001, 1003; 2057, 2058, 2059 or 2060. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139497, 445623, 'ART', '451', 2020, 'Advanced Printmaking', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Research problems in printmaking; choice of media. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisites: 1001, 1003; 2057, 2058, 2059 or 2060. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139499, 946614, 'CINS', '3030', 2020, 'Enterprise Management Information Systems', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139500, 455071, 'SOCL', '4099', 2020, 'Senior Seminar', 'A capstone course for the sociology major. A small-group interdisciplinary approach to relevant issues in sociology research, writing, and presentation. Open to all majors. May be repeated for a maximum of 3 hours credit. Prerequisites: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139501, 456383, 'OCCT', '2000', 2020, 'Seminar: Professional Development', 'Foundations of the professional development of the occupational therapy assistant practitioner, and the exploration of personal, individual, and societal factors that contribute to the health professional-patient/client relationship. Prerequisite: 2.5 cumulative GPA (uncorrected). OCTA majors only. Su II', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139502, 365973, 'TOXI', '4042', 2020, 'Industrial Hygiene II', 'Continuation of Industrial Hygiene I. Detailed discussion of specific occupational hazards continues. Discussions include review of properties of the hazard, industrial exposure potential, exposure monitoring techniques, regulatory standards, and control methodologies. Discussion regarding indoor air quality, ergonomics issues, and industrial ventilation systems is included. Prerequisite: TOXI 4041. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139503, 177649, 'OCCT', '2004', 2020, 'Pre-Clinical Lab', 'Introduction to the role of the occupational therapy assistant in the clinical setting and exploration of the influence of personal perspectives, social systems, and culture on health, wellness, and occupational performance across the lifespan. Three contact hours of lab pre week. Prerequisite: 2.5 cumulative GPA (uncorrected). OCTA majors only. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139504, 423207, 'CODI', '4028', 2020, 'Articulation Disorders', 'Types, causes, symptoms, and therapy for articulatory defects in speech. Prerequisite: 4017, 4018, or consent of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139505, 423207, 'CODI', '428', 2020, 'Articulation Disorders', 'Types, causes, symptoms, and therapy for articulatory defects in speech. Prerequisite: 4017, 4018, or consent of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139506, 570302, 'RELG', '320', 2020, 'Religions of the World', '3 credits each (320-321) A systematic analysis of the origins, doctrines, and practices of the major world religions. Particular attention will be given to the philosophical foundations of each religion. (Same as PHIL 320-321)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139507, 551663, 'RELG', '340', 2020, 'Life and Teachings of Jesus of Nazareth', 'A study of the biblical accounts of the life and teachings of Jesus in their historical and cultural context. Prerequisite: RELG 208.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139508, 732449, 'RELG', '344', 2020, 'Life and Letters of Paul', 'Emphasis on the universally recognized Pauline literature with a focus on the theological innovations of Paul and his missionary penetration of the Greco- Roman world. Prerequisite: RELG 208.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139509, 74910, 'MUSC', '4006', 2020, 'Special Problems: Piano Pedagogy and Literature (Formerly MUSC 402D)', 'Investigative study of special problems by students with particular needs in music. Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated. (Formerly MUSC 402D)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 99.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139510, 840005, 'MUSC', '4099', 2020, 'The Classic Era', 'Upper level course designed for graduate students and advanced undergraduates. Topics include discussion of major composers, styles, and genres from the middle of the 18th century until the early 19th century. Composers and their works are situated within a larger cultural and historical context. Emphasis is placed on aural identification and written analysis of representative works. A research paper and accompanying assignments form a significant portion of the course grade. Students will be introduced to electronic resourses for music research. Prerequisite: MUSC 4092 or approval of the head of the Division of Music. Sp, even.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139511, 124133, 'RELG', '362', 2020, 'Christian Theology', 'An introduction to the biblical, historical, philosophical, and systematic aspects of Christian theology with emphasis on the current trends of theology as related to Universalism, Existentialism, and Liberation Theology.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139512, 373358, 'HIST', '492', 2020, 'Russia to 1917', 'Founding of the nation, tsarist institutions, conditions leading to the revolutions of 1917. Prerequisite: HIST 112. (Formerly 333.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139513, 812169, 'CHEM', '4020', 2020, 'Advanced Physical Chemistry', 'An introduction to group theory including molecular symmetry, molecular orbital theory, electronic spectroscopy, and vibrational spectroscopy. Three hours of lecture per week. Prerequisite: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 3022. F, even', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139515, 929134, 'FRNH', '4073', 2020, 'Applied Linguistics', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139516, 119393, 'SOCL', '3005', 2020, 'Popular Culture', 'An indepth examination of the forms of popular culture - activities that occupy our leisure time proliferation of these forms, and popular cultures impact on socialization, life-styles, and social change.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139517, 120221, 'SOCL', '4005', 2020, 'Theories of Crime and Delinquency', 'An analysis of the extent of crime and delinquency; impact of crime and elinquency on society; physical, social, and psychological causation of crime and delinquency; and current issues in criminology. (Same as CJUS 4005.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139518, 218260, 'PHYS', '415', 2020, 'Mechanics', 'Rigid bodies, vibrational systems, and advanced general methods. Prerequisites: PHYS 315; MATH 132.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139519, 433231, 'PHYS', '4006', 2020, 'Basic Physics Laboratory', 'Modern physics experiments in solid state, atomic and nuclear physics and selected experiments in departmental research areas. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisites: PHYS 405.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139520, 907408, 'PHYS', '4009', 2020, 'Optics', 'Principles and applications of geometrical and physical optics. Prerequisites: PHYS 208 and credit or registration in MATH 232.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139521, 907408, 'PHYS', '409', 2020, 'Optics', 'Principles and applications of geometrical and physical optics. Prerequisites: PHYS 208 and credit or registration in MATH 232.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139522, 46322, 'PHYS', '4010', 2020, 'Physics for Secondary Teachers', 'Elementary concepts of physics applicable to junior and senior high school science courses. Not applicable toward B.S. or M.S. degree in physics. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139523, 940651, 'PHYS', '4021', 2020, 'Research', 'Research problems that emphasize current progress in physics. Three hours of laboratory work per week per credit hour. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139524, 604392, 'PHYS', '4026', 2020, 'Analog Electronics Laboratory', 'Basic measurement techniques, filters, power supplies, diodes, transitors, and operational amplifiers. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisite: Registration or credit in PHYS 424.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139525, 864350, 'PHYS', '4033', 2020, 'Introductory Quantum Mechanics', 'The development of introductory quantum theory from a phenomenological point of view with applications to atomic physics and chemistry. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139526, 863783, 'NURS', '4041', 2020, 'Perioperative Nursing Theory', 'Advanced course focusing on the study of aseptic technique and care of patients in the operating room/recovery room. Emphasis is placed on perioperative concepts and principles. Prerequisites: NURS 3004, 3005 or 3007, 3006, or Registered Nurse licensure.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139527, 527347, 'PHYS', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Maximum, 6 cr. for undergraduates; Maximum, 3 cr. for graduates. Investigative and advanced study in: A. Advanced Mechanics, B. Electromagnetic Fields, C. Heat and Thermodynamics, D. Quantum Mechanics, E. Fluid Mechanics. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139528, 328077, 'PHYS', '2002', 2020, 'Descriptive Astronomy Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 2001. Two hours of laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in PHYS 2001.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139529, 564792, 'SOCL', '3000', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Selected studies in sociology. Content and credit varies. C. Sociological Imagination (Same as SOCL 101 and 102). D. Portrait of a Family (Same as SOCL 419). G. Beliefs and Believers. No more than 6 hours may be applied toward degree requirements.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139530, 203423, 'SOCL', '4044', 2020, 'Field Studies of Foreign Areas', 'Extended thematic field study outside the United States with guest lectures, tours, and assigned readings. A. Far East: B. Middle East; C. Latin America; D. Europe; E. England. Topics may not be repeated for credit.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139531, 633023, 'SOCL', '442', 2020, 'Field Studies of Foreign Areas', 'Extended field study tours of major foreign areas of the world. A. Western Europe; B. Northern Europe; C. South Pacific. Topics may not be repeated.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139532, 597475, 'SOCL', '4055', 2020, 'Sociology of Balanced Living', 'The study of factors influencing the socialization process, dynamics of relationships, and life satisfaction. Focus is on making choices and meeting challenges based on understanding of the interaction process and life skills training.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139533, 820518, 'PHYS', '3091', 2020, 'Directed Study', '3 credits each. Maximum, 6 credits. Investigative and advanced study in A. Theoretical Mechanics, B. Electrical Circuits, C. Modern Physics, D. Fluid Mechanics. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139534, 245550, 'PHYS', '4001', 2020, 'Heat and Thermodynamics', 'Principles and application of heat transfer and the laws of thermodynamics. Prerequisites: PHYS 208; MATH 232.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139535, 943088, 'PHYS', '3028', 2020, 'Popular Readings in Physics', 'Reading discussion of a popular work in the physics and physical science literature with a Physics professor. Maximum of 2 hours toward degree. Permission of Department Head required.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139536, 881225, 'PHYS', '3017', 2020, 'Electricity and Magnetism', 'The theory of electricity and magnetism as applied to the elements of electrical circuits. Prerequisites: PHYS 208, MATH 132.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139537, 958453, 'GEOS', '4021', 2020, 'Environmental Economics', 'Principles and methods for critically analyzing environmental issues from an economic and policy perspective. Review of current environmental issues with emphasis on agriculture related topics. Prerequisites: AGEC 201 or ECON 202 (Same as AGEC 421).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139538, 310851, 'GEOS', '4030', 2020, 'Surface Hydrology', 'Fundamentals of surface hydrology including: components of the hydrologic cycle; hydrographs; flood frequency analysis; and flood routing through rivers, reservoirs, and watersheds. Includes practical exercises and the use of personal computers. Prerequisites: GEOL 101 or permission of the instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139539, 720705, 'GEOS', '4040', 2020, 'Environmental Earth Science', 'A survey of the interactions between people and the physical environment, including hazardous earth processes, hydrology and pollution, waste disposal, environmental health, mineral resources, energy, and land use. Prerequisites: Any of the following--GEOS 101, 402, GEOL 101, 206, GEOG 213.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139540, 548967, 'GEOS', '4041', 2020, 'Geoenvironmental Seminar', '1 credit; maximum 3 credits. Geoenvironmental topics are examined in depth through library research, audiovisual materials analysis, and interactive software. Investigations are presented and critiqued during roundtable discussions. Assigned topics vary each semester. May be repeated for a maximum of 3 cr. Prerequisites: Any pertinent basic science course or permission of the instructor.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139541, 497469, 'GEOS', '4045', 2020, 'Advanced Geographic Information Systems (GIS)', 'A project-oriented course intended to demonstrate how principles learned in GEOS 435 can be applied to solving complex real-world problems. Prerequisite: GEOS 435.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139542, 837366, 'GEOS', '4060', 2020, 'Archeology and Geology of Natural Disasters', 'Case studies of archeological and geologic evidence for the history, causes, and effects of historical and prehistoric natural disasters. Use of archeological and geologic data to develop realistic supportable scenarios for the natural disasters will be stressed. Prerequisites: ANTG 201; GEOL 101 and 102.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139543, 923699, 'GEOS', '4061', 2020, 'Cooperative Education Experience', 'Planned and supervised work experience in students major field. Only open to juniors and seniors in the Department of Geosciences who are approved for the Cooperative Education Program. Grade of CR (credit) or NC (no credit) will be awarded. A. Atmospheric Science, B. Geography, C. Geology, D. Geophysics. May be repeated for a total of 3 credits. May not be applied to fulfill major requirement.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139544, 8919, 'PHYS', '315', 2020, 'Mechanics', 'Statics, kinematics, and dynamics. Prerequisites: PHYS 204 or 208; MATH 131.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139545, 811618, 'PHYS', '1005', 2020, 'Physics and Society', 'Readings and discusssions of current articles on the interactions of physics and society.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139546, 484460, 'PHYS', '1006', 2020, 'Physics and Society', 'Readings and discusssions of current articles on the interactions of physics and society.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139547, 328077, 'PHYS', '202', 2020, 'Descriptive Astronomy Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 2001. Two hours of laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in PHYS 2001.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139548, 403953, 'PHYS', '3008', 2020, 'Laboratory Techniques', 'Selected experiments in advanced physics. Three hours of laboratory per week. Prerequisite: PHYS 208.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139549, 403953, 'PHYS', '308', 2020, 'Laboratory Techniques', 'Selected experiments in advanced physics. Three hours of laboratory per week. Prerequisite: PHYS 208.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139550, 847041, 'PHYS', '3006', 2020, 'Health Physics', 'Medical aspects of radiation for students in the health professions including nuclear radiation, radiation protection for patients and medical personnel, and the effects of radiation on living systems. May not be applied to a major in physics or chemistry. Prerequisite: PHYS 204.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139551, 851990, 'PHYS', '3002', 2020, 'Radiological', 'The nature and use of X-Rays and radiological materials. May not be applied to a major in physics or chemistry. Prerequisite: PHYS 204.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139552, 216241, 'PHYS', '2020', 2020, 'History of Science', 'An introduction to the major influences of scientific thought and discovery on the course of history. Prerequisites: 3 cr. in introductory science.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139553, 236989, 'PHYS', '2022', 2020, 'Majors’ Introduction to the Physics Laboratory', 'How to use basic scientific instruments, such as the oscilloscope, and department facilities such as the VAX system (Maple) and the photo darkroom. Permission of the department head. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139554, 30541, 'PHYS', '2015', 2020, 'Photography', 'A descriptive treatment of optical principles of cameras, enlargers, and other lens systems utilized in modern processes of photography. Significance of f-stops, shutter times, and film speeds.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139555, 37446, 'PHYS', '2013', 2020, 'Acoustics of Music and Speech', 'A non- mathematical treatment of frequency, amplitude, and wavelength of sounds and their influence on pitch, loudness, and quality. Discussion of vibrating strings, membranes, and air columns as related to musical instruments and speech mechanisms.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139556, 661859, 'GEOS', '4016', 2020, 'Seminar', '1 credit; maximum, 3 credits. Presentation of oral and written reports on current geology literature and problems of special interest.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139557, 613961, 'GEOS', '4020', 2020, 'Human Impact On the Environment', 'This course will assess the environmental changes caused by human activity. Specifically, attention will be focused on human impacts on vegetation, animals, soil, hydrology, geomorphology, and climate. Prerequisite: GEOG 213 or GEOS 330 or permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139558, 280663, 'KINS', '4038', 2020, 'Exercise Physiology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany KINS 437. Emphasis is given to demonstration of physiological responses to exercise testing, as well as other laboratory procedures unique to exercise science. Prerequisite: Credit for or concurrent enrollment in KINS 437. Kinesiology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139559, 489272, 'GEOS', '3030', 2020, 'Introduction to Geomorphology', 'The recognition, classification, origin, and relationship of and forms.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139560, 939292, 'GEOS', '4004', 2020, 'Earth Science Laboratory', 'Two hours laboratory to accompany 402.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139561, 934169, 'GEOS', '4002', 2020, 'Principles of Earth Science', 'Earths place in the solar system; nature of material composing the earth; processes which have shaped and are shaping the earth; rocks, minerals, soils, topographic features and their origin; rock structures; topographic; geologic, and weather maps, and aerial photographs.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139562, 916772, 'GEOS', '3031', 2020, 'Geomorphology Laboratory', 'Three hours laboratory to accompany 330.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139563, 896831, 'GEOS', '4000', 2020, 'Directed Study-- E-Tv', 'Selected studies in Geosciences. Content varies. No more than 12 hours may be applied toward degree requirements. May not be applied to major in Geology. A. Planet Earth, C. Earth Revealed (Introductory Geology), D. Out of the Past: An Introduction to Archeology.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139564, 610052, 'GEOL', '4025', 2020, 'Sedimentation', 'The genesis, transportation, deposition, and classification of sediments; tectonic and environmental factors influencing deposition and sedimentary structure. Prerequisites: GEOL 211, 213.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139565, 931289, 'GEOL', '4026', 2020, 'Sedimentation Laboratory', 'Three hours laboratory to accompany 425.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139566, 112462, 'GEOL', '4029', 2020, 'Micropaleontology Laboratory', 'Six hours laboratory to accompany 419.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139567, 741481, 'GEOL', '4030', 2020, 'Coal', 'A study of the physical and chemical properties of the various ranks of coal, distribution, origin, microscopic analysis, utilization, evaluation, methods of extraction, and land reclamation. Prerequisites: GEOL 327, 329.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139568, 178796, 'GEOL', '4018', 2020, 'Planetary Geology', 'A survey of the geologic processes operating on the solid surface planetary bodies. Comparative geologic histories of the terrestrial planets and major satellites. Prerequisite: GEOL 303.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139569, 206449, 'GEOL', '4019', 2020, 'Micropaleontology', 'Study of foraminifera, their classification, morphology, environmental significance and use in correlation. Prerequisites: GEOL 211, 213.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139570, 310387, 'GEOL', '4023', 2020, 'X-Ray and Optical Mineral Analysis', 'Principles and techniques of mineral identification and analysis using the x-ray diffractometer and petrographic microscope. Prerequisites: GEOL 215, 217.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139571, 635750, 'GEOL', '4024', 2020, 'X-Ray and Optical Mineral Analysis Laboratory', 'Six hours laboratory to accompany 423.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139572, 546081, 'GEOL', '4015', 2020, 'Vertebrate Paleontology', 'A survey of the vertebrates through geologic time with special emphasis on morphology, function, evolution, time and spatial distribution. Prerequisites: GEOL 102, 104.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139573, 499478, 'MUSC', '4033', 2020, 'Chamber Singers', 'An auditioned choir drawn from the membership of Concert Choir that performs a wide range of repertoire and tours for ULM. Prerequisite: Approval of the director. May be repeated. Music and Music Education majors must enroll for zero credit.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 10.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139574, 374732, 'GEOL', '4007', 2020, 'Subsurface', 'Study and application of subsurface methods. Prerequisites: GEOL 303, 323.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139575, 314149, 'GEOL', '4008', 2020, 'Subsurface Laboratory', 'Six hours laboratory to accompany GEOL 407.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139576, 647093, 'GEOL', '4010', 2020, 'Geochemistry', 'Basic principles governing the origin, distribution, and migration of elements in the earth. Prerequisites: GEOL 215, 217.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139577, 340354, 'GEOL', '4013', 2020, 'Physical Marine', 'A general introduction to the physical processes at work on the shores of the Mississippi Sound, with emphasis on the erosional and depositional effects of waves and currents at various tidal stages. Conducted each summer under the direction of the staff of the Gulf Coast Marine Laboratory at Ocean Springs, Mississippi. Prerequisites: GEOL 327, 329, or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139578, 225827, 'GEOL', '4014', 2020, 'Chemical Marine', 'Supervised research in the chemistry of the water of the Mississippi Sound and the geochemistry of the bottoms beneath these waters. Conducted each summer under the direction of the staff of the Gulf Coast Marine Laboratory at Ocean Springs, Mississippi. Prerequisites: GEOL 327, 329, and CHEM 108, 111, 203, 204, or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139579, 476712, 'GEOL', '2015', 2020, 'Crystallography and Mineralogy', 'Principles of crystallography and mineral identification. Survey of the major ore- and rock-forming mineral groups. Prerequisites: GEOL 101, 103, and enrollment in or credit for CHEM 108, 111.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139580, 131429, 'GEOL', '2017', 2020, 'Crystallography and Mineralogy Laboratory', 'Six hours of laboratory to accompany 215.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139581, 673677, 'GEOL', '2020', 2020, 'Rocks and Minerals', 'Survey of the major ore minerals, rock-forming groups. Classification and occurrence of igneous sedimentary and metamorphic rocks. Prerequisites: GEOL 101, 103.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139582, 804310, 'GEOL', '2021', 2020, 'Rocks and Minerals Lab', 'Six hours of laboratory to accompany GEOL 220. Hand specimen identification of major mineral species and rocks. Field expenses: .00.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139583, 155351, 'GEOL', '3000', 2020, 'Geologic Field Methods', 'Instrumental methods, note- taking, and map preparation for field mapping. Course will include instruction and practice in compass and clinometer, hand-level, altimeter, plane table, and GPS methods, and use, handling, and care of the alidade and other instruments. Field expenses. Prerequisites: GEOL 200, GEOS 330 and 331, and MATH 112.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139584, 329204, 'GEOL', '3003', 2020, 'Structure', 'The recognition, description, classification, origin and relationships of geologic structures. Prerequisites: GEOL 102, 104, 215, 217, MATH 111, 112, Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139585, 22521, 'GEOL', '3009', 2020, 'Stratigraphy', 'Principles of biostratigraphy and lithostratigraphy, correlation methods, nomenclature, geochronology, paleoecology, facies, tectonics, and stratigraphic problems. Prerequisites: GEOL 211, 213.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139586, 863365, 'GEOL', '3023', 2020, 'Structure Laboratory', 'Three hours laboratory to accompany GEOL 303.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139587, 555102, 'GEOL', '3027', 2020, 'Petrology', 'Classification, origin, and occurrence of igneous, metamorphic, and sedimentary rocks. Prerequisites: GEOL 215, 217, and current enrollment in 329.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139588, 673419, 'GEOL', '3029', 2020, 'Petrology Laboratory', 'Three hours of laboratory to accompany 327. Field expenses: .00.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139589, 901662, 'GEOL', '3035', 2020, 'Crystals and Crystal Chemistry', 'Principles of crystallography. Origins and physiochemistry of minerals, igneous, metamorphic, and sedimentary rocks. Prerequisites: GEOL 220, 221.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139590, 124690, 'GEOL', '3036', 2020, 'Crystals and Crystal Chemistry Lab', 'Three hours of laboratory to accompany GEOL 335. Crystal notation and identification. Advanced techniques of rock and mineral identification. Field expenses: .00.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139591, 345741, 'GEOL', '4000', 2020, 'Geologic Mapping', 'Geologic and structural mapping and preparation of geologic maps. Written reports and maps are required. Three hours of laboratory per week and two extended field trips. Field expenses. Prerequisites: GEOL 300, 303, 309, 323, 335, 336.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139592, 648992, 'GEOL', '4001', 2020, 'Gulf Coast', 'The physiography, stratigraphy, structure, economics and origin of the Gulf Coastal province. Prerequisites: 303, 309, 323.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139593, 106744, 'GEOL', '4002', 2020, 'Plate Tectonics', 'A thorough treatment of the underlying processes driving the processes active in the solid earth, and how these processes affect modern interpretations of the geologic record. Prerequisites: GEOL 303, 309, 327, GEOS 330.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139594, 590514, 'GEOL', '4003', 2020, 'Petroleum', 'The origin, geologic distribution, and accumulation of petroleum. Prerequisites: GEOL 303, 323.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139595, 186618, 'GEOL', '4005', 2020, 'Economic Geology-- Metals', 'The origin and distribution of metallic ores. Prerequisites: GEOL 215, 217.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139596, 116662, 'GEOL', '4006', 2020, 'Economic Geology-- Non-Metals', 'The origin, distribution, geology, and use of non-metallic ores with emphasis on Louisianas economic minerals. Prerequisites: GEOL 215, 217.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139597, 620902, 'GEOL', '2013', 2020, 'Paleontology Laboratory', 'Three hours laboratory to accompany 211.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139598, 456955, 'GEOL', '2008', 2020, 'Engineering Laboratory', 'Two hours laboratory to accompany 206. Credit may not be earned in both GEOL 103 and 208.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139599, 403604, 'GEOL', '2011', 2020, 'Paleontology', 'Invertebrate fossils, classification, morphology, time and space, distribution, paleoecology, evolutionary trends, and their use in correlation. Prerequisites: GEOL 102, 104. Field expenses --.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139600, 412164, 'GEOL', '2006', 2020, 'Engineering Geology', 'Engineering properties of rocks, properties of soils, construction materials, earthquakes, earth movements, subsurface exploration and site selection for engineering works. Credit may not be earned in both GEOL 101 and 206.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139601, 590615, 'GEOG', '4014', 2020, 'Old World Archeology', 'A survey of the major archeological sequences of prehistoric Eurasia, Africa, and Oceania. (Same as GEOG 308.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139602, 965621, 'GEOG', '420', 2020, 'Latin American Field Course', 'Supervised geographic research and observation in a Latin American setting. Local examples illustrate broad themes in the historical shaping of the Latin American landscape. The course includes introductory meetings at ULM followed by field observation and discussion in a Latin American location. Prerequisite: GEOG 403 or permission of the department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139603, 223440, 'GEOG', '423', 2020, 'Archeological Field Techniques', 'A field course introducing the basic techniques of archeological mapping, excavation, cataloging, specimen preparation and preservation. A study of soils, physical stratigraphy, synecology, and techniques of artifact laboratory analysis. May be repeated once for a maximum of 12 hours credit. (Same as ANTG 423.)', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139604, 952968, 'GEOL', '2000', 2020, 'Geology in the Field', 'An introduction to the study of geology as conducted in the field. This course will integrate the review of the published geology of a region with observation and analysis of the geology found in the field as seen on required multi- day field trips to that region. The course will include an introduction to basic field methods and preparation of geologic reports. One hour of class per week and at least one extended field trip. Field expenses. Prerequisites: GEOL 101, 102, 103, 104, and registration in or completion of GEOL 220 and 221.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139605, 557870, 'GEOL', '1005', 2020, 'Geology of National Parks', 'A study of the processes and principles involved in geologic development of our national parks. Emphasis is placed on understanding and appreciating the special geologic features for which each park is famous. Prerequisite: 101.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139606, 672321, 'GEOG', '405', 2020, 'Africa', 'The geographical features, with particular reference to economic, social and political developments; a study of the heritage and background, physical and cultural, of the present-day Afro-American culture.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139607, 887193, 'GEOG', '410', 2020, 'The Archeology of Louisiana Indians', 'An introduction to the archeology of Louisianas Indian tribes from Paleo-Indian times (10,000 B.C.) through the historic period. Prerequisite: Junior or senior standing or permission of the instructor. (Same as ANTG 410.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139608, 982053, 'GEOG', '409', 2020, 'Asia', 'A survey of the physical environment of the continent as a whole, followed by a detailed study of China, India, and Japan.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139609, 127532, 'GEOG', '4015', 2020, 'Political Geography', 'Problems in production, trade, government, and world development growing out of geographic conditions. Prerequisite: GEOG 101-102.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139610, 127532, 'GEOG', '415', 2020, 'Political Geography', 'Problems in production, trade, government, and world development growing out of geographic conditions. Prerequisite: GEOG 101-102.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139611, 561712, 'GEOG', '4011', 2020, 'Honors Social Science', 'Discussion and investigation of topics in anthropology, econimics, geography, political science, psychology, or sociology. Course content varies and may link two or more of these disciplines. Prerequisites: Admisson to the Honors Program or permission of the University Honors Council. (May be repeated for up to six hours of credit.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139612, 109376, 'GOVM', '201', 2020, 'American National Government', 'Consideration of the nature of democracy, civil rights, federalism, the political process, the legislative, executive, and judicial branches, and current problems.<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CPOL 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139613, 109376, 'GOVM', '2001', 2020, 'American National Government', 'Consideration of the nature of democracy, civil rights, federalism, the political process, the legislative, executive, and judicial branches, and current problems.<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CPOL 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139614, 695928, 'GRMN', '2001', 2020, 'Intermediate German I', 'A continuation of 1001-1002, with an increased emphasis upon reading and discussion. Work in the computerized Language Learning Center is required. Prerequisite: 1002 or 1005.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CGRM 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139615, 218210, 'GEOG', '2015', 2020, 'Cartography', 'Development of cartography, techniques, nature, and usage of map projections; interpretation of maps; map construction.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139616, 708015, 'GEOG', '3001', 2020, 'Cultural Geography', 'An advanced course focusing on the study of culture and the expression of material culture in the landscape. Prerequisite: GEOG 1001 or, 1002 or, 2003 or permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139617, 655526, 'GEOG', '2014', 2020, 'Physical Geography Laboratory', 'Two hours laboratory to accompany Geography 2013.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139618, 655526, 'GEOG', '214', 2020, 'Physical Geography Laboratory', 'Two hours laboratory to accompany Geography 2013.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139619, 650899, 'GEOG', '3020', 2020, 'Conservation Geography', 'Problems and techniques of conservation in agriculture, forestry, industry, mining, water, air, and the urban environment. Investigation of conservation ideology and political action. Emphasis on North America with some study of international phenomena. Prerequisite: GEOG 1001 or GEOL 1001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139620, 569587, 'GEOG', '403', 2020, 'Latin America', 'A regional study of the configuration, climates, natural resources, cultural patterns, and peoples.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139622, 964452, 'PHYS', '3010', 2020, 'Digital Electronics', 'Digital electronics including gates, Boolean algebra, combinational logic, binary number operations, flip-flops, latches, and counters. Prerequisite: PHYS 2004 or 2008.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139623, 784146, 'FINA', '3023', 2020, 'Real Estate Finance and Investments', 'The principles of finance as applied to the real estate business; financial institutions, sources of financing, brokerage, property development, analysis of real estate investment, and current development in real estate. Prerequisite: 303 or approval of instructor. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139624, 368555, 'FINA', '4009', 2020, 'Real Estate Appraisal', 'Fundamentals of appraising residential, commercial, and industrial real estate. Prerequisite: 303, CONS 210, or approval of instructor. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139625, 592248, 'FINA', '4011', 2020, 'Real Estate Law', 'Legal principles affecting ownership and/or management of real property in general, with special emphasis placed in Louisiana Law. Specific areas include transfers, deeds, leases, land contracts, escrows, title insurance, foreclosures, zonings, and recordings. Prerequisite: 303 or approval of instructor. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139626, 41291, 'FINA', '4013', 2020, 'Urban Development', 'Measurement of urban obsolescence and deterioration. Planning concepts used to guide contemporary urban growth and alleviate common problems. Governmental programs influencing urban development, including technical and financial assistance. Specific topics include comprehensive plans, zoning, land development, parks and school location. Prerequisite: ECON 201, 202. Sp, even', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139627, 208738, 'MGMT', '4005', 2020, 'Motion Economy and Time Analysis', 'Principles of motion economy as related to the human body, the work place, and tools and equipment. Techniques of making time and motion studies; development of setup standards on machine performance; time study as a basis of cost control. Prerequisite: MGMT 301. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139628, 19757, 'MGMT', '4007', 2020, 'Collective Bargaining', 'Process of developing and administering agreements between labor and management concerning terms and conditions of employment. Theoretical analysis research reports, and actual bargaining. Prerequisite: 301 and Senior standing or approval of department head. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `courses` VALUES (139631, 181405, 'FINA', '2003', 2020, 'Principles of Real Estate', 'Purchasing, leasing, developing, and operating real estate; interest, liens, contracts, deeds, titles, and recording as related to individuals, corporations and estates. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139632, 181405, 'FINA', '203', 2020, 'Principles of Real Estate', 'Purchasing, leasing, developing, and operating real estate; interest, liens, contracts, deeds, titles, and recording as related to individuals, corporations and estates. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139633, 761380, 'FINA', '4014', 2020, 'Capital Market Seminar', 'Application of principles of bank operations and operations of other financial institutions. Group discussions of capital adequacy, financial liquidity, legal environment, capital market institutions, funds management, and other topics. Prerequisite: 315 and ECON 301.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139634, 489867, 'ECON', '4010', 2020, 'Economics of Aging', 'An examination of issues related to the economic status of persons as they grow older. Attention will be given to problems and policies which relate to income maintenance planned and unplanned expenditures, inflation, reduced income, post-retirement employment, public and private pensions, health insurance, pre-retirement counseling and legislative reforms. Prerequisite: 201 or SOCL 101 or permission of instructor. (Formerly 510) F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139635, 234644, 'MGMT', '309', 2020, 'Operations Management', 'Examines the production function and its applicability to business operations and scientific decision processes. Includes forecasting and scheduling, and project, quality, capacity, and inventory management. Prerequisites: 3001 or 3005; MATH 1016; or consent of management program coordinator. F, Sp, Sum<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CMGM 3213', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139636, 923432, 'AGRO', '301', 2020, 'Resource Conservation and Management', 'Designing and laying out conservation practices necessary to reduce erosion. Emphasis will be placed upon surveying, mapping, drainage, terracing, water impoundment and safe water movement. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: MATH 1011. (Formerly AGMC 301).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139638, 589906, 'ECON', '4007', 2020, 'History of Economic Thought', 'An analytical study of the development of economic thought; the influence of the mercantilists and physiocrats; emphasis given classical and neoclassical doctrines as reflected in modern theory, analytical techniques, and current thinking. Prerequisite: 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139639, 539444, 'ECON', '4009', 2020, 'Government Regulation and Control', 'Economic principles as applied to government regulation of business. The impact of legislation and commission regulation on public policies. The regulatory effect of tax laws. Prerequisite 201, 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139640, 790295, 'ECON', '4003', 2020, 'Public Sector Economics', 'Theory and practice of local, state, and federal government expenditures and revenues; shifting and incidence of the various forms of taxation; consideration of the integrating of revenues and expenditures into fiscal policy and reform. Prerequisite: 201, 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139641, 572453, 'ECON', '4001', 2020, 'Current Problems', 'Current problems of economic life and possible solutions; analysis of present policies of government and industry as such policies are influenced by foreign economic organization and cooperation. Prerequisite: 201, 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139642, 412466, 'ECON', '3091', 2020, 'Survey of Principles', 'A combined micro-macro course designed primarily for non-business majors, or advanced students who are deficient in Economic principles. Prerequisite: Open only to non-business majors, and those who have not received credit for Economics 201 or 202. Prerequisite: junior standing. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139643, 709033, 'ECON', '3015', 2020, 'Comparative Economic Systems', 'Analytical study of economic problems of, and the theoretical framework under, different economics systems. Prerequisite: 201, 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139644, 21422, 'ECON', '3009', 2020, 'Labor Law and Legislation', 'Current position of public regulation in labor relations; economic analysis of legislative, executive, and judicial actions to determine rights, duties, and responsibilities of labor unions and employers. Prerequisite: 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139645, 343689, 'ECON', '3005', 2020, 'Business Cycles and Forecasting', 'General characteristics of business cycles and theories as to their cause. Fluctuations in economic activity, their importance, principal explanations suggested, and proposed remedies. Methods of estimating the probable degree and direction of business and economic change with a view to reducing business risk and uncertainty. Prerequisite: 201, 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139646, 445920, 'AGEC', '2001', 2020, 'Introductory Agricultural Economics', 'Identification of resources used in agriculture. Basic concepts, principles and applications of agricultural economics to the farm operation.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139647, 716423, 'ART', '4002', 2020, 'Creating Paper / Casting and Molding', 'Study and processing of basic skills in creating paper from laminations to cast paper. One hour lecture, 5 hours laboratory per week. Prerequisite: 1001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139648, 257144, 'KINS', '1038', 2020, 'Racquetball', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning raquetball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139649, 462696, 'KINS', '1052', 2020, 'Handball', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning handball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139650, 354444, 'KINS', '2043', 2020, 'Scuba Diving', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning scuba diving.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139651, 307843, 'ACCT', '3017', 2020, 'Tax Fundamentals', 'Tax problems of individuals, with emphasis on planning to minimize taxes. Not open to accounting majors. Prerequisite: 212 and 213; junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139652, 307843, 'ACCT', '317', 2020, 'Tax Fundamentals', 'Tax problems of individuals, with emphasis on planning to minimize taxes. Not open to accounting majors. Prerequisite: 212 and 213; junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139654, 678685, 'CONS', '460C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Advanced Surveying Problems (Formerly CONS 460C)', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. Directed individual study. Prerequisite: Approval of director. (Formerly CONS 460C)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139655, 674970, 'THEA', '1000', 2020, 'Career Planning', 'Teaches the basics of the theatre business to include resume and portfolio preparation, personal record keeping and career paths. F', 0.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139656, 544784, 'THEA', '3051', 2020, 'Scenic Design', 'Teaches application of art fundamentals and historical research to the design of scenery for theatre, television and film through projects in drawing, rendering and model building. Laboratory hours on TheatreWorks.ULM productions required. Prerequisite: THEA 3001 and 3003 or permission of the instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139657, 253464, 'THEA', '4001', 2020, 'Costume Design', 'Teaches application of art fundamentals and historical research to the creation of costumes for theatre, television and film through drawing and rendering projects. Laboratory hours on TheatreWorks.ULM productions required. Prerequisite: THEA 3060 or permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139658, 589031, 'THEA', '4050', 2020, 'Advanced Design Practice', 'Teaches advanced design skills. May be repeated to a maximum of nine credits. Prerequisites: THEA 3001 & 3051 or 3060 & 4001 or 2007 or 3003 as appropriate and permission of the instructor.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139659, 868954, 'THEA', '4043', 2020, 'Contemporary Theatre Practices: France', 'Examines current acting and directing styles and techniques in the various technical areas: scenery, lighting, sound, makeup, costumes, and properties. Formerly THEA 442A)', 3.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139660, 866012, 'SPAN', '4074', 2020, 'Second Language Acquisition', 'The application of second language acquisition theory in the classroom. Prerequisite: Spanish/French 4073.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139661, 866012, 'SPAN', '474', 2020, 'Second Language Acquisition', 'The application of second language acquisition theory in the classroom. Prerequisite: Spanish/French 4073.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139662, 950756, 'TOXI', '2001', 2020, 'Environmental Toxicology', 'This course will encompass both the fate and effects of chemicals in the environment, with emphasis in aquatic and terrestrial ecosystems. Potential sources, routes of exposure, and physical, chemical, and biological factors important with the movement of contaminants within various components of the ecosystems will be examined. In addition, emerging environmental regulations, issues, and case studies will be discussed. Prerequisites: BIOL 1020, 1021; CHEM 1007, 1009. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139663, 53075, 'THEA', '4080', 2020, 'Apprenticeship', 'Provides for working with an acknowledged master in specific theatre craft. Master must agree to supervise and teach the student. Student must design a learning contract which is signed by the student, the master and the Director of Theater. The master can not be a member of the ULM Theater faculty. Prerequisite: Permission of Director of Theater.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139664, 153871, 'ENGL', '2020B', 2020, 'Professional Writing & Communication: Sciences & Applied Sciences', '3 cr. Instruction in technical and professional writing and communication in sciences and applied sciences. Emphasis on written and oral forms. Includes practice in documentation, collaboration, oral presentation, and research in the field. Prerequisites: ENGL 1002; junior standing or permission of English Dept. Head; restricted to biology, chemistry, geosciences, computer science, aviation, and agriculture majors. (Formerly ENGL 220B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139665, 880246, 'KINS', '1013', 2020, 'Bowling I', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning bowling.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139666, 845758, 'KINS', '1017', 2020, 'Softball', 'Skill, techniques, and knowledges of beginning softball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139667, 326487, 'KINS', '1018', 2020, 'Volleyball', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning volleyball.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139668, 504186, 'KINS', '1008', 2020, 'Soccer', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning soccer.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139669, 799611, 'KINS', '1011', 2020, 'Archery', 'Skills, techniques, and knowledges of beginning archery.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139671, 646188, 'TOXI', '4015', 2020, 'Analytical Toxicology', 'Quantitative and qualitative methods of chemical analysis of toxic substances. Prerequisites: TOXI 4012; CHEM 3007, 3008; credit or registration in 4016. Toxicology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139672, 869400, 'THEA', '4025', 2020, 'Directing', 'Teaches directorial skills in leadership, script selection and analysis, conduct of auditions, rehearsals and performance evaluation through workshop and application. Prerequisites: THEA 1011, 2021 and permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139673, 489593, 'THEA', '4086', 2020, 'Senior Project', 'Provides a culminating project for students in technical production, design and direction through which they can demonstrate proficiency in their chosen area. Prerequisite: Permission of Director of Theater.', 1.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139676, 676281, 'SPAN', '105', 2020, 'Elementary Spanish I and II', 'Same as Spanish 1001 and 1002. An introduction to the basic grammatical structures of Spanish with the objectives of developing an elementary ability to speak, understand, read, and write the language.\r\n\r\nLCCN: CSPN 1026', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139677, 676281, 'SPAN', '1005', 2020, 'Elementary Spanish I and II', 'Same as Spanish 1001 and 1002. An introduction to the basic grammatical structures of Spanish with the objectives of developing an elementary ability to speak, understand, read, and write the language.\r\n\r\nLCCN: CSPN 1026', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139678, 478140, 'SPAN', '197', 2020, 'Beginning Spanish', 'Independent reading, grammar, and/or conversation. Work in the computerized Language Learning Center is required. Prerequisite: SPAN 1002 or 1005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139679, 93913, 'SPAN', '1098', 2020, 'Beginning Spanish', 'Independent reading, grammar, and/or conversation. Work in the computerized Language Learning Center is required. Prerequisite: SPAN 1002 or 1005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139680, 668273, 'SPAN', '1099', 2020, 'Beginning Spanish', 'Independent reading, grammar, and/or conversation. Work in the computerized Language Learning Center is required. Prerequisite: SPAN 1002 or 1005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139681, 165786, 'FRNH', '205', 2020, 'Intermediate French I and II', 'Same as French 2001-2002. A continuation on the intermediate level of 1001-1002, with an increased emphasis upon reading and discussion. Work in the computerized Language Center is required. Prerequisite: A \"C\" or better in 1002 or permission of Department head.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CFRN 2026', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139682, 241196, 'SPAN', '3008', 2020, 'Survey of Spanish Literature', 'Selection from the outstanding authors of Spain. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139683, 333167, 'SPAN', '3011', 2020, 'Phonetics', 'An introduction to the Spanish phonetic system with emphasis on pronunciation practice in the language learning facility. Prerequisite: SPAN 1002 or the equivalent.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139684, 413700, 'SPAN', '3022', 2020, 'Independent Reading', 'Directed reading and discussion of excerpts from Hispanic literature with continued emphasis on understanding, speaking, reading, and writing Spanish. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139685, 397195, 'SPAN', '3023', 2020, 'Independent Reading', 'Directed reading and discussion of excerpts from Hispanic literature with continued emphasis on understanding, speaking, reading, and writing Spanish. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139686, 738997, 'SPAN', '4002', 2020, 'Seminar in Spanish Literature', 'Maximum, 6 cr. In- depth study and analysis of a specific Spanish-language literary movement or writer. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139687, 269122, 'SPAN', '4006', 2020, 'Advanced Spanish Syntax', 'An analysis of the more complex and problematic areas of Spanish grammar and vocabulary usage. Prerequisite: SPAN 2031 or equivalent.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139688, 790696, 'SPAN', '4007', 2020, 'Contemporary Latin American Literature', 'Maximum 6 cr. An analysis and discussion of outstanding works from the Spanish American literature of the twentieth century. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005 or permission of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139689, 135862, 'SPAN', '4015', 2020, 'Contemporary Spanish Literature', 'Extensive reading of authors of the Generation of 1898 and of the Twentieth Century. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139690, 135862, 'SPAN', '415', 2020, 'Contemporary Spanish Literature', 'Extensive reading of authors of the Generation of 1898 and of the Twentieth Century. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139691, 513944, 'SPAN', '4073', 2020, 'SPAN 473', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139692, 30079, 'SPAN', '4075', 2020, 'Language, Culture and the Classroom', 'The application of second language acquisition theory in the elementary or secondary classroom. (Same as Spanish 4075). Prerequisite: Spanish/French 4074.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139693, 258193, 'SPED', '4065', 2020, 'Student Teaching for Special Education', 'Directed observation and participation in special education situations. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 12.0000, 12.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139694, 46653, 'SPED', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Focused investigation on selected problems in Special Education. Prerequisite: Approval of instructor.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139695, 584750, 'SOCL', '422', 2020, 'Anthropology of Latin America', 'Description of indigenous social organizations prior to conquest. Survey of community ethnographic studies of African, Amerind, Asiatic and European cultures in contemporary rural and urban Latin America. Prerequisite: SOCL 3007 or approval of department head. (Same as ANTG 4022.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139696, 6641677, 'COMM', '2020', 2020, 'Visual Literacy', 'Examines the connection between visual images and persuasion, i.e., how images act rhetorically upon viewers; students become adept at visual analysis.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139697, 644254, 'FCSC', '4015F', 2