t majors. Prerequisite: 4000. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139822, 248740, 'FCSC', '429', 2020, 'Practicum in Preschool', 'Program planning and implementation for the pre-school. Teaching experience with prekindergarten children. For Family Life/Child Development majors. Prerequisite: 4000. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139823, 977161, 'ECON', '202', 2020, 'Microeconomic Principles', 'Focuses on such concepts as demand, supply, elasticity, production and cost. Analyzes market models of perfect competition, monopoly and imperfect competition. Includes discussion of international trade issues and government interventions. F, Sp, Su<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CECN 2223', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139827, 657514, 'EQSC', '4013', 2020, 'Horse Production', 'Theory and practical work on breeding, feeding, and management of horses. Prerequisite: EQSC 330.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139828, 710072, 'FCSC', '4021', 2020, 'Student Teaching', 'Modern methods of teaching family and consumer sciences in the secondary schools; integrating philosophy of family and consumer sciences, principles of learning, student experiences, needs, and interests; cooperative planning and evaluation; professional ethics. Prerequisite: FCSC 3013. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 12.0000, 12.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139830, 192120, 'ENGL', '4080', 2020, 'Internship-Technical & Professional Communication', '3 credits, 6 credits, maximum. Advanced instruction and on-the-job experience in technical writing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139833, 780386, 'ELED', '4065', 2020, 'Student Teaching in the Lower Elementary School', 'Directed observation and participation in classroom activities in the lower grades in an approved elementary school. Must be admitted to Teacher Education. F, Sp', 12.0000, 12.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139834, 751551, 'ELED', '4066', 2020, 'Student Teaching in the Upper Elementary School', 'Directed observation and participation in classroom activities in the upper grades in an approved elementary school. F, Sp For Undergraduates and Graduates', 12.0000, 12.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139835, 492729, 'ELED', '4054', 2020, 'Creative Activities for Early Childhood Education', 'An investigation of methods to develop childrens creative activities within specific content areas. Prequisite: Must be admitted to Teacher Education. Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139838, 119114, 'HUMN', '1011', 2020, 'Fine Arts Appreciation: Local (Formerly HUMN 110A)', '1 credit; maximum, 3 credits. Credit is given for attendance of selected cultural attractions.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139839, 119114, 'HUMN', '110A', 2020, 'Fine Arts Appreciation: Local (Formerly HUMN 110A)', '1 credit; maximum, 3 credits. Credit is given for attendance of selected cultural attractions.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139845, 740440, 'ELED', '483C', 2020, 'Practicum: Elementary Education (Formerly ELED 483C)', 'Internship program designed to give supervised experience in the school. Must be admitted to Teacher Education. (Formerly ELED 483C)', 3.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139846, 740440, 'ELED', '4086', 2020, 'Practicum: Elementary Education (Formerly ELED 483C)', 'Internship program designed to give supervised experience in the school. Must be admitted to Teacher Education. (Formerly ELED 483C)', 3.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139847, 64880, 'EDFN', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Investigative study on selected problems by students with particular needs.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139848, 773380, 'ELED', '3001', 2020, 'Principles of Teaching in the Elementary School', 'Procedures and techniques of teaching in the elementary school.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139849, 947310, 'ECON', '1003', 2020, 'Contemporary Economic Issues', 'Introduction to the analysis of current national issues, including international business issues and business ethics, using the economic approach. Not open to students with prior credit in both Economics 2001 and 2002. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139850, 606385, 'ECON', '3011', 2020, 'Intermediate Microeconomic Analysis', 'Theory and behavior of consumers, analysis of production and costs, optimal decision making by the firm in competitive, monopolistic and imperfectly competitive markets, optimal resource allocation. Prerequisite: 201, 2002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139851, 362110, 'ECON', '3012', 2020, 'Intermediate Macroeconomic Analysis', 'Determinants of national income and employment. The role of consumption spending, business investment, government spending, and taxing and monetary policies in determining the level of economic activity. Prerequisites: 2001, 2002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139852, 396006, 'ECON', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Individual study of selected economics topics under the direction of a senior faculty member. Prerequisite: Approval of Department Head. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139854, 310794, 'EDFN', '4003', 2020, 'Research for Practitioners', 'An introduction to research, through which students will become consumers of research in their respective fields.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139855, 930647, 'EDFN', '4030B', 2020, 'Special Topics: United States School Systems On Location', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A. Study of International Education on Location; B. Study of United States School Systems on Location; C. Comparative Education; D. Evaluation in Education; E. Educational Technology and Media.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139856, 602907, 'EDFN', '4030A', 2020, 'Special Topics: International Education On Location', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A. Study of International Education on Location; B. Study of United States School Systems on Location; C. Comparative Education; D. Evaluation in Education; E. Educational Technology and Media.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139857, 784374, 'DHYG', '4036', 2020, 'Directed Study: Periodontology (Formerly DHYG 432B)', '1-3 credits; maximum, 9 credits. Individual study and/or research in selected dental hygiene topics. Prerequisite: Approval of program director. (Formerly DHYG 432B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139858, 784374, 'DHYG', '432B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Periodontology (Formerly DHYG 432B)', '1-3 credits; maximum, 9 credits. Individual study and/or research in selected dental hygiene topics. Prerequisite: Approval of program director. (Formerly DHYG 432B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139859, 175282, 'DHYG', '4026', 2020, 'Survey of Dental Specialties', 'Students learn the techniques used in the various specialties of dentistry such as periodontics, orthodontics, endodontics, oral surgery, prosthodontics, and hospital dentistry as they relate to the treatment of pediatric and geriatric patients. Prerequisites: 4019, 4021, 4022, 4031; registration in 4028, 4029, 4033. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139860, 581672, 'CURR', '3014', 2020, 'CURR 314', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139861, 711875, 'DHYG', '2050', 2020, 'Oral Histology and Embryology', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139862, 737783, 'DHYG', '4020', 2020, 'Community & Preventive Dentistry Field Experience', 'Continuation of 4019. Primary focus is the application of public health principles through selected field experiences in current aspects of community dental health including needs assessment, program planning, and follow-up assessment of program success. Prerequisites: 4019, 4021, 4022, 4024, 4033; registration in 4028, 4029. Sp', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139863, 610383, 'DANC', '4094', 2020, 'Directed Study: