trating on the World Wide Web. The course will cover support issues related to providing more advanced WWW services, including user support, security, operations, staffing, and purchasing. Prerequisite: CSCI 3030.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139870, 934331, 'CURR', '4031', 2020, 'CURR 431', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139871, 18188, 'CURR', '3038', 2020, 'Upper Elem School Curr and Instruction Strategies', 'Procedures and techniques for developing skills to teach content areas in the upper elementary grades.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139876, 195031, 'CSCI', '4061', 2020, 'Cooperative Education Experience', 'Planned and supervised work experience in students major field. Open only to juniors and seniors in the Department of Computer Science who are approved for the Cooperative Education Program. Grades of CR (credit) or NC (no credit) will be awarded. May be repeated for a total of 3 credits. May not be applied to fulfill major requirements.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139877, 361956, 'CSCI', '420', 2020, 'Introduction to Biostatistics I', 'An introduction to the discipline of statistics and its application to problems of biology, including human biology, medicine, and public health. Topics include Bayesian inferences, estimation techniques, hypothesis testing, goodness of fit, and analysis of variance. Prerequisite: Math 1014 or Math 1031 or permission of department head. (Same as Math 4020).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139882, 858425, 'COUN', '4064', 2020, 'Counseling Procedures', 'The study of theory, processes, and relationships involved in individual and family counseling approaches and practices. Designed as a prepracticum experience, the course includes laboratory demonstrations and practice to develop initial counseling skills.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139883, 577539, 'COUN', '4081', 2020, 'Continuing Studies i