s major field to include phlebotomy, patient relations, laboratory operations, and laboratory computers. Grades of A, B, C, and NC (No Credit) will be awarded. May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Students must work a minimum of 20 hrs./week and must be compensated by employer. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139915, 483742, 'CLSC', '4064', 2020, 'Clinical Microbiology', 'Advanced concepts in the use and interpretation of medical microbiological procedures and data. Prerequisite: Completion of three years of pre-clinical courses. F, Sp, Sum', 2.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139918, 701281, 'CLSC', '1010', 2020, 'CLSC 110', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139919, 749641, 'CINS', '4095', 2020, 'Seminar: Special Topics (Formerly CINS 492C)', '1-3 credits per semester. May be repeated for a maximum of 6 credits. Seminar in information systems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly CINS 492C)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139920, 881026, 'CLSC', '3045', 2020, 'Directed Study: Serology (Formerly CLSC 338E)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems in serology. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139921, 648693, 'CINS', '492B', 2020, 'Seminar: Methodologies (Formerly CINS 492B)', '1-3 credits per semester. May be repeated for a maximum of 6 credits. Seminar in information systems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly CINS 492B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139922, 780740, 'CLSC', '475C', 2020, 'Clinical Laboratory Science Problems', 'An introduction to emerging medical technologies and research in: A. Urinalysis; B. Hematology; C. Immunology; D. Blood Bank/Transfusion Medicine; E. Serology; F. Clinical Chemistry; H. Toxicology; I. Microbiology; J. Other associated areas of clinical laborator