imum of 6 credits. Seminar in information systems. Topic areas: A. Software; B. Methodologies; C. Special Topics. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139929, 134264, 'CJUS', '3003', 2020, 'Community-Based Corrections', 'An in-depth study of correctional programs, practices, and theory within the American community. Survey of community corrections in terms of historical contributions; legal, social, and ethical considerations; professionalism; roles of staff, administration, and community resources; and relationships among and within community systems. Prerequisite: 1001, 2070, or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139930, 312652, 'CLSC', '1011', 2020, 'CLSC 111', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139931, 648693, 'CINS', '4094', 2020, 'Seminar: Methodologies (Formerly CINS 492B)', '1-3 credits per semester. May be repeated for a maximum of 6 credits. Seminar in information systems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly CINS 492B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139932, 749641, 'CINS', '492C', 2020, 'Seminar: Special Topics (Formerly CINS 492C)', '1-3 credits per semester. May be repeated for a maximum of 6 credits. Seminar in information systems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly CINS 492C)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139933, 196176, 'COUN', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Investigative study on selected problems by students with particular needs.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139934, 290888, 'CHEM', '422A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Analytical', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A directed study for undergraduates and graduates. May include laboratory and/or library work. Four to six hours per week for each credit hour earned. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 422A)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139936, 129259, 'CINS', '2005', 2020, 'Intro to Computer-Based Management Information', 'Introduction to the use of the computer for business applications; productivity software (word processing, electronic spreadsheet, data management, and presentation graphics). CINS majors must earn a minimum grade of &quot;C&quot;. Prerequisites: Completion of all developmental requirements. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139939, 874145, 'CHEM', '4096', 2020, 'Research: Inorganic (Formerly CHEM 499C)', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 cr. Research problems that can be completed in one semester. Three to six hours laboratory per week per credit hour. Prerequisites: Junior or senior standing in chemistry and approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 499C)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139940, 472703, 'BUSN', '2015', 2020, 'Current Business Problems', '1 credit per semester; maximum, 3 cr. Intensive study and analysis of selected current problems in business. Different topics are considered each semester.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139941, 607780, 'BIOL', '4104', 2020, 'Problems: Bacteriology / VIrology (Formerly BIOL 403B)', 'Problems: Bacteriology / VIrology. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403B)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139943, 429427, 'BIOL', '1009', 2020, 'Laboratory Experience for the Life Sciences', 'A laboratory course to accompany Biology 1001 & 1010 lecture course. Two hours\r\nlaboratory. Prerequisites: Credit or registration in 1001 or 1010, or approval by the Department Head. Non-majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139944, 185592, 'AVIA', '491C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Traffic Control (Formerly AVIA 491C)', 'Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Traffic Control. Maximum, 6 cr. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491C)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139945, 161693, 'AVIA', '4051', 2020, 'Advanced Aerospace Seminar', 'Problems in aerospace development, history, organization and management. Field trips to aerospace centers for research, development, and operations.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139946, 649508, 'BIOL', '400C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Through the Genetic Maze', 'Selected studies in general and biological science. Content varies. A. Oceanus; B. Brain, Mind, and Behavior; C. Through the Genetic Maze; D. Cosmos; E. Race to Save the Planet. May be repeated for a maximum of 12 credit hours. No more than 6 semester hours may be applied toward degree requirements.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139947, 53235, 'BIOL', '4107', 2020, 'Problems: Animal Science / Genetics (Formerly BIOL 403E)', 'Problems: Animal Science / Genetics. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139948, 53235, 'BIOL', '403E', 2020, 'Problems: Animal Science / Genetics (Formerly BIOL 403E)', 'Problems: Animal Science / Genetics. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139949, 369997, 'BIOL', '400B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Brain, Mind, and Behavior', 'Selected studies in general and biological science. Content varies. A. Oceanus; B. Brain, Mind, and Behavior; C. Through the Genetic Maze; D. Cosmos; E. Race to Save the Planet. May be repeated for a maximum of 12 credit hours. No more than 6 semester hours may be applied toward degree requirements.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139951, 888555, 'BIOL', '4106', 2020, 'Problems: Ecology (Formerly BIOL 403D)', 'Problems: Ecology. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403D)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139952, 888555, 'BIOL', '403D', 2020, 'Problems: Ecology (Formerly BIOL 403D)', 'Problems: Ecology. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403D)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139953, 906944, 'BIOL', '306', 2020, 'Genetics Laboratory', 'A laboratory to accompany 3005. Lab topics include Mendelian genetics to molecular genetics. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisites: credit with \"C\" or better or registration in 3005.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 3521', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139954, 75856, 'BIOL', '115', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Anatomy and Physiology II', 'A continuation of 1014. Structure and functions of the circulatory,\r\nrespiratory, digestive, excretory, endocrine, and reproductive systems.\r\nPrerequisite: C or better in 1014. Non-majors only. Cannot be taken for\r\ncredit if credit has been awarded in 3010 (formerly 3011, 3012).<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 2223', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139955, 951181, 'ATMS', '3015', 2020, 'Physical Meteorology', 'Introduction to physical principles underlying atmospheric radiation, cloud physics and precipitation processes. Prerequisite: ATMS 3003 and PHYS 2008.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139956, 7361168, 'ATMS', '4003', 2020, 'Synoptic Meteorology Laboratory', 'Application of dynamics and thermodynamics to weather analysis and forecasting theory and practice with an emphasis on communication skills. Thermodynamic diagrams; analysis of scalar and vector fields; synoptic-scale weather systems; numerical weather prediction. Prerequisites: C or better in ATMS 3005.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139957, 365232, 'ATMS', '4050', 2020, 'Atmospheric Pollution', 'A study of elements, effects and meteorology of air pollution including the &quot;Greenhouse&quot; effect, acid rain, and ozone depletion problems. Air pollution modeling and prediction is also covered. Prerequisites: Completion of freshman mathematics requirements and CHEM 1007.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139958, 444603, 'ATMS', '4061', 2020, 'Meteorology for Teachers', 'A non-mathematical introduction to meteorology designed for elementary and secondary school science teachers. The courses are a blend of lecture, demonstrations, and hands-on work and are designed to be taken in sequence (4060-4061). The courses cannot be used to satisfy degree requirements in Atmospheric Science. Prerequisite: ATMS 4060.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139959, 219250, 'AVIA', '2021', 2020, 'Instrument Ground Trainer Lab', 'Development of skills of scan, interpretation, and control for instrument flight. Prerequisite: 2020 or concurrent enrollment.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139960, 219250, 'AVIA', '221', 2020, 'Instrument Ground Trainer Lab', 'Development of skills of scan, interpretation, and control for instrument flight. Prerequisite: 2020 or concurrent enrollment.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139961, 432360, 'PHYS', '4005', 2020, 'Basic Physics Laboratory', 'Classical physics experiments in heat and thermodynamics, mechanics, optics, and electricity and magnetism. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisites: PHYS 315 and 401.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139962, 211952, 'AVIA', '3001', 2020, 'Aerodynamics', 'Analysis of the physics of flight including the application of basic aerodynamics to the wing and airfoil and the analysis of lift and drag components relative to the wing platform and airplane performance. The application of aerodynamic effects of turbo jet engines involving the principles of propulsion. Prerequisite: private pilot certificate or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139963, 304953, 'ATMS', '104', 2020, 'Basic Meteorology Laboratory II', 'A laboratory course designed to expose students to basics of climatology. Topics include atmospheric elements, the earths energy balance, climate regions, and global climate change. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in ATMS 1002, 1003.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139964, 345686, 'MAFT', '2050', 2020, 'Skills for Marriage and Couples', 'Designed to provide students with information and skills to support enduring and satisfying marriage/couples relationships.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139965, 403904, 'MUSC', '321', 2020, 'Basketball Pep Band', 'Entertainment ensemble for home basketball games. Group travels to conference tournament and postseason games. Prerequisite: Approval of the director. May be repeated.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139966, 435758, 'ATMS', '110', 2020, 'Microcomputers in Meteorology', 'Two hours of laboratory work learning to operate personal computer systems dealing with meteorological data. Discussions will consider data distribution, reception and archival; IBM operating systems; Weathercapture software; DIFAX; and the PC-McIDAS network.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139967, 388726, 'ART', '4055', 2020, 'Advanced Photography', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Individual instruction in planning and executing a personal response to the visual elements and creative composition. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2046.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139968, 128316, 'ART', '4046', 2020, 'Special Problems: Painting (Formerly ART 441C)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441C)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139969, 659884, 'BIOL', '4103', 2020, 'Problems: Anatomy / Physiology (Formerly BIOL 403A)', 'Problems: Anatomy / Physiology. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403A)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139970, 349610, 'ART', '1004', 2020, 'Figure Drawing', 'Drawing made from models. Six hours studio. Prerequisite: 1003. Additional Course Fee .\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CART 2213', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139971, 748195, 'ARAB', '1098', 2020, 'Beginning Arabic', 'An independent study of elementary Arabic with an emphasis on the script, pronunciation, and grammar of Modern Standard Arabic.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139972, 677025, 'ARAB', '1099', 2020, 'Beginning Arabic', 'An independent study of elementary Arabic with an emphasis on the script, pronunciation, and grammar of Modern Standard Arabic.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139973, 356406, 'ARAB', '1097', 2020, 'Beginning Arabic', 'An independent study of elementary Arabic with an emphasis on the script, pronunciation, and grammar of Modern Standard Arabic.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139974, 973701, 'ARAB', '3007', 2020, 'Arabic Civilization', 'Introduction to the religion of Islam and the intellectual and spiritual heritage of the Arabs. The early Arabs, the Revelation, theology, religious law, Sufism and modernist phenomena. Architectural, scientific, philosophical and literary developments.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139976, 435712, 'FRNH', '1002', 2020, 'Elementary French II', 'A continuation of the study of French on the elementary level. Prerequisite: A \"C\" or better in French 1001 or permission of Department Head.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CFRN 1023', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139977, 839530, 'AHSC', '1002', 2020, 'Orientation to Allied Health Professions', 'An on-line introduction to allied health and rehabilitation professions focusing upon roles, career paths, and collaborative training.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139978, 547033, 'CJUS', '101', 2020, 'Introduction to Criminal Justice', 'An examination of the history, organization, and function of the various local and federal agencies that make up the criminal justice system. The survey is organized around the three major components of the criminal justice system: police, courts, and corrections.<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCRJ 1013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139979, 408392, 'AGRI', '491F', 2020, 'Agriculture Biometrics (Formerly AGRI 491F)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Individualized work on special problems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly AGRI 491F)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139980, 704545, 'AGRI', '495C', 2020, 'Agricultural Research: Animal Science (Formerly AGRI 495C)', 'Student participation in research projects in the areas of Animal Science. Two to three hours per week per credit hour. Prerequisites: Junior or senior standing in agriculture and approval of department head. (Formerly AGRI 495C)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139981, 421340, 'MUSC', '214', 2020, 'Jazz Ensemble', 'Prerequisite: Approval of the director. May be repeated. Music and Music Education majors must enrolle for zero credit.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 10.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139982, 618265, 'MUSC', '211', 2020, 'Woodwind Ensemble', 'Prerequisite: Approval of Head of Division of Music. May be repeated. Music and Music Education majors must take for zero credit.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 10.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139983, 639053, 'POLS', '3001', 2020, 'Research Methods', 'This course is designed to introduce political science majors to the scope and research methods of the discipline. Prerequisite: POLS 201 or permission of the instructor AND department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139984, 23323, 'MUSC', '3041', 2020, 'Voice', 'Performance - Major. May be repeated for a maximum of 6 hours of credit.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139985, 431138, 'MSED', '3008', 2020, 'Practicum in Instrumental Technique', 'A laboratory ensemble of music education students to gain further experience on minor applied instruments--strings, woodwinds, brass, and percussion; also provides opportunity to develop conducting skills. Prerequisite: one credit of minor applied instrument to be played in the ensemble.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139986, 294252, 'MSED', '3022', 2020, 'Materials / Methods in Vocal Music in Elem School', 'Vocal class and rehearsal management, methods, and materials in the elementary school.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139987, 761221, 'MUSC', '3036', 2020, 'Music Education for the Elementary Grades', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139988, 464774, 'MSED', '4005', 2020, 'Band Directors Workshop', '3 credits, maximum, 9 credits. A &quot;refresher&quot; course for instrumental music education teachers emphasing the basic concepts of the marching band. New concepts and teaching techniques in marching band will be discussed. Also, related areas such as administration, arranging, new music, charting, auxiliary units, and marching percussion will be covered. Films and video tapes will be used extensively.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139989, 159968, 'MSED', '4007', 2020, 'Piano Teachers Workshop', '3 credits, maximum, 9 cr. A course for piano teachers, including instructional procedures, methods and materials, and teaching demonstrations.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139990, 834449, 'MSED', '4009', 2020, 'Choral Directors Workshop', '3 credits, maximum, 9 cr. A course designed for choral directors including vocal techniques, choral literature and interpretation, rehearsal methods, and teaching techniques.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139991, 253353, 'MUSC', '1003', 2020, 'Aural Skills I', 'Course covers fundamental elements of melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic dictation and sight-singing. Prerequisite: MUSC 1001 or equivalent.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139992, 253353, 'MUSC', '103', 2020, 'Aural Skills I', 'Course covers fundamental elements of melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic dictation and sight-singing. Prerequisite: MUSC 1001 or equivalent.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139993, 378752, 'FRYS', '1001', 2020, 'University Seminar', 'To maximize the students potential to achieve academic success and to adjust responsibly to the individual and interpersonal challenges presented by collegiate life.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139994, 645983, 'AGRI', '4012', 2020, 'Internship in Agriculture', 'Supervised work experience with industry in the use of materials and equipment related to the student&#39;s major field of interest. Six hours maximum towards B.S. degree. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139995, 631687, 'AGRI', '4013', 2020, 'Internship in Agriculture', 'Supervised work experience with industry in the use of materials and equipment related to the student&#39;s major field of interest. Six hours maximum towards B.S. degree. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139996, 387525, 'ART', '4041', 2020, 'Special Problems', '3 credits per course. Any area may be repeated. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. A. Graphic Design; B. Ceramics; C. Painting; D. Photography; E. Drawing; F. Printing; G. Sculpture. Additional course fee may apply to certain topics.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139997, 164882, 'MATH', '4032', 2020, 'Fundamentals of High School Mathematics II', 'Emphasis is on teaching at the high school level. Topics include, but are not restricted to, algebra, algebraic structures, data analysis, basic statistics. Not applicable toward a major or minor in mathematics. Applies to middle and high school certification.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (139998, 466969, 'MILS', '499C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Cadet Troop Leader Training (Formerly MILS 499C)', 'Maximum 9 cr. Directed study at a military installation. Prerequisite: Approval of the Professor of Military Science.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (139999, 176650, 'MSED', '4013', 2020, 'Music Educaton Workshop: Intermediate (Formerly MSED 411B)', 'A course designed to instruct teachers and supervisors of elementary music in singing, playing instruments, moving, creating, arranging, and selecting music. (Formerly MSED 411B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140000, 176650, 'MSED', '411B', 2020, 'Music Educaton Workshop: Intermediate (Formerly MSED 411B)', 'A course designed to instruct teachers and supervisors of elementary music in singing, playing instruments, moving, creating, arranging, and selecting music. (Formerly MSED 411B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140001, 574730, 'MNSC', '4080', 2020, 'Marine Science for Teachers', 'Survey of the marine sciences; field and classroom techniques for the teaching of marine science at the elementary and secondary school levels. Credit can be applied only to degrees in education. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory or participating state university.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140002, 646419, 'MRKT', '4009', 2020, 'Marketing Management', 'Analysis of actual business situations requiring decisions by marketing executives in the marketing mix and environmental areas of marketing. Prerequisites: Six hours of Marketing above MRKT 3001. Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140003, 740406, 'MRKT', '4092', 2020, 'Topics in Marketing', 'Specialized study of topics in Marketing. Content Varies. Prerequisite: 3001', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140004, 740406, 'MRKT', '492', 2020, 'Topics in Marketing', 'Specialized study of topics in Marketing. Content Varies. Prerequisite: 3001', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140005, 794241, 'MRKT', '3005', 2020, 'Personal Selling', 'The fundamental principles of selling; the economic problems connected with personal selling; an analysis of the product and the market; the interview; and building good will. Prerequisite: MRKT 3001. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140006, 466969, 'MILS', '4095', 2020, 'Directed Study: Cadet Troop Leader Training (Formerly MILS 499C)', 'Maximum 9 cr. Directed study at a military installation. Prerequisite: Approval of the Professor of Military Science.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140008, 775753, 'MILS', '4094', 2020, 'Directed Study: Airborne School (Formerly MILS 499B)', 'Maximum 9 cr. Directed study at a military installation. Prerequisite: Approval of the Professor of Military Science. (Formerly MILS 499B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140009, 626715, 'MSED', '4014', 2020, 'Music Education Workshop: Advanced (Formerly MSED 411C)', 'A course designed to instruct teachers and supervisors of elementary music in singing, playing instruments, moving, creating, arranging, and selecting music. (Formerly MSED 411C)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140016, 596139, 'MCOM', '1001', 2020, 'Survey of Mass Media for Users', 'A critical survey of print and electronic media designed to enhance the users media literacy and media consumer skills. For non-MCOM majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140017, 596139, 'MCOM', '101', 2020, 'Survey of Mass Media for Users', 'A critical survey of print and electronic media designed to enhance the users media literacy and media consumer skills. For non-MCOM majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140018, 140851, 'MATH', '405', 2020, 'Partial Differential Equations', 'Fourier series, boundary value problems, partial differential equations, special functions, with an emphasis on applications. Prerequisite: MATH 3001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140019, 421484, 'MATH', '4095', 2020, 'Research: Analysis (Formerly MATH 498B)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Open to advanced undergraduates who are capable of developing a problem independently. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly MATH 498B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140020, 286030, 'MATH', '436', 2020, 'Intro Mathematical Concepts in Operations Research', 'A mathematical approach to concepts in advanced linear and nonlinear programming, dynamic programming, game theories, queueing theory and other standard topics in operations research. Prerequisites: CSCI 4035 and MATH 3003. (Same as MATH 4036.)', 0.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140021, 249434, 'MATH', '421', 2020, 'Introduction to Biostatistics II', 'A continuation of 4020. Topics include linear and multiple regression, logistics regression, longitudinal data analysis, nonparametric methods and principal component techniques. Prerequisites: Math 4020 or CSCI 4020 and junior standing or above. (Same as Math 4021).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140022, 252725, 'MUSC', '4074', 2020, 'Form and Analysis', 'Intensive study of the larger musical forms. Prerequisite: 2004 and 2005, or approval of the Head of the Division of Music.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140023, 252725, 'MUSC', '474', 2020, 'Form and Analysis', 'Intensive study of the larger musical forms. Prerequisite: 2004 and 2005, or approval of the Head of the Division of Music.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140024, 803074, 'MUSC', '4061', 2020, 'Keyboard Harmony & Creative Musicianship for Piano', '1 credit, 2 credit maximum. A functional approach to keyboard skills for piano instructors. A combination of lab and lecture to include harmonization, chord voicing, transposition, modulation, improvisation, sight reading, and score reading. Development of proficiency in these skills, as well as an understanding of how they can be taught at different levels.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140027, 471301, 'NURS', '4054', 2020, 'Critical Care Nursing: SICU (Formerly NURS 450D)', 'The indepth study of critical care aspects of nursing, including support mechanisms. Prerequisite: NURS 4004, 4005, 4003, Registered Nurse license, or permission of the Director, School of Nursing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140028, 374209, 'NURS', '4055', 2020, 'Critical Care Nursing: PICU (Formerly NURS 450E)', 'The indepth study of critical care aspects of nursing, including support mechanisms. Prerequisite: NURS 4004, 4005, 4003, Registered Nurse license, or permission of the Director, School of Nursing. (Formerly NURS 450E)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140031, 484272, 'MUSC', '402B', 2020, 'Special Problems: History and Literature (Formerly MUSC 402B)', 'Investigative study of special problems by students with particular needs in music. Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated. (Formerly MUSC 402B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 99.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140032, 294145, 'THEA', '1001', 2020, 'Play Reading I', 'Reading and discussing 15 plays by contemporary American playwrights. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140033, 374506, 'MUSC', '3075', 2020, 'Sixteenth Century Counterpoint', 'Composition of two, three, and four-voice motets and a technical study of related choral tradition, with the liturgical literature of the Renaissance and Gregorian chant as a frame of reference. More complex contrapuntal devices may be elected by students with adequate background. Class performance, analysis, and hearing of representative works are correlated with written work. Prerequisite: MUSC 204.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140034, 762742, 'MUSC', '3020', 2020, 'Percussion Class', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140035, 258037, 'MUSC', '3018', 2020, 'Brass Class', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140036, 960193, 'MUSC', '3014', 2020, 'String Class', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140037, 881564, 'MUSC', '3016', 2020, 'Woodwind Class', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140038, 348519, 'MUSC', '3013', 2020, 'String Class', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140039, 810381, 'MUSC', '3011', 2020, 'Voice Clas