entation. Topic varies; may not take the same topic twice. \r\nPre-requisite: Junior Standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140145, 854856, 'RADT', '455B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Therapeutic Radiology (Formerly RADT 455B)', 'Individual investigation of selected problems in the Radiological Sciences. Prerequisite: Approval of the Department Head. F, Sp, S (Formerly RADT 455B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140157, 712874, 'THEA', '491E', 2020, 'Directed Study: Theatre Management (Formerly THEA 491E)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491E)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140158, 712874, 'THEA', '4096', 2020, 'Directed Study: Theatre Management (Formerly THEA 491E)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491E)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140162, 787083, 'THEA', '491D', 2020, 'Directed Study: Technical Theatre (Formerly THEA 491D)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491D)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140163, 787083, 'THEA', '4095', 2020, 'Directed Study: Technical Theatre (Formerly THEA 491D)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491D)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140173, 931660, 'MILS', '499', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Maximum 9 cr. Directed study at a military installation: A. Air Assault School; B. Airborne School; C. Cadet Troop Leader Training; D. Northern Warfare Training; E. Mountain Warfare Training; F. Other. Prerequisite: Approval of the Professor of Military Science.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140205, 498047, 'DHYG', '432A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Education and Supervision (Formerly DHYG 432A)', '1-3 credits; maximum, 9 credits. Individual study and/or research in selected dental hygiene topics. Prerequisite: Approval of program director. (Formerly DHYG 432A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140207, 400439, 'FCSC', '211', 2020, 'Residential Studio', 'Design of residential interiors for client use; emphasis on programming, planning for spatial requirements and presentation of floor plans, swatch boards, elevations. Six hours studio. Prerequisites: FCSC 2006.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140227, 517865, 'ENGL', '351', 2020, 'Junior Seminar: Poetry / Drama', 'Intensive study of a significant body of poetry and/or drama, with an emphasis on close reading. Prerequisite: one 2000-level literature course in English.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140228, 546350, 'RADT', '4013', 2020, 'Advanced Clinical Radiography', 'Twenty-one hours per week of supervised clinical experience in an approved medical center. Prerequisites: Credit or registration in RADT 3028, 4003, 4005, 4009, 4010, 4019. F', 5.0000, 5.0000, 5.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140229, 790653, 'ENGL', '220A', 2020, 'Technical Writing: Pharmacy & Health Sciences', '3 cr. Instruction in technical and professional writing and communication in health sciences. Emphasis on written and oral forms. Includes practice in documentation, collaboration, oral presentation and research in the field. Prerequisites: ENGL 102 or 103; junior standing or permission of English Dept. head; restricted to health sciences majors. (same as ENGL 220A)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140268, 249183, 'MLSC', '3025', 2020, 'Clinical Chemistry and Toxicology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 3024 including qualitative and quantitative analysis of physiologic components and composition of the various components of blood and other body fluids and methods of analysis for toxic substances. Three hours laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp (Formerly CLSC 325)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140276, 967620, 'TOXI', '4013', 2020, 'General Toxicology Laboratory', 'Laboratory exercises to accompany 4011. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 4011. Toxicology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140277, 967620, 'TOXI', '413', 2020, 'General Toxicology Laboratory', 'Laboratory exercises to accompany 4011. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 4011. Toxicology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140278, 615903, 'TOXI', '4024', 2020, 'Clinical Toxicology', 'Information on the clinical management of poisonings including the assessment of toxic potential, stabilization of vital function, and specific antidotal measures. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in TOXI 4012, 4014. F (Same as PHARM 5024).', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140279, 335202, 'THEA', '4019', 2020, 'Children’s Theatre', 'Teaches the selection, direction of plays for child audiences.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140280, 119817, 'THEA', '4023', 2020, 'Creative Dramatics', 'Teaches the use of imaginative and creative activities for instruction in college, secondary and elementary school programs.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140281, 16214, 'THEA', '4027', 2020, 'Theatre Leadership and Management', 'House and box office management, public relations and program development for arts production.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140282, 921248, 'THEA', '4031', 2020, 'Summer Theatre Production', 'Provides practical application of theatre skills in a summer theatre environment. Students participation is determined through audition and application process. Prerequisite: Permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140284, 413856, 'TOXI', '4001', 2020, 'General Laboratory Techniques', 'This class is designed to provide the student with basic skills required to work in a toxicology laboratory. Prerequisite: Consent of instructor. Toxicology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140287, 308329, 'CMST', '4053', 2020, 'Rhetoric of Social Movements', 'Understanding and analyzing social movements that seek to create social and/or political change, using primary texts from social movements as well as rhetorical scholarship that analyses social movements. Examines discourses and images used for gaining compliance, changing attitudes/behaviors, inspiring action, and creating social change. Prerequisite: COMM 3030 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4053)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140288, 253183, 'THEA', '1002', 2020, 'Play Reading II', 'Reading and discussing 15 plays by contemporary non-American playwrights. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140289, 837996, 'THEA', '1010', 2020, 'Theatre Fundamentals: Skills', 'Teaches the basic skills required to function in a production company: Production Organization, Scene Shop Skills, Property Operations, Electrical Operations, Scene Painting, Sound Operations, Costume Shop Operations, Wardrobe Operations, and Make-up Operations. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140290, 904301, 'THEA', '2002', 2020, 'Play Reading IV', 'Reading and discussing 15 plays by Modern European playwrights. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140291, 62904, 'THEA', '3021', 2020, 'Intermediate Acting', 'Teaches intermediate skills in specialized areas such as auditioning, performance of musical theater and period styles. Topic and credit varies with the subject matter. Prerequisite: THEA 221 or permission of instructor. May be repeated for a maximum of nine credits.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140292, 355392, 'THEA', '3000', 2020, 'Directed Study-- E-Tv', 'Content Varies. A. Drama: Play, performances, and perception. No more than 12 semester hours may be applied toward degree requirements.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140293, 454686, 'THEA', '4009', 2020, 'Dramatic Literature, Theory, and Criticism', 'A study of the developments in Western dramatic theory, literature, and criticism from the ancient Greeks to the present.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140294, 162495, 'THEA', '4087', 2020, 'Senior Recital', 'Provides a culminating project for performance students to demonstrate their proficiency. Prerequisite: Permission of the Director of Theater.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140295, 311510, 'THEA', '4015', 2020, 'Theatre History I', 'Studies the history of theatre art and dramatic literature from primitive beginnings to the year 1700. Emphasis is placed on historical research in support of design and directing concept development. Prerequisite: HIST 1011, 1012 or consent of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140296, 915888, 'THEA', '3003', 2020, 'Lighting', 'Teaches theory, design and practice of lighting for theater, television and film. Laboratory hours on Theatre Works.ULM productions required.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140297, 19614, 'THEA', '3009', 2020, 'Playwrighting', 'Teaches the writing of short plays through theory, example and practice.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140298, 862006, 'THEA', '3060', 2020, 'Costume Construction', 'Teaches pattern drawing, costume alteration and sewing for theatre, television and film through application projects. Laboratory hours on TheatreWorks.ULM productions required.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140299, 213417, 'THEA', '2021', 2020, 'Beginning Acting', 'Teaches the basic skills of memorization, relaxation, concentration, physicalization, vocal control and script interpretation through exercises and scene study.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140300, 207095, 'THEA', '3001', 2020, 'Scenic Construction', 'Teaches principles and techniques for the building, rigging and shifting of scenery through study, exercises and application. Laboratory hours on TheatreWorks.ULM productions required.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140301, 281264, 'CMST', '3004', 2020, 'Intercultural Communication', 'An international perspective on communication between members of different cultures. Verbal and nonverbal code systems, social patterns, values, and belief systems examined as they affect the sharing of meaning. Special attention given to Health Care, Business, and Education contexts. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. May not be used as a substitute for a foreign language. (Formerly CMST 4004)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140302, 81652, 'MCOM', '352', 2020, 'Video Production', 'Introduction to in-studio video production, including camera techniques and effects, equipment utilization and lighting. One hour lecture, four hours studio. Additional course fee. (Formerly MCOM 3052)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140303, 28651, 'SPCH', '451', 2020, 'American Public Address', 'Provides a study of American public address from colonial times to the present. Prerequisite: COMM 2001, 3030 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4051)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140304, 511210, 'CMST', '450', 2020, 'Communciation Theory', 'An analysis and evaluation of predominant communication theories that identify fundamental communicative forces in human action. Prerequisite: COMM 1018, 2010 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4050)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140305, 511210, 'CMST', '4050', 2020, 'Communciation Theory', 'An analysis and evaluation of predominant communication theories that identify fundamental communicative forces in human action. Prerequisite: COMM 1018, 2010 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4050)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140306, 960977, 'SPCH', '4026', 2020, 'Health Communications', 'The study of communication perspectives and skills helpful in providing integrated, coordinated services between various allied health professions. Prerequisite: Junior standing.(Formerly CMST 4026)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140307, 877251, 'CMST', '4062', 2020, 'Advanced Small Group Communication', 'Studies of group action, interaction, and leadership designed to apply small group theory. Emphasis on the nature of group communication as exemplified in the discussion/conference model. Prerequisites: COMM 2060 or consent of instructor. (Formerly COMM 4062)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140308, 934543, 'COMM', '3042', 2020, 'Communication and Gender', 'Exploration of how gender and communication interact, how gender influences communication, how gender is communicated, and how communication influences our understandings of gender and what it means to be gendered beings. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3041)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140309, 224533, 'SPAN', '3012', 2020, 'Culture and Civilization of Mexico', 'Advanced studies in the history and culture of Mexico with continued emphasis on understanding, speaking, reading, and writing. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140310, 888508, 'MATH', '250', 2020, 'Numerical Foundations for Teachers', 'Students will discuss problem solving strategies, and investigate elementary number theory, arithmetic operations and algorithms. Emphasis is placed on applying the processes of problem solving, reasoning, connections, communications, and representation by combining discussion, modeling, manipulatives, cooperative learning and technology. For Elementary Education Majors only. Prerequisite: A grade of \"C\" or better in MATH 1009 or MATH 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140311, 803389, 'MATH', '2055', 2020, 'Mathematical and Statistical Foundations for Elementary Teachers', 'Students will analyze patterns, functions, algebraic underpinnings, and statistics. Emphasis is placed in the processes of problem solving, reasoning and proof, describing and analyzing data, probability explorations, connections, communications and representation by combining discussion, modeling, manipulatives, cooperative learning and technology. For Elementary Education Majors only. Prerequisite: A grade of &quot;C&quot; or better in Math 2050. (Students may not receive credit for MATH 2055 if they have credit in MATH 2052.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140312, 593542, 'SPED', '4063', 2020, 'Student Teaching for Special Education', 'Directed observation and participation in special education situations. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140313, 509408, 'SPED', '4064', 2020, 'Student Teaching for Special Education', 'Eighteen weeks directed observation and participation in special education. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 9.0000, 9.0000, 9.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140314, 302793, 'SPCH', '1000', 2020, 'Foundations of Speech Communication', 'Experiential learning approach to special problems in communication: articulation, speech anxiety, interviews, presentational skills, and related concerns. This course does not replace or substitute for a required course.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140315, 246606, 'COMM', '1018', 2020, 'Interpersonal Communication', 'Stresses practical application of communication concepts and skills. Emphasis on self-concept, language, perception, listening, nonverbal communication, and resolution of interpersonal skills development.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCOM 2213', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140316, 874501, 'MUSC', '192', 2020, 'Enjoyment of Jazz', 'Logical musical derivations and developments of American Jazz, both of itself as an art form and its influence on other areas of music. Ethnic influences such as Afro-American Jazz, New Orleans ragtime, and Memphis influences will be explored.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CMUS 1023', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140317, 475376, 'MCOM', '2002', 2020, 'Media Performance', 'The role of the announcer; principles of communication in the electronic media; voice and diction, including foreign pronunciation; techniques for various program types. Lecture and lab. A fee is charged each student to help defray expenses related to this course.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140319, 414715, 'CMST', '3011', 2020, 'Argumentation and Debate', 'Argumentation as a method for critical inquiry. Emphasis on debate as argument exemplar with instruction in analysis, reasoning, and use of evidence. Participation in debates. Prerequisite: COMM 2001 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3011)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140320, 33246, 'CMST', '335', 2020, 'Nonverbal Communication', 'The process of generating and interpreting messages from such nonverbal sources as space, physical appearance, time, facial expressions, and other nonverbal codes explored for effects on interpersonal relationships. Prerequisite: COMM 1018, 2001 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3035)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140321, 44248, 'SPAN', '3007', 2020, 'Survey of Spanish Literature', 'Selection from the outstanding authors of Spain. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140322, 44248, 'SPAN', '307', 2020, 'Survey of Spanish Literature', 'Selection from the outstanding authors of Spain. Prerequisite: SPAN 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140323, 347842, 'SOCL', '447A', 2020, 'Regional United States Field Studies: North (Formerly SOCL 447A)', 'Extended thematic field study within the United States with guest lectures, tours, and assigned readings. May not be repeated for credit. (Formerly SOCL 447A)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140324, 110129, 'SOCL', '4025', 2020, 'Seminar in Death and Dying', 'Exploration of the social organization of dying, including a view on cross-cultural perspectives on death, treatment of the dying patient, and the grief process. (Same as GERO 4025)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140325, 339759, 'SOCL', '3010', 2020, 'Sociology in Film', 'An examination of sociological concepts and themes in American and foreign popular and educational films. A fee will be assessed to cover partial cost of film rental.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140326, 296790, 'SOCL', '4036', 2020, 'Seminar in the Development of Sociology', 'The study of social thought that influenced sociological ideas and concepts. Recent trends and influences in modern sociology will be discussed.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140327, 736722, 'SOCL', '4004', 2020, 'Medical Sociology', 'An analysis of human adaptation to illness, the sick role, social organization of medical institutions, and the sociology of death.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140328, 632503, 'SOCL', '4019', 2020, 'The Family', 'The past and present role of the family as the primary social group in our culture; problems facing the modern family in a changing social world.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140329, 437501, 'SOCW', '4001', 2020, 'The Child and the Community', 'Examines the common and particular needs of children in the community, social welfare services and resources developed by communities for the care and training of children. Prerequisites: Junior standing, or approval of department head and/or instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140330, 764899, 'SOCW', '4016', 2020, 'Practice II', 'Generalist social work theory and its application at the macro level of practice. This course will focus on the application of social work skills of assessment and problem- solving at the organizational and community level. To be taken concurrently with Social Work 4021 and 4022.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140331, 816141, 'SOCW', '4006', 2020, 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'Defines the abused and neglected child and family and examines the dynamics associated with dysfunctional families. (May not receive credit for 406 and 408.)', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140332, 816141, 'SOCW', '406', 2020, 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'Defines the abused and neglected child and family and examines the dynamics associated with dysfunctional families. (May not receive credit for 406 and 408.)', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140333, 960977, 'CMST', '426', 2020, 'Health Communications', 'The study of communication perspectives and skills helpful in providing integrated, coordinated services between various allied health professions. Prerequisite: Junior standing.(Formerly CMST 4026)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140334, 911329, 'SOCW', '4010', 2020, 'Human Services in a Rural Environment', 'This course examines human services in rural environments, stressing the social and cultural factors that affect the delivery of services in rural environments. Focus is on the practice shills and resource knowledge base needed by the helping professional to be most effective working with rural micro, mezzo, and macro client systems. Prerequisites: Junior standing, or approval of the department head and/or instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140335, 356557, 'SOCW', '4003', 2020, 'Family VIolence and Social Work Practice', 'Identifies the four major kinds of violence with families; assesses the dynamics and complex issues associated with family violence and their implications for the social worker; looks at current local, state, and national efforts to resolve the problem. Emphasis is on an overview of treatment and prevention programs for victims and perpetrators of domestic violence. Prerequisites: Junior level standing, or permission of the department head and/or the instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140336, 784782, 'SOCW', '3019', 2020, 'Challenges and Services Related to Aging', 'Examines the challenges people experience in relation to or as a consequence of aging, and the resources available to deal with specific problems.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140337, 423385, 'SOCW', '4005', 2020, 'Differential Diagnosis', 'An organized introduction to and synopsis of the criteria for the individual diagnoses in the DSM-IV and other diagnostic tools related to the functionality of human behavior in the context of diverse social systems. Prerequisites: PSYC 2001 and 4001, and junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140338, 495400, 'RADT', '4010', 2020, 'Advanced Procedures Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 409. Prerequisite: Registration in RADT 409. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140339, 33495, 'RADT', '4012', 2020, 'Advanced Radiographic Procedures Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany RADT 411. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140340, 147510, 'RADT', '4019', 2020, 'Pathology', 'A general survey of medical and surgical diseases related to diagnostic radiography. Prerequisite: BIOL 1014, 1015, 1016, 1017, and 2014 or 2028.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140341, 947109, 'RADT', '4027', 2020, 'Advanced Imaging', 'Generators, digital image manipulation and controls, digital fluoroscopy, and subtraction radiography. Introduction to Ultrasound, MRI, and Nuclear Medicine image acquisition. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140342, 510176, 'READ', '3021', 2020, 'Reading in the Primary Grades', 'Materials and methods for beginning reading instruction. Must be admitted to Teacher Education. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140344, 805696, 'SPED', '4081', 2020, 'Continuing Studies in Special Education', 'Various topics in special education. May be repeated. Credit may not be applied toward a degree. Grade of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140345, 788635, 'RADT', '3016', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures I', 'The principles and skills involved in routine radiographic positioning to deomonstrate the thoracic/abdominal cavities, and extremities and associated girdles. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `courses` VALUES (140346, 442379, 'RADT', '3017', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures Laboratory I', 'A laboratory course to accompany RADT 3016. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140347, 442379, 'RADT', '317', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures Laboratory I', 'A laboratory course to accompany RADT 3016. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140348, 7941, 'RADT', '3027', 2020, 'Clinical Radiography', 'Thirty-five hours per week of supervised clinical experience in an approved medical center. Prerequisite: RADT 324. S', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140349, 701541, 'BUSN', '3001', 2020, 'International Business', 'Designed to focus on the environment of international business. Course content includes strategic issues for the functions of marketing, operations, human resources, finance, accounting, and information systems while also addressing legal, ethical, and cultural issues from a global perspective. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140350, 262164, 'RADT', '4011', 2020, 'Advanced Radiographic Procedures', 'The principles and skills involved in radiographic procedures. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140351, 538013, 'PSYC', '3039', 2020, 'Introduction to Research Methods', 'An introduction into the basics of scientific research methods with emphasis on the applications of research to psychological and educational topics. Prerequisite: PSYC 2001. F, Sp, Su', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140352, 62941, 'RADT', '3009', 2020, 'Methods of Patient Care', 'General patient care, principles of body mechanics, and specific nursing procedures related to radiologic technology. Prerequisite: RADT 2004. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140353, 132007, 'RADT', '3013', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures', 'The principles and skills involved in routine radiographic positioning to demonstrate the extremities and associated girdles. Prerequisites: RADT 204; BIOL 114, 115, 116, 117, and 214 or 228; registration in RADT 314. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140354, 299251, 'RADT', '3011', 2020, 'Imaging Equipment and Radiation Production', 'Introduction to the systems, components, and processes of x-ray production, x-ray interaction with matter, and radiation protection. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140355, 223153, 'PHIL', '407', 2020, 'Theories of Human Nature', 'This course will cover the theories of human nature that have arisen historically and also in the contemporary world. Major figures to be covered include Plato, Aristotle, Aquinas, Hobbes, Locke, Hume, Kant, Darwin, Marx, Nietzche, Freud, Sartre, Maslow, and Contemporary Psychological theories. This course will answer questions like what is the human being3, what are human beings capable of3, what does it mean to live a fulfilled human life3, what is the purpose of human life1, is the human being basically aggressive or kind, and how do human beings differ from animals', 0.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140356, 257077, 'MLSC', '3048', 2020, 'Directed Study: Other Problems in Medical Lab Science (Formerly CLSC 338J)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338J)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140357, 224676, 'MUSC', '2012', 2020, 'Brass Ensemble', 'Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated. Music and Music Education majors must enroll for zero credit.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 10.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140358, 224676, 'MUSC', '212', 2020, 'Brass Ensemble', 'Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated. Music and Music Education majors must enroll for zero credit.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 10.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140359, 715927, 'PHIL', '491A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Logic', 'Directed study and/or research in selected areas of philosophy. A. Logic; B. Ethics; C. Ancient, Medieval, and Modern; D. Theory of Knowledge. Prerequisite: Advanced standing, approval of department head, and permission of the instructor.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140360, 257077, 'CLSC', '338J', 2020, 'Directed Study: Other Problems in Medical Lab Science (Formerly CLSC 338J)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338J)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140361, 969405, 'PSYC', '4041', 2020, 'Psychology of Child Abuse', 'Identification, treatment, and prevention of child abuse and neglect. F, Sp, Su', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140362, 73989, 'PSYC', '4027', 2020, 'Theories of Personality', 'Survey of the dominant personality theories. Prerequisite: nine hours of psychology. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140363, 639249, 'PSYC', '4025', 2020, 'Psychology of Adulthood and Aging', 'Study of physical, intellectual, personality, social and emotional development during the middle and older years of the life span. Su', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140364, 116760, 'PSYC', '3025', 2020, 'Human Learning and Cognition', 'Principles of knowledge acquisition and usage in humans. Emphasis on the structure, processes, and models of memory, attention, information processing, and the neural basis of cognition. Prerequisite: PSYC 2001. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140365, 35003, 'PSYC', '4003', 2020, 'Exceptional Children and Youth', 'Legal definitions and clinical classifications of children and youth who vary from normal (mentally, physically, or emotionally). Emphasis on etiology, identification, and educational service provision in multicultural settings. Prerequisite: PSYC 2001, 2003. (Formerly The Exceptional Child.) Su', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140366, 706039, 'PSYC', '317', 2020, 'Learning Laboratory', 'A laboratory to accompany PSYC 315. Three hours laboratory.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140367, 351909, 'POLS', '202', 2020, 'State and Local Government', 'An intensive study of state and local government, structural components, political process, and basic problems. Special emphasis on Louisiana government.<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CPOL 2113', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140368, 549413, 'PSYC', '3015', 2020, 'Learning and Motivation', 'Principles of learning and related principles of motivation and memory, with emphasis on scientific method and experimental findings. Prerequisite: PSYC 2001. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140369, 549413, 'PSYC', '315', 2020, 'Learning and Motivation', 'Principles of learning and related principles of motivation and memory, with emphasis on scientific method and experimental findings. Prerequisite: PSYC 2001. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140370, 997123, 'PHIL', '410', 2020, 'Environmental Philosophy', 'Philosophical issues regarding the ethics, aesthetics and economics of the environment along with a meta-critique of the science of the environment.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140371, 755740, 'PHIL', '401', 2020, 'Ancient and Medieval', 'Philosophical thought from the Pre-Socratic to the sixteenth century, including Plato and Aristotle, the Epicureans and the Stoics, the Neo-Platonists, and Aquinas; the rise and fall of medieval scholasticism. (Formerly 301.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140372, 420107, 'PHIL', '300A', 2020, 'Directed Study: a Study of Religion', 'Selected studies in Philosophy and Religion. Content varies. A. A Study of Religion. (Same as Philosophy 300A.) B. Ethics in America. C. The Examined Life.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140396, 143424, 'PHAR', '4089', 2020, 'Introductory Toxicology', 'Survey of the occurrence, properties and harmful effects of natural and man-made toxic substances in personal, occupational and global environments. Prerequisites: Credit or registration in Zoology 3011, 3013, and Chemistry 3004.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140397, 17903, 'PHAR', '494', 2020, 'Retail Pharmacy Management', 'Principles and problems related to the planning, organizing, and controlling of the retail pharmacy. Prerequisite: 451.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140399, 242604, 'PHAR', '423', 2020, 'Medical Immunology', 'Cellular and serum immunology. Antibody structure and function. Types of antigen antibody reactions. Immunosuppression, tolerance and enhancement. Systems mediating immunologic injury and inflammation. Immunogenetics. Prerequisites: 4008, 4012, 4036.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140400, 397589, 'PHAR', '454', 2020, 'Law', 'Local, state and federal laws, rules and regulations relating to the practice of Pharmacy. Prerequisite: Second Year Pharmacy.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140401, 2188, 'PHAR', '425', 2020, 'Drug Information Retrieval and Evaluation', 'Introduction to services and resources used to provide evaluative information and associated professional responsibilities. Prerequisite: First Year Pharmacy Standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140402, 745834, 'PHAR', '4070', 2020, 'Hospital Pharmacy', 'The history of hospitals, organization and administration of patient care facilities, distribution of pharmaceuticals to inpatients and outpatients, abilities required of the pharmacist, and the many roles of the pharmacist as a member of the health team. Prerequisites: Second Year Pharmacy Standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140403, 261200, 'PHAR', '4036', 2020, 'Pharmacology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 412. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: 411; credit or registration in 412.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140404, 261200, 'PHAR', '436', 2020, 'Pharmacology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 412. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: 411; credit or registration in 412.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140405, 978726, 'PHAR', '4050', 2020, 'Pharmacy Care Lab IV', 'A capstone course aimed at further development of problem solving skills relevant to making clinical decisions and solving medication related problems. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in Pharmacy 414, 418, 587.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140406, 978726, 'PHAR', '450', 2020, 'Pharmacy Care Lab IV', 'A capstone course aimed at further development of problem solving skills relevant to making clinical decisions and solving medication related problems. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in Pharmacy 414, 418, 587.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140407, 830807, 'PHAR', '4024', 2020, 'Pharmaceutics IV', 'A study of parenterally administered drugs and specialized delivery systems. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory per week. Prerequisite: 432.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140408, 11082, 'PHAR', '4046', 2020, 'Non-Prescription Medications and Self-Care', 'Selection and use of non-prescription medications for self- treatment of disease or to treat self-limiting disease states. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 413.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140409, 455998, 'PHAR', '4026', 2020, 'Aging and Drug Use in the Elderly', 'An examination of normative and pathological aging and their effect on drug use and response in the aged population. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 414.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140410, 11082, 'PHAR', '446', 2020, 'Non-Prescription Medications and Self-Care', 'Selection and use of non-prescription medications for self- treatment of disease or to treat self-limiting disease states. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 413.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140413, 473903, 'PHAR', '4079', 2020, 'Nuclear Pharmacy', 'Handling and stora