e to advanced melodic and rhythmic dictation and sight-singing and intermediate harmonic dictation. Prerequisite: MUSC 1005 or equivalent. (Formerly 271)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140502, 578811, 'MUSC', '1093', 2020, 'Literature and Appreciation', 'For music majors; open to others by approval of the Head of the Division of Music.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140503, 556735, 'MUSC', '1017', 2020, 'Beginning and Intermediate Recorder Class', 'There is no course description available at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140504, 962172, 'ART', '101', 2020, 'Basic Design', 'Introduction to art structure and general analysis of the principles and elements of design. One hour lecture and five hours studio.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CART 1113', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140505, 586092, 'MUSC', '104', 2020, 'Music Theory II', 'Course covers the use and function of cadences, phrases, non-chord tones and seventh chords. Prerequisite: MUSC 1002 or equivalent.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140506, 733650, 'MUSC', '105', 2020, 'Aural Skills II', 'Course covers intermediate melodic dictation, rhythmic dictation and sight-singing. Fundamentals of harmonic dictation are introduced. Prerequisite: MUSC 1003 or equivalent.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140507, 4148, 'MILS', '310', 2020, 'Leadership Tactics', 'Military leadership principles, land navigation, small unit tactics, and physical training. Registration in MILS 3011 required.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140508, 957929, 'MILS', '3011', 2020, 'Advanced Leadership Lab I', 'Laboratory course to accompany MILS 3010. A practical laboratory of applied leadership that is planned and executed by the MS IV cadets. Activities include drill and ceremonies, land navigation, rappelling, rifle marksmanship, tactics, first aid, water survival, physical conditioning, and communications.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140509, 7