 '4002', 2020, 'Linear Spaces', 'A study of abstract vector spaces including function spaces, linear transformations, operators, functionals and duality, bilinear and quadratic forms. Prerequisite: MATH 2002, 1032.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140541, 710835, 'MATH', '4031', 2020, 'Fundamentals of High School Mathematics I', 'Emphasis is on teaching at the high school level. Topics include, but are not restricted to, number concepts and relationships, geometry and measurement. Not applicable toward a major or minor in mathematics. Applies to middle and high school certification.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140542, 384911, 'MATH', '4025', 2020, 'Advanced Modern Algebra', 'Continuation of Math 3086; Euclidean domains, unique factorization domains, principal ideal domains, Galois theory and related topics. Prerequisite: A grade of &quot;C&quot; or better in MATH 3086.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140543, 384911, 'MATH', '425', 2020, 'Advanced Modern Algebra', 'Continuation of Math 3086; Euclidean domains, unique factorization domains, principal ideal domains, Galois theory and related topics. Prerequisite: A grade of &quot;C&quot; or better in MATH 3086.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140544, 111575, 'MATH', '4019', 2020, 'Topology', 'Point sets, axiomatic bases, topology of the line and the plane. Emphasis on connectedness, compact sets, and continuous transformations. Prerequisite: MATH 2040 and 1032.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140545, 111575, 'MATH', '419', 2020, 'Topology', 'Point sets, axiomatic bases, topology of the line and the plane. Emphasis on connectedness, compact sets, and continuous transformations. Prerequisite: MATH 2040 and 1032.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140546, 8081, 'MCOM', '435', 2020, 'Journalism Management', 'Methods and practices for the production, promotion, and management of print and broadcast news; issues and techniques of managing and leading media companies in rapidly changing business and cultural environments. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140548, 119169, 'MCOM', '4051', 2020, 'Advanced Photocommunication', 'Theory and tecniques of photocommunication for print media, emphasizing use of still photography for in-depth investigating and reporting. Prerequisite: MCOM 351.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140549, 382343, 'MCOM', '4045', 2020, 'Broadcast Management', 'Organization and administration of broadcast stations and other electronic media systems, with attention to operations, community relations, and financial management. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140550, 780893, 'COMM', '4071', 2020, 'Visual Communication', 'Theories of perception, methods of analysis of visual media, and principles and strategies of visual communication, emphasizing critical thinking about the role and function of media in society.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140551, 248813, 'MCOM', '4050', 2020, 'Advanced Audio Production', 'Theory and advanced techniques of audio production for radio, video, film and music recording, from conception through completion, emphasizing multitrack, non-destructive, and non-linear production. A fee is charged each student to help defray expenses related to this course. Prerequisite: MCOM 350.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140552, 718035, 'MCOM', '3061', 2020, 'Public Relations Writing and Planning', 'Publicity planning, writing for all media, and developing techniques for working with mass media and other publics. Lecture and lab. Prerequisite: COMM 2010. (Formerly MCOM\r\n3061)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140553, 526970, 'MCOM', '3053', 2020, 'Film Production', 'Introduction to cinematography, production techniques, equipment utilization and editing in 8mm and 16mm formats. A fee is charged each student to help defray expenses related to this course. Prerequisite: Sophomore standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140554, 450315, 'COMM', '2000', 2020, 'Mass Media and Society', 'History, structure and practices of media industries and professions, and their roles in society; introduction to issues, vocabulary and technological trends for media producers. (Formerly MCOM 2001)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140555, 3883417, 'MCOM', '4009', 2020, 'Feature & Editorial Writing', 'Researching and writing human-interest features; analyzing political, social and economic affairs and writing opinions; print, Web and electronic media styles and formats. Prerequisite: COMM 2010. (Formerly MCOM 4009)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140556, 3883417, 'COMM', '4009', 2020, 'Feature & Editorial Writing', 'Researching and writing human-interest features; analyzing political, social and economic affairs and writing opinions; print, Web and electronic media styles and formats. Prerequisite: COMM 2010. (Formerly MCOM 4009)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140557, 339718, 'MCOM', '3080', 2020, 'Mass Communication Ethics', 'Theories of ethics and the practice of ethical decision-making in mass communications professions and situations. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140558, 873481, 'MCOM', '3050', 2020, 'Audio Production', 'Introduction to audio production for radio, video, film and music recording, including principles, equipment, pre-production, production, and post-production. A fee is charged each student to help defray expenses related to this course. Prerequisite: Sophomore standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140559, 91333, 'COMM', '4033', 2020, 'Electronic News Gathering', 'Concepts and practices of news coverage for the electronic media, with special attention to field techniques, visualization and editing. Lecture and studio. Additional course fee. Prerequisite: COMM 2030. (Formerly MCOM 4033)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140560, 533212, 'MCOM', '4030', 2020, 'Investigative Journalism', 'Investigating and in-depth reporting/writing on single topics such as crime, corporate malfeasance, political corruption and institutional neglect; print, Web and electronic media styles and formats. Prerequisite: COMM 2030. (Formerly MCOM 4030)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140561, 843949, 'MNSC', '4055', 2020, 'Marine Vertebrate Zoology', 'Field and laboratory studies of marine vertebrates with particular emphasis on the fishes, including classification, structure, function, and ecology. Prerequisites: 16 semester hours of zoology and permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140562, 953867, 'MNSC', '4060', 2020, 'Coastal Marine Geology', 'Geomorphologic features of estuarine, coastal, and continental shelf environments; erosional, depositional, and geochemical processes; field and laboratory methods. Prerequisites: physical and historical geology; general chemistry or mineralogy; and permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140563, 191066, 'MNSC', '4070', 2020, 'Marine Environmental Chemistry', 'Chemical composition of the oceans; chemical, biological, and geological interactions. Prerequisites: 16 semester hours of chemistry and permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140564, 304198, 'MRKT', '3004', 2020, 'Sales Management', 'Organization of sales departments; selecting; training, compensating, motivating, and maintaining sales personnel; budgeting; distribution cost analysis; special problems in managing an outside sales force. Prerequisite: MRKT 301. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140565, 240733, 'MRKT', '4003', 2020, 'Services Marketing', 'Study of the special characteristics of service enterprises and the development of marketing strategies for such organizations. Prerequisites: MRKT 3001. Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140566, 240733, 'MRKT', '403', 2020, 'Services Marketing', 'Study of the special characteristics of service enterprises and the development of marketing strategies for such organizations. Prerequisites: MRKT 3001. Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140567, 121767, 'MCOM', '3040', 2020, 'Advertising Principles', 'Survey of the role and function of advertising in society: structures, media roles, and basic techniques and creative strategies as they apply to print and electronic media. Prerequisite: Sophomore standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140568, 209311, 'MCOM', '331', 2020, 'Journalism II', 'Builds upon MCOM 330 with development of news gathering, writing and editing for print and broadcast media, emphasizing interviewing techniques, newscasting and special events and stories. Students will be assigned campus beats. Prerequisite: MCOM 330.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140569, 209311, 'MCOM', '3031', 2020, 'Journalism II', 'Builds upon MCOM 330 with development of news gathering, writing and editing for print and broadcast media, emphasizing interviewing techniques, newscasting and special events and stories. Students will be assigned campus beats. Prerequisite: MCOM 330.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140570, 870910, 'MCOM', '2020', 2020, 'Evolution of American Journalism', 'The struggle of American journalists from colonial to modern times to develop, preserve and extend responsible reporting in print and electronic media.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140571, 950219, 'MCOM', '2021', 2020, 'Evolution of Broadcasting', 'History of the development of radio, television, cable, satellite and other electronic media industries and media production practices.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140572, 643656, 'MCOM', '3000', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Selected studies in mass communications. Content varies. Prerequisite: Consent of advisor and instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140573, 266562, 'MCOM', '3011', 2020, 'Feature Writing', 'Preparation of human interest and feature articles for newspapers and magazines. Prerequisite: MCOM 210 or consent of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140574, 800320, 'MCOM', '370', 2020, 'Mass Communication Theory and Research', 'Theories and research techniques for the study of mass communications processes and effects, emphasizing methods of audience identification, measurement and evaluation for print and electronic media. Prerequisites: MATH 1011 or higher; junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140575, 653488, 'MNSC', '4050', 2020, 'Marine Invertebrate Zoology', 'General study of the classification, structure, function, and ecology of marine and estuarine invertebrates; emphasis on field studies of invertebrates of the Louisiana Gulf Coast. Prerequisites: 8 semester hours of zoology and permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140576, 927582, 'MGMT', '413', 2020, 'Supply Chain Management', 'Examines the integration and coordination of activities, such as purchasing, outsourcing, materials management, logistics, supplier selection, and global sourcing to create an efficient and effective flow of materials. Prerequisite: 3001 or MRKT 3001 or consent of management program coordinator. S,F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140577, 565655, 'MGMT', '4014', 2020, 'Quality Management', 'Examines the design of products and services using control processes for continuous and total quality improvement. Explores service and manufacturing industries and a variety of methods and procedures for quality analysis and improvement. Addresses analytical methods for maintaining quality. Prerequisite: 3009 or consent of management program coordinator. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140579, 580183, 'MNSC', '4011', 2020, 'Marine Field Ecology', 'Relationships of marine and estuarine organisms to environmental factors; interactions among organisms; ecological processes of energy and materials flow; field studies of communities and ecosystems of the Louisiana coastal zone. Prerequisites: BIOL 1020, 1021; 3030 or 3032; CHEM 1007, 1009; permission of instructor. Four weeks. LUMCON Summer course; alternating years.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140580, 653754, 'MNSC', '3001', 2020, 'Introduction to Marine Zoology', 'Field and laboratory survey of marine animals, particularly those of the Louisiana Gulf Coast, including classification, morphology, physiology, and ecology. Prerequisites: Biology 204, 205, 208, 209; permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140581, 664170, 'MNSC', '4001', 2020, 'Marine Botany', 'Study of marine and coastal algae and vascular plants, including classification, morphology, life cycles, and ecology; emphasis on field and laboratory studies. Prerequisites: 12 hours botany including Biology 438; permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140582, 405089, 'MNSC', '4010', 2020, 'Marine Ecology', 'Relationships of marine and estuarine organisms to environmental factors; interactions among organisms; ecological processes of energy and materials flow; field studies of communities and ecosystems of the Louisiana coastal zone. Prerequisite: Biology 204, 205, 330, 332; Chemistry 107, 109; permission of the instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140583, 146295, 'MGMT', '307', 2020, 'Human Resource Management', 'Examines organizational human resource management issues such as manpower planning, recruitment, selection, appraisal, compensation, transfer and promotion, safety; and other personnel topics. Prerequisite: 3001 or 3005 or approval of management program coordinator. F, Sum<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CMGM 3313', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140584, 331354, 'MCOM', '3090', 2020, 'Practicum', 'Supervised, on-campus application of methods and techniques in an area of mass communications. Prerequisite: Completion of 9 credit hours of COMM courses, plus approved practicum proposal. (Formerly MCOM 3090)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140585, 861505, 'MNSC', '4020', 2020, 'Marine Microbiology', 'Introduction to the estuarine and marine microbes, especially bacteria and fungi; classification, methodology, role in marine ecosystems, biogeochemical cycles, and diseases of marine animals. Prerequisites: 12 hours of biology, including Biology 214, 215; permission of instructor. Offered summer only. Five weeks at a Louisiana Universities Marine Consortium coastal laboratory.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140586, 191955, 'MGMT', '409', 2020, 'Strategic Management', 'Examines business policy and strategy formulation, implementation, and control from an overall management perspective. Requires strategy recommendations based on an integrative analysis of an organizations resources, capabilities and competencies, as well as external forces, trends, and influences that shape competition. Prerequisite: Business Law 4001, Computer Science 1070, Finance 3015, Management 3001, Marketing 3001, Business 3005, Quantitative Methods 2010, and senior standing in the College of Business Administration. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140588, 107773, 'LATN', '2008', 2020, 'Literature of the Late Republic', '1-3 credits; maximum, 3 credits. Prerequisite: LATN 2002 or approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140589, 678984, 'KINS', '4044', 2020, 'Health Education and Promotion Planning', 'This course will enhance student understanding of community health planning. Prerequisite: KINS 2041.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140590, 678984, 'KINS', '444', 2020, 'Health Education and Promotion Planning', 'This course will enhance student understanding of community health planning. Prerequisite: KINS 2041.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140591, 970598, 'KINS', '4031', 2020, 'Methods and Materials in Health Education', 'Materials, techniques, and methods of teaching health in schools. Ten (10) hours of classroom observation will be completed during this course. Prerequisite: Must be admitted to teacher education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140592, 207752, 'KINS', '445', 2020, 'Issues in Kinesiology', 'Develops student ability to research, critically examine, and debate controversial issues in kinesiology. Prerequisite: Junior standing', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140593, 207752, 'KINS', '4045', 2020, 'Issues in Kinesiology', 'Develops student ability to research, critically examine, and debate controversial issues in kinesiology. Prerequisite: Junior standing', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140594, 624476, 'LIBR', '3007', 2020, 'School Library Media Administration', 'Administration of school library media centers with emphasis on programs of service, objective and standards, and such management problems as acquisitions, mechanical preparation of materials, budgets, facilities, and evaluation. Includes clinical experiences and six hours of observations in library settings.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140595, 76940, 'LIBR', '3003', 2020, 'Young Adult Literature', 'Study of literature for young adults in grades seven - twelve. Emphasis on reading needs and interests of youth; principles of selection and evaluation; and extensive reading of books.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140596, 324254, 'LATN', '308', 2020, 'Literature of the Golden Age', '1-3 credits; maximum, 3 credits. Prerequisite: LATN 2002 or approval of the department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140597, 766665, 'LIBR', '3001', 2020, 'Children’s Literature', 'Survey of literature for children preschool - grade eight; application of criteria in selecting and evaluating types of literature for developmental and curriculum needs. Extensive reading of childrens books. Prerequisite: Approval of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140598, 240201, 'KINS', '4013', 2020, 'Management of Health, Physical Education, and Recr', 'The purpose and functions of the management process in the instructional and related area programs in todays classroom as well as experiences in those areas outside the normal classroom setting. Federal and state regulations in education, alternative programs, discipline and other current problems are discussed. Ten (10) hours of classroom observation will be completed during this course. Prerequisite: KINS 211 and Junior standing. (Formerly Administration and Health, Physical Education, and Recreation.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140599, 4330335, 'TOXI', '1010', 2020, 'Introduction to Food Safety and Toxicology', 'Focus on toxicology of drugs, pesticides and natural food toxins along with food\r\nadditives, preservatives and colors. Prerequisites: None, F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140600, 633125, 'KINS', '4019', 2020, 'Modern Fitness', 'Lectures and exercises designed to convert deconditioned people to conditioned status with sufficient basic knowledge to remain conditioned for a lifetime. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140601, 399417, 'KINS', '3034', 2020, 'Methods and Materials in Physical Education', 'Materials, techniques, and methods of teaching physical education in the three different school levels. Prerequisite: Must be admitted to teacher education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140602, 30095, 'KINS', '3065', 2020, 'Fitness', 'Basic knowledge, values, understanding, and teaching procedures of selected fitness programs. Courses also includes a review of health related fitness testing, risk factors, risk stratification, medical history and HPAA compliance. Prerequisite: KINS 2011, KINS 2021. Kinesiology majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140603, 261290, 'KINS', '4008', 2020, 'Physical Activity for Students With Special Needs', 'This course examines how physical activities and motor skills can be tasked analyzed and modified to include a wide range of individuals with special needs. Basic knowledge, skills and competencies in Special Education are covered with an emphasis in pedagogical principles.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140604, 310064, 'KINS', '2048', 2020, 'Officiating', 'Principles, techniques and practices of officiating with emphasis on rules, rule interpretations and mechanics of basketball and football. Practical experience will be arranged.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140605, 566603, 'KINS', '2049', 2020, 'Officiating Spring Sports', 'This course is designed to enhance the students ability to understand the basic principles, techniques, and practices of officiating youth sports with emphasis on rules, rule interpretations, and mechanics for Dixie League softball/baseball, FIFA U6-U19 soccer, and USTA tennis.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140606, 305606, 'KINS', '2056', 2020, 'Living With Health', 'Content and theory related to basic health information; critical health issues; improving and maintaining optimal health and wellness. Students with prior credit in Kinesiology 241 are not eligible to receive credit in Kinesiology 256. Cannot be used to satisfy major or minor requirements.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140607, 398321, 'KINS', '3001', 2020, 'Coaching Football', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching football. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140608, 693551, 'KINS', '3002', 2020, 'Coaching Basketball', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching basketball. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing. ', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140609, 890802, 'KINS', '3003', 2020, 'Coaching Baseball and Softball', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching baseball and softball. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140610, 759876, 'KINS', '3004', 2020, 'Coaching Track and Field', 'Theory, techniques, and skills of coaching track and field. Prerequisites: KINS 211 and junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140611, 906730, 'H&HP', '335', 2020, 'Team Sports', 'Basic skills, strategies, rules, and teaching procedures of selected team sports. Prerequisite: Health and physical education major.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140612, 947598, 'KINS', '432', 2020, 'Kinesiology and Biomechanics', 'Survey of the anatomy and physiology of human movement and biomechanical analysis of human motor performance. Prerequisite: KINS 2011. KINS majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140613, 745743, 'HORT', '4072', 2020, 'Plantscapes', 'The principles, techniques, and concepts used in interior and exterior plantscapes. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 1001 or 1003. (Formerly HORT 470, 471).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140614, 670492, 'INSU', '3011', 2020, 'Health and Social Insurance', 'Analysis of the nature of health and social insurance; hospitalization and medical insurance, surgical benefits, major-medical coverages, disability income contracts; causes, extent, and economic consequences of old age dependency, unemployment, and disability. Prerequisite: RMIN 2005 or permission of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140615, 183734, 'RMIN', '3020', 2020, 'Insurance Operations', 'Operations of an insurance company, including regulation, underwriting, claims, ratemaking, and the financial accounting process and global strategies of an insurance organization. Prerequisite: RMIN 2005', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140616, 394389, 'H&HP', '2033', 2020, 'Water Safety Instruction', 'Qualifies individuals to teach and certify American Red Cross Aquatic courses. Prerequisite: 2020.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140617, 416129, 'INSU', '4010', 2020, 'Insurance Internship', 'Planned and supervised work experience within the fields of risk management and insurance. Open only to juniors and seniors in Risk Management and Insurance program with approval of Director. Prerequisite: RMIN 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140618, 183734, 'INSU', '320', 2020, 'Insurance Operations', 'Operations of an insurance company, including regulation, underwriting, claims, ratemaking, and the financial accounting process and global strategies of an insurance organization. Prerequisite: RMIN 2005', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140619, 183734, 'INSU', '3020', 2020, 'Insurance Operations', 'Operations of an insurance company, including regulation, underwriting, claims, ratemaking, and the financial accounting process and global strategies of an insurance organization. Prerequisite: RMIN 2005', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140620, 307461, 'HORT', '4012', 2020, 'Vegetable and Fruit Industry', 'Management practices concerning establishment, production, storage and marketing of vegetables and fruits. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 1001 or 1003. (Formerly HORT 410, 411).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140621, 97891, 'HORT', '3062', 2020, 'Ornamental Horticulture', 'Principles and practices involved in the production, usage and maintenance of woody ornamentals, florist, and greenhouse plants. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 101 or 103. (Formerly HORT 360, 361).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140622, 109447, 'HORT', '3050', 2020, 'Floral Arranging', 'A survey of the art of floral arranging including the basic materials, equipment, design dish and bottle gardens, drying flowers, judging, corsages and specialty pieces. Prerequisites: AGRI 1001 or 1003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140623, 109447, 'HORT', '350', 2020, 'Floral Arranging', 'A survey of the art of floral arranging including the basic materials, equipment, design dish and bottle gardens, drying flowers, judging, corsages and specialty pieces. Prerequisites: AGRI 1001 or 1003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140624, 517339, 'HIST', '493', 2020, 'Soviet Union and Commonwealth of Independent State', 'The revolutions of 1917 and the development of the Soviet system. Political, social, and economic developments in the U.S.S.R. with special attention to the role of the Soviet Union in world affairs. The collapse of the U.S.S.R. and the emergence of the Commonwealth of Independent States. Prerequisite: HIST 112. (Formerly 425.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140625, 736089, 'HIST', '437', 2020, 'Reconstruction and the New South, 1865-1939', 'Reconstruction represented a larger change in the nations history than the Civil War as the South experienced its evolving stages, but more particularly, dealing with new relationships between the races. Efforts to revive agriculture and industry; the development of politics, education, religion, society, and culture from the postbellum period through the Depression and the New Deal. Prerequisite: HIST 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140626, 386829, 'HIST', '4090', 2020, 'East Central Europe Since 1400', 'This course will examine the social, political, economic, and cultural development of the lands traditionally known as Poland, Hungary, Bohemia, and Ukraine from the late Middle Ages to the present. This course will introduce the main forces and personalities that shaped Eastern European history in the past and continue to shape it today.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140627, 75809, 'MUSC', '4005', 2020, 'Special Problems: Theory and Composition (Formerly MUSC 402C)', 'Investigative study of special problems by students with particular needs in music. Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 99.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140628, 757504, 'HIST', '4077', 2020, 'The Middle Ages', 'The social, cultural, religious, political, and economic history of Europe from the end of the Roman Empire to the Renaissance. Particular attention is devoted to the Church, feudalism, manorialism, political institutions, and the rise of towns and capitalism. Prerequisite: HIST 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140629, 579666, 'HIST', '4075', 2020, 'Ancient Near East and Greece', 'Egypt, Sumer, Assyria, Babylonia and other civilization in the Ancient Near East from 3100 B.C.E.; Greece from the Mycenaean Period through Periclean Athens. Emphasis on archaeological evidence, political developments, cultural accomplishments. Prerequisite: HIST 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140630, 172214, 'HIST', '4076', 2020, 'Ancient Rome', 'Ancient Rome from Romulus through the early Empire, with an emphasis on the development of Roman traditions during the Republic and the transition from Republic to Empire under the Julio-Claudians. Roman government, class structure, and the significance of important historical figures will be emphasized. Prerequisite: HIST 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140631, 434855, 'CHEM', '4098', 2020, 'Research: Physical (Formerly CHEM 499E)', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 cr. Research problems that can be completed in one semester. Three to six hours laboratory per week per credit hour. Prerequisites: Junior or senior standing in chemistry and approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 499E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140632, 585197, 'HIST', '481', 2020, 'Europe, 1890-1945', 'This course surveys European history from the close of the 19th century to the end of World War II. The focus is primarily upon national and international politics, but with careful attention to economic, social and cultural developments in their relationship to political change. Prerequisite: HIST 112.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140633, 509970, 'CHEM', '422E', 2020, 'Directed Study: Physical', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A directed study for undergraduates and graduates. May include laboratory and/or library work. Four to six hours per week for each credit hour earned. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 422E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140634, 728139, 'HIST', '3031', 2020, 'French History', 'A survey of French political institutions, cultural developments, and social structure from 800 to the present. (Formerly HIST 487)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140635, 728139, 'HIST', '487', 2020, 'French History', 'A survey of French political institutions, cultural developments, and social structure from 800 to the present. (Formerly HIST 487)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140636, 361555, 'HIST', '4085', 2020, 'English Constitutional and Legal History', 'Emphasis on the unique legal and constitutional developments of the English system in Western Europe and their impact on American political thought. The class will consider the notion of limited government, the rule of law and the development of political party government from 1730 to 1979. The latter part of the class will concentrate on the decline of the Liberal Party, the rise of the Labor Party and the important legal reforms since World War II. Prerequisities: HIST 111, 112.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140637, 607384, 'HIST', '4060', 2020, 'The Old South', 'The political, economic, and social development of the ante-bellum South. Settlement patterns; sectional distinctiveness; political ideology; development of slavery and the plantation system; abolitionism and slavery defense; and the growth of southern nationalism. Prerequisite: HIST 2001. (Formerly 403.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140638, 825662, 'HIST', '469', 2020, 'American Constitutional and Legal History', 'The development of American constitutional and legal systems from the Colonial period to the present. An emphasis will be placed on the Constitutional Convention of 1787 and the intent of the Founding Fathers. Important court decisions will be reviewed up to the Reconstruction period. Later topics, such as civil rights, the imperial presidency and constitutional developments within this century, will also be considered. Prerequisites: HIST 201, 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140639, 186839, 'HIST', '4064', 2020, 'The American Frontier', 'The westward movement in America from 1607 to 1890, emphasizing the process of pioneering and the influence of the frontier on American institutions. (Formerly 315.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140640, 881842, 'HIST', '470', 2020, 'History of Biblical Lands', 'This course is an introduction to the material culture, cultural history and cultural process of the biblical world, with an emphasis on the connections between archaeology and the Bible. Prerequisites: History 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140641, 130528, 'HIST', '4072', 2020, 'Colonial Latin America', 'Discovery, exploration, and settlement; Spanish and Portuguese colonial systems; political, economic, and social development including the wars of independence. (Formerly 3021.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140642, 391502, 'HIST', '458', 2020, 'Recent America', 'The position of America in world affairs since 1914; the political and economic forces that led to the Depression; World War II and the changing concept of American democracy. Prerequisite: HIST 202. (Formerly 415.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140645, 738407, 'CINS', '4093', 2020, 'Seminar: Software (Formerly CINS 492A)', '1-3 credits per semester. May be repeated for a maximum of 6 credits. Seminar in information systems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly CINS 492A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140646, 523793, 'HIST', '452', 2020, 'The Age of Jefferson and Jackson', 'An investigation into the complex character of Jefferson, his political impact upon the Republic and the ambiguous legacy he left after 1826. Andrew Jackson will be considered as a symbol of a new democratic age. The new Jacksonian spirit will be reviewed in the light of social reform movements, 1815 to 1840. The course will also consider Native-American cultures and the changing attitudes towards slavery. Prerequisite: HIST 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140647, 429868, 'HIST', '4047', 2020, 'U S Military History 1865-Present', 'This course examines the development of the U.S. Military and the wars it fought from the end of the Civil War to the present.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140648, 323216, 'HIST', '4051', 2020, 'The Revolutionary Generation', 'The history of the American Revolution, placing it within the Trans-Atlantic community, its impact upon domestic society, and its influence upon the revolutionary generation of England, Ireland, and Europe generally. In considering political developments, attention will also focus upon the Revolutions impact upon women, Native Americans and the institution of slavery. The course will conclude with a review of the Articles of Confederation and the weaknesses of the early Federal Union. Prerequisite: HIST 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140649, 294340, 'HIST', '449', 2020, 'Native American History', 'This course offers an overview of Native American history from pre-Columbian times to the present. Topics include Native American culture, interaction with Europeans, and relations with the US government. Prerequisites: History 2001 or 2002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140650, 294340, 'HIST', '4049', 2020, 'Native American History', 'This course offers an overview of Native American history from pre-Columbian times to the present. Topics include Native American culture, interaction with Europeans, and relations with the US government. Prerequisites: History 2001 or 2002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140651, 429868, 'HIST', '447', 2020, 'U S Military History 1865-Present', 'This course examines the development of the U.S. Military and the wars it fought from the end of the Civil War to the present.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140652, 859882, 'HIST', '4030', 2020, 'World War II', 'An examination of the causes, conduct, and immediate aftermath of World War II giving attention to major military campaigns and experiences of war as seen by military leaders and combatants in Asia, Europe, and the Pacific. Prerequisite: HIST 1012 or 2002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140653, 484272, 'MUSC', '4004', 2020, 'Special Problems: History and Literature (Formerly MUSC 402B)', 'Investigative study of special problems by students with particular needs in music. Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated. (Formerly MUSC 402B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 99.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140654, 75809, 'MUSC', '402C', 2020, 'Special Problems: Theory and Composition (Formerly MUSC 402C)', 'Investigative study of special problems by students with particular needs in music. Prerequisite: Approval of the Head of the Division of Music. May be repeated.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 99.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140655, 176297, 'HIST', '456', 2020, 'The Gilded Age', 'Economic, political, and social changes during the rise of industrial America between Reconstruction and the coming of World War I. Prerequisite: HIST 202. (Formerly 438.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140657, 559555, 'ENGL', '4052', 2020, 'Directed Study: Creative Writing (Formerly ENGL 450B)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Advanced standing and approval of department head. (Formerly ENGL 450B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140658, 38693, 'GERO', '456E', 2020, 'International Studies: Middle East (Formerly GERO 456E)', 'Extended gerontology field study outside the United States with guest lectures, visits to gerontological related facilities and programs, and assigned readings related to aging in the designated study region. (Formerly GERO 456E)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140659, 419096, 'GERO', '457C', 2020, 'Regional United States Field Studies: East (Formerly GERO 457C)', 'Extended gerontology field study within the United States with guest lectures, visits to gerontological facilities and programs, and assigned readings related to aging in the designated study region. May not be repeated for credit. (Formerly GERO 457C)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140660, 300307, 'HONR', '1001', 2020, 'Honors Colloquium', 'A scheduled gathering to discuss topics relevant to a semester theme. May be repeated for a total of 7 credits. Grades of CR (credit) or NC (no credit) will be assigned. Prerequisites: Admission to the Honors Program or permission of the Honors Council. (Formerly HONR 101H)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 7.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140661, 300307, 'HONR', '101H', 2020, 'Honors Colloquium', 'A scheduled gathering to discuss topics relevant to a semester theme. May be repeated for a total of 7 credits. Grades of CR (credit) or NC (no credit) will be assigned. Prerequisites: Admission to the Honors Program or permission of the Honors Council. (Formerly HONR 101H)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 7.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140662, 720351, 'HIST', '3009', 2020, 'Islam', 'Survey of Islamic history from the inception in 7th century Arabia to the present day. Special emphasis on the religious principles and the institutions of the civilizations to which it gave rise. Attention is given to those factors that continue to make Islam an important force in the world today. (Same as RELG 3009.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140663, 580551, 'HIST', '439', 2020, 'The South, World War II to the Present', 'World War II proved to be a significant watershed in the South. Emphasis will be placed on its industrialization, agricultural mechanization, and, especially the Second Reconstruction in Civil Rights, as well as its political, economic, religious, social, and cultural development. The South as a section will be placed in its proper perspective within the national experience. Prerequisite: HIST 202.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140664, 273299, 'HIST', '3010', 2020, 'African-American History', 'Black American history beginning with early West African civilization to the present. Attention will be devoted to immigration, the slave system, civil rights, and modern black movements with emphasis on significant African-American leaders. May not be substituted to meet History requirements in 1011-1012, 2001-2002, or 3005. (Formerly 105.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140665, 879153, 'GERO', '4011', 2020, 'Social Work Practice With the Elderly', 'An introduction to the social, economic, and psychological dimensions of aging using a person-in-environment approach. (Same as SOCW 4011.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140666, 879153, 'GERO', '411', 2020, 'Social Work Practice With the Elderly', 'An introduction to the social, economic, and psychological dimensions of aging using a person-in-environment approach. (Same as SOCW 4011.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140667, 247991, 'GERO', '4031', 2020, 'Elder Law', 'An examination of legal challenges older Americans are facing as they plan their later years and seek to maximize their quality of life. These challenges include age discrimination in employment, housing alternatives and options, financial management and planning, medical needs and attention, and consent, and long-term care.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140668, 773056, 'GERO', '4025', 2020, 'Seminar in Death and Dying', 'Exploration of the social organization of dying, including a view on cross-cultural perspectives on death, treatment of the dying patient, and the grief process. (Same as GERO 4025)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140669, 238405, 'GRMN', '2009', 2020, 'Advanced German', 'Introduction to finer points of German language, development of writing skills in German, grammatical and stylistic analysis of literary texts. Prerequisite: 202 or 205.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140670, 801931, 'GERO', '1001', 2020, 'Basic Activity', 'An introduction to the profession of Activity Directors, Therapeutic activity practice, and their integration into health care. An examination of practice standards, practitioner behavior, activity planning, and service delivery.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140671, 608315, 'GEOS', '4050', 2020, 'Remote Sensing of the Environment', 'This course will cover the basics and the interpretation of remote sensing data that will include aerial photography, U. S. and French satellite imagery, thermal infrared, Sideways Looking Radar, Synthetic Aperture Radar, and other airborne platforms such as the Daedalus Multispectral Scanner used by NASA.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140672, 493041, 'H&HP', '1002', 2020, 'Aerobic Fitness', 'Fitness activities that improve cardiorespiratory endurance, flexibility, body composition, muscular strength and endurance.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140673, 559674, 'GEOG', '2003', 2020, 'Louisiana', 'A survey of the natural landscape; land forms, climate, soils, drainage, and the geographic factors; agriculture, transportation, and population.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140674, 58436, 'FRNH', '3015', 2020, 'Foreign Language Practicum', 'Application of language skills in a foreign-language environment. Student will be involved in a total immersion living situation and will receive a minimum of fourteen clock hours per week in formal language instruction. Prerequisite: French 2002, 2005 or equivalent.', 3.0000, 12.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140675, 36178, 'FRNH', '4075', 2020, 'Language, Culture and the Classroom', 'The application of second language acquisition theory in the elementary or secondary classroom. (Same as Spanish 4075). Prerequisite: French 4074.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140676, 435600, 'FRNH', '2031', 2020, 'Grammar and Composition', 'Elements of French grammar and syntax with drill in style, idioms, and verb forms. Prerequisite: 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140677, 435600, 'FRNH', '231', 2020, 'Grammar and Composition', 'Elements of French grammar and syntax with drill in style, idioms, and verb forms. Prerequisite: 2002 or 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140679, 374124, 'FINA', '4005', 2020, 'Case Problems in Financial Management', 'Case studies of financial topics; emphasis on sources and uses of funds, cost of funds, return on investments; analysis of financial statements. Prerequisite: 3016. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140680, 374124, 'FINA', '405', 2020, 'Case Problems in Financial Management', 'Case studies of financial topics; emphasis on sources and uses of funds, cost of funds, return on investments; analysis of financial statements. Prerequisite: 3016. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140682, 873390, 'FCSC', '4031', 2020, 'Parenting: Fathers, Mothers, and Children', 'Practical knowledge of parenting roles. Interrelationships of fathers, mothers, and children. Current issues in parenting, including bonding, discipline, child care, family crises, support systems and non- traditional parent situations. Parents and children in historical and contemporary perspectives.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140683, 475385, 'FCSC', '4004', 2020, 'Research in Family and Consumer Sciences', 'A review of current research and public policy in the field of Family and Consumer Sciences. Prerequisite: Senior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140684, 573256, 'FCSC', '4007', 2020, 'Presentation Techniques', 'Principles and techniques of presentations. Four hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140685, 619772, 'FCSC', '4009', 2020, 'Visual Merchandising', 'Preparation of window and store displays, fashion shows, and store promotions.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140686, 330615, 'FCSC', '4035', 2020, 'Housing the Elderly', 'Examination and application of the guidelines, issues and choices associated with housing disruption and re-location of the elderly. (Same as GERO 4035.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140687, 193617, 'FCSC', '4030', 2020, 'Current Trends in the Industry', 'Study of current trends of the industry. Review of the journals and other publications used in the industry. Prerequisite: Senior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140688, 987267, 'FINA', '4001', 2020, 'Investments', 'The principles of investments in stocks and bonds and their application to specific classes of investments. Sources of financial information; interpreting financial news; protection in purchasing of securities, taxation of securities. Prerequisite: 3015. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140689, 987267, 'FINA', '401', 2020, 'Investments', 'The principles of investments in stocks and bonds and their application to specific classes of investments. Sources of financial information; interpreting financial news; protection in purchasing of securities, taxation of securities. Prerequisite: 3015. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140690, 548296, 'FCSC', '4033', 2020, 'Fashion Merchandising Practicum', 'An in-depth experience planned and supervised to meet individual needs of students. Includes work experience and/or field study. Prerequisites: Senior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140691, 368837, 'FCSC', '4032', 2020, 'Fashion Merchandising Pre-Practicum', 'A survey of the job market with emphasis on researching a company, writing a resume, and interviewing skills. Class research project includes developing a questionnaire, collecting and analyzing data. Prerequisites: Senior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140692, 640749, 'FCSC', '4012', 2020, 'Advanced Nutrition', 'Problems in human nutrition. Investigation of recent developments in the field of nutrition.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140693, 950064, 'FCSC', '2019', 2020, 'Practicum in Day Care Administration', 'Program development, evaluations and participation in day care centers. Nine hours laboratory for Day Care Management majors. Prerequisite: FCSC 3001, 3005, and FCSC major.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140694, 260157, 'FCSC', '400', 2020, 'Preschool Methods', 'Planning and preparation of units and lessons for the preschool. Prerequisites: Senior standing, 3011, 3012.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140695, 626626, 'FCSC', '3037', 2020, 'Commercial Studio', 'Design of commercial interiors including practice of the process of cost estimating, client presentation; selection of furnishings, office systems and materials. Six hours studio. Prerequisites: 2006, 2011, 2021.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140696, 497335, 'FCSC', '3017', 2020, 'Consumer Education', 'Explanation of family consumer decisions in relation to alternatives in attainment of family goals.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140697, 489470, 'FCSC', '3029', 2020, 'Fashion Merchandising', 'A study of the fashion process from concept to manufacturing, distribution, and retailing. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140698, 704390, 'FCSC', '3030', 2020, 'Fashion Merchandising', 'The processes involved in apparel buying for different types of fashion retailers with emphasis on merchandising and controlling. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140699, 886573, 'FCSC', '355', 2020, 'Computer-Aided Design', 'Two dimensional drafting and design. One hour of lecture; four hours studio. (Same as FCSC 3055.) Prerequisite: Junior standing. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140700, 793904, 'FCSC', '3013', 2020, 'Methods', 'Modern methods of teaching family and consumer sciences in secondary schools. Prerequisites: Educational Foundations 2001, PSYC 2005, 3001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140701, 289211, 'FCSC', '312', 2020, 'Preschool Child Laboratory', 'Required laboratory to accompany FCSC 3011. Three hours laboratory.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140702, 987979, 'FCSC', '2021', 2020, 'Textiles', 'A study of fibers and fabrics, their properties, identification, uses, and care.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140703, 862623, 'FCSC', '3001', 2020, 'Literacy and Language in Early Childhood', 'This course introduces theory, research, and techniques in Language and Literacy, and teaches students how to apply them in early childhood classrooms. Prerequisites: FCSC 2015, 2020.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140704, 237241, 'FCSC', '2015', 2020, 'Program Planning', 'Techniques of organizing activities for day care centers. Emphasis on creative arts, music, literature, and science. Prerequisite: 212. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140705, 786771, 'FCSC', '2000', 2020, 'Clothing Construction', 'The construction of simple garments with the use of commercial patterns.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140706, 700777, 'FCSC', '2002', 2020, 'Clothing C