ation of classroom art. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140817, 884749, 'CURR', '3013', 2020, 'Materials and Methods in Speech', 'Materials, techniques and methods of teaching speech. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140818, 221833, 'CJUS', '230', 2020, 'The Police', 'An in-depth examination of the law enforcement sub-system of the criminal justice system. Includes historical precedents to American systems, the diversity of agencies and their roles, the internal components of agencies, and their interrelationships with other system components and other social and legal agents and agencies. Prerequisite: 1001 or approval of the program director.<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCRJ 2313', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140819, 758439, 'CJUS', '3008', 2020, 'Substance Abuse', 'Analysis of the social, physical, and psychological impact of substance abuse. Examination of types, incidence, and forms of abuse and an analysis of social and legal reactions. Social trends and laws are examined to provide the student with foundations for a critical and analytical examination of substance abuse. Prerequisite: 1001 or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140820, 10075, 'CONS', '4018', 2020, 'Foundation Problems Laboratory', 'Laboratory course to accompany 4017. Three hours laboratory. Sp, F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140821, 10075, 'CONS', '418', 2020, 'Foundation Problems Laboratory', 'Laboratory course to accompany 4017. Three hours laboratory. Sp, F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140822, 463924, 'CONS', '4019', 2020, 'Construction Documents and Regulatory Agencies', 'Current building codes and significant aspects of construction specifications. Prerequisite: Senior standing or approval of director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140823, 980553, 'CHEM', '304', 2020, 'Organic Chemistry II', 'Spectroscopic techniques and the chemistry of aromatic compounds, carbonyl compounds, and amines will be covered. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 230. (Formerly 304)<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 2223', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140824, 175068, 'CSCI', '4063', 2020, 'Theory of Programming Languages', 'A formal treatment of programming language design and translation concepts. Programming language syntax and semantics. Finite and pushdown automata, scanners, symbol tables, parsers, machine-independent code generation. Prerequisite: CSCI 3013.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140825, 774330, 'CSCI', '4091', 2020, 'Computer Science Capstone', 'Culmination of course work experiences with a full software life cycle project development. Focus on product planning, management, and delivery including testing and quality assurance. Generation of artifacts, including detailed specifications, design documents, and user manual. Prerequisites: CSCI 3005, 3020, 4055, and 4060.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140826, 242678, 'CURR', '4014', 2020, 'Curriculum Design and Evaluation', 'Theory and practices of curriculum design and evaluation; social and psychological factors related to the adoption and acceptance of new programs in public schools.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140827, 39644, 'COUN', '4080', 2020, 'Effective Parenting', 'Designed to help students and parents-to-be understand the principles and techniques of establishing effective parent-child relationships.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140828, 755417, 'COUN', '4034', 2020, 'Career Development in the Elementary Schools', 'Methods and systems of introducing the world of work to elementary school children.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140829, 12803, 'CONS', '4028', 2020, 'Value Management', 'Utilization of the constructors special knowledge to cut the cost of a construction project to the lowest practicable level without compromising its function or sacrificing quality and aesthetics. Prerequisite: Approval of director and junior standing. (Formerly 411.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140830, 894009, 'CONS', '4010', 2020, 'Analytic and Conceptual Estimating', 'Separation of conceptual planning into its constituent elements and essential features. Feasibility of a construction project by analysis of income, construction investment, operating cost and risk. Prerequisite: Approval of director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140831, 992675, 'CONS', '407', 2020, 'Project Control Systems', 'Analysis and application of scheduling techniques. The use of critical path method (CPM) and program evaluation and review (PERT). Prerequisites: 3003, 3004. F, Sp', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140832, 992675, 'CONS', '4007', 2020, 'Project Control Systems', 'Analysis and application of scheduling techniques. The use of critical path method (CPM) and program evaluation and review (PERT). Prerequisites: 3003, 3004. F, Sp', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140833, 8100, 'CONS', '3028', 2020, 'Capital Projects', 'Theory of control and management by owner corporations of cost, time, and value of construction for capital ventures. Techniques for control of projects, with emphasis on general principles and relationships. Prerequisites: Approval of director. (Formerly 311.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140834, 47119, 'CONS', '3055', 2020, 'Computer-Aided Design', 'Two dimensional drafting and design. One hour of lecture; four hours studio. (Same as FCSC 3055.) Prerequisite: Junior standing. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140835, 160973, 'CONS', '3024', 2020, 'Environmental Construction', 'An introduction to pollutants, hazardous and toxic substances encountered on the job site. Emphasis on biological hazards, health safety standards in regard to handling and disposal of products and liability management. Prerequisite: Junior standing. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140836, 431305, 'CONS', '3022', 2020, 'Pipeline Construction', 'An introduction to pipeline construction including basic design considerations, standards and regulations, estimating and bidding, acquisition of Right-of-Way, construction equipment and procedures, safety, and pipeline maintenance. Prerequisite: Approval of director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140837, 651461, 'CONS', '3009', 2020, 'Concrete Structures and Form Design Laboratory', 'Laboratory course to accompany 3008. Three hours laboratory. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140838, 651461, 'CONS', '309', 2020, 'Concrete Structures and Form Design Laboratory', 'Laboratory course to accompany 3008. Three hours laboratory. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140839, 678289, 'CONS', '3008', 2020, 'Concrete Structures and Form Design', 'Theory and principles of design and building of concrete structures and forms in conformance with current codes and practices. Prerequisites: 2006, 2007. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140840, 752870, 'CONS', '3003', 2020, 'Construction Techniques', 'Continuation of 2003 and 2004 as applied to larger construction projects. Prerequisites: 2003, 2004, 2008, 2009. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140841, 95749, 'CONS', '2060', 2020, 'Mechanical and Electrical Systems', 'A survey of systems for water supply and sanitation, heating and air conditioning, and electric service and installations.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140842, 753094, 'CONS', '3006', 2020, 'Steel Structures Laboratory', 'Laboratory course to accompany 3005.Three hours laboratory. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140843, 753094, 'CONS', '306', 2020, 'Steel Structures Laboratory', 'Laboratory course to accompany 3005.Three hours laboratory. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140844, 64750, 'CONS', '2025', 2020, 'Damaged Building Inspections', 'Inspection of damaged buildings and reporting needs for repair or demolition.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140845, 224701, 'CONS', '2024', 2020, 'Commercial and Industrial Inspections', 'Inspection of buildings under construction, alteration or repair for compliance with building laws.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140846, 962091, 'CONS', '2022', 2020, 'Plan and Specification Reviews', 'Under direct supervision, the student trainee examines plans and specifications of buildings for conformity with zoning regulations and building laws.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140847, 276888, 'CONS', '2023', 2020, 'Residential Inspections', 'Inspection of fences, patios, carports, residential blockwalls, etc.; conducting occupancy surveys in various structures such as apartments and hotels.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140848, 169801, 'CONS', '2021', 2020, 'Local and State Building Codes', 'Under direct supervision, the student trainee develops effective public contacts with builders and contractors in conducting routine work within a building department office.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140849, 607347, 'CONS', '2014', 2020, 'Interior Systems', 'A study of interior environmental systems including construction techniques, material handling, storage and transporation. Materials and systems influence of interior design as they pertain to acoustics, sound transmission, fire hazards, lighting, and energy.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140850, 468455, 'CONS', '2020', 2020, 'Construction Inspection', 'Introduction to principles and practices of inspecting construction projects-in-progress with emphasis on the nature of construction problems encountered on the job site.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140851, 521536, 'CONS', '1002', 2020, 'Basic Graphics', 'Introductory course in architectural drafting. Use and care of instruments and equipment, line weights, lettering, simple plans, sections and details. Three hours of studio. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140852, 984575, 'CONS', '1012', 2020, 'Architectural Drafting', 'Introduction to plan reading with instructions given in basic architectural graphics; details of working drawings and shop drawings related to building construction. F, Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140853, 673902, 'CSCI', '442', 2020, 'Simulation and Modeling', 'General principles of stochastic simulation. Model development, analysis, and validation. Comparison of alternative models. Use of special purpose simulation languages. Prerequisites: CSCI 3005 and MATH 3003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140854, 911003, 'CSCI', '4083', 2020, 'Artificial Intelligence', 'Study of the computer in context with human thought processes. Heuristic programming; search strategies; knowledge representation; perception; learning; natural language understanding; user interfaces; intelligent systems. Prerequisites: 3005 and 3010.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140855, 911003, 'CSCI', '483', 2020, 'Artificial Intelligence', 'Study of the computer in context with human thought processes. Heuristic programming; search strategies; knowledge representation; perception; learning; natural language understanding; user interfaces; intelligent systems. Prerequisites: 3005 and 3010.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140856, 733977, 'CSCI', '4081', 2020, 'Expert Systems', 'A course in Applied Artificial Intelligence for non-programmers who are interested in the use and development of expert systems within their own fields of study. Not applicable toward a degree in computer science. Prerequisite: Senior or graduate standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140857, 779844, 'CSCI', '4075', 2020, 'Knowledge Discovery in Databases', 'An introduction to the field of Knowledge Discovery in Databases, KDD. Topics to be included are: data selection, cleaning, coding, pattern recognition, the discovery of hidden knowledge, learning rules, and data mining algorithms for large databases. Prerequisites: CSCI 4055 and MATH 3003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140858, 81454, 'CSCI', '4035', 2020, 'Linear Programming', 'Development of the simplex algorithm, revised simplex, duality, and application. Prerequisite: MATH 2002. 4036. INTRODUCTION TO MATHEMATICAL CONCEPTS IN OPERATIONS RESEARCH. 3 cr. A mathematical approach to concepts in advanced linear and nonlinear programming, dynamic programming, game theories, queueing theory and other standard topics in operations research. Prerequisites: CSCI 4035 and MATH 3003. (Same as MATH 4036.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140859, 683654, 'KINS', '4034', 2020, 'Kinesiology Professional Development Seminar', 'This course is designed as a pre-internship experience that will provide undergraduate kinesiology students with the key training needed to engage in the professional activities that are central to a successful career in kinesiology-related fields. Although issues of substantive, exercise, fitness, sport, and/or wellness importance naturally will be addressed, the primary focus will be on the strategies and skills that are needed to translate one&#39;s substantive knowledge into a successful career -- one that advances both the individual&#39;s goals and the general community goals of improved health, decreased disease, and the reduction of health disparity. As this description indicates, this course is most appropriate for undergraduate students who will be pursuing careers that emphasize their preparation in kinesiology-related fields. Prerequisite: Junior standing and KINS 2011. KINS majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140860, 308667, 'ACCT', '310', 2020, 'Intermediate Financial Accounting I', 'First in a two-course sequence intended to study the theory and application of financial reporting for business entities. Prerequisites: minimum grades of &quot;B&quot; in 2012 and 2013 and junior standing. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140861, 809661, 'MUSC', '4092', 2020, 'Historical Survey II', 'The second of a two-course sequence covering the major eras of Western music. Topics include discussion of major composers, styles, and genres from approximately 1750 until the present, as well as the influence of other cultures on Western music. Composers and their works are situated within a larger cultural and historical context. Emphasis is placed on aural identification and written analysis of representative works from a variety of\r\ntime periods. A research paper and accompanying assignments form a significant\r\nportion of the course grade. Students will be introduced to electronic resources for music research. For music majors, open to others by approval of the Head of the Division of Music. Prerequisite: MUSC 1093. Offered in Spring Semester. Required course for all B.M. and B.M.E. majors, regardless of concentration.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140862, 286030, 'CSCI', '436', 2020, 'Intro Mathematical Concepts in Operations Research', 'A mathematical approach to concepts in advanced linear and nonlinear programming, dynamic programming, game theories, queueing theory and other standard topics in operations research. Prerequisites: CSCI 4035 and MATH 3003. (Same as MATH 4036.)', 0.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140863, 286030, 'CSCI', '4036', 2020, 'Intro Mathematical Concepts in Operations Research', 'A mathematical approach to concepts in advanced linear and nonlinear programming, dynamic programming, game theories, queueing theory and other standard topics in operations research. Prerequisites: CSCI 4035 and MATH 3003. (Same as MATH 4036.)', 0.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140864, 808433, 'CSCI', '3098', 2020, 'Computer Projects', 'Involvement in practical computer projects. Prerequisite: Permission of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140865, 90359, 'CSCI', '3069', 2020, 'Introduction to Programming', 'This course will emphasize programming techniques in a modern programming language, currently Pascal, using microcomputers. Program design, coding, debugging, and testing of programs for a wide variety of problems commonly solved by computers. Not applicable toward a degree in computer science. Prerequisite: CSCI 1070.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140866, 90359, 'CSCI', '369', 2020, 'Introduction to Programming', 'This course will emphasize programming techniques in a modern programming language, currently Pascal, using microcomputers. Program design, coding, debugging, and testing of programs for a wide variety of problems commonly solved by computers. Not applicable toward a degree in computer science. Prerequisite: CSCI 1070.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140867, 571773, 'CSCI', '3050', 2020, 'Research Methods for Computer Science', 'An introduction to methods used in computer science research. Topics include techniques and conventions in research methods, evaluation approaches, and presentation of results. Prerequisite: CSCI 2026.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140868, 97476, 'CSCI', '3067', 2020, 'Advanced Software Applications', 'A study of advanced applications and their use in producing professional level presentations. Students will utilize problems from their major field of study, occupation, and/or other areas of interest. The word processor, spreadsheet, and other tools will be used to integrate the study into a desktop publication. Not applicable toward a degree in computer science. Prerequisites: CSCI 1070.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140869, 660340, 'CINS', '2020', 2020, 'Introduction to Business Programming', 'Fundamentals of problem solving, programming logic, and algorithm specification using various modeling tools; coding of algorithms in a programming language. Prerequisites: CSCI 1070, MATH 1016 and completion of all developmental requirements, or permission of instructor. (Formerly CINS 201) F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140870, 16557, 'CINS', '3041', 2020, 'Advanced Networking', 'Planning, building, and administering local area networks. Emphasis placed on installation, management, and maintenance of client/server networks. Coverage of TCP/IP, remote access, and other popular services. Prerequisite: CINS 3040. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140871, 25908, 'CSCI', '203', 2020, 'Intermediate Programming', 'Continuation of CSCI 2000, with increased emphasis on program design (including structured and object oriented techniques). Topics include class design and implementation, inheritance, and event-driven-programming. Prerequisites: Grade of \"C\" or better in CSCI 2000; and credit in MATH 1011 or 1013 or permission of the department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140873, 741692, 'CSCI', '1080', 2020, 'Foundations of Computer Science', 'An introduction to the foundations of computer science and problem solving using a modern, high-level programming language. Not applicable toward a degree in Computer Science.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140874, 335351, 'CSCI', '2064', 2020, 'Introduction to Computer Organization', 'Basic logic design, coding, number representation and arithmetic binary representation, and computer architecture. Prerequisite: CSCI 2026, 2053, and credit or registration in CSCI 2065.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140875, 747298, 'CSCI', '2065', 2020, 'Computer Organization Laboratory', 'Laboratory class to accompany 2064. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 2064.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140876, 747298, 'CSCI', '265', 2020, 'Computer Organization Laboratory', 'Laboratory class to accompany 2064. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 2064.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140877, 703265, 'CSCI', '3005', 2020, 'Analysis of Algorithms', 'The design and analysis of computer algorithms and data structures. Classes of algorithms studied include sorting, searching, graph, parallel and NP- complete. An in-depth study into both efficiency and design. Correctness and formal verification of algorithms. Prerequisites: CSCI 3026 and grade of &quot;C&quot; or better in 2073.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140879, 354745, 'CSCI', '377', 2020, 'Internet for the User', 'Introduction to the Internet from the user&#39;s perspective. Topics covered will include the history and operation of the Internet, Internet research strategies, and basic web-page design and construction. Not applicable toward a degree in computer science. Prerequisites: CSCI 1070 or departmental approval.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140880, 712461, 'MLSC', '3023', 2020, 'Serology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 3022 to include representative tests of all types of serological testing performed in the clinical laboratory. Three hour laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. (Formerly CLSC 323)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140881, 256146, 'CODI', '1052', 2020, 'Speech and Language Acquisition', 'The development of speech in children in the family and the effects of culture on language.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140882, 325076, 'CODI', '2020', 2020, 'Beginning Sign Language', 'An introductory course in the study of American Sign Language (ASL) and Pidgin Sign English (PSE) with an emphasis on the Deaf Community and their culture. An understanding of some of the basic cultural differences of the Deaf and how they relate to the development and existence of sign languages will be coupled with basic skills in both ASL and PSE. Non-majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140883, 309543, 'SPLP', '4001', 2020, 'Phonetics', 'Correct sound pronunciation; phonetic transcription rules through application of the International Phonetic Alphabet to General American English and other varieties. (Prereq: SPLP 1013, 1052, 2001, 2002)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140884, 309543, 'SPLP', '401', 2020, 'Phonetics', 'Correct sound pronunciation; phonetic transcription rules through application of the International Phonetic Alphabet to General American English and other varieties. (Prereq: SPLP 1013, 1052, 2001, 2002)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140885, 966823, 'CODI', '4017', 2020, 'Phonetics', 'Correct sound formation and pronunciation; learning of transcription rules for American phonetics and other sound classification systems. Enrollment in 418 is required.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140886, 813788, 'CODI', '4018', 2020, 'Phonetics Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 417. Two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 417, or approval of instructor.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140887, 449577, 'SPLP', '4031', 2020, 'Stuttering', 'Review of modern theories and therapies of stuttering, nature, causes, diagnosis, and treatment of stuttering.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140888, 979033, 'CODI', '4036', 2020, 'Manual Communication', 'An introductory course in manual communication of the hearing impaired. Emphasis on drills and exercises to help students acquire a sign vocabulary fluency.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140889, 268561, 'CODI', '1051', 2020, 'General Foundation in Audiology', 'The nature of deafness and hard of hearing problems of children.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140890, 706294, 'CINS', '1001', 2020, 'Microcomputer Operations', 'An introduction to information systems. Topics include hardware, operating systems, and application programs with hands-on experience. Not open to College of Business juniors and seniors. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140891, 377791, 'CHEM', '4031', 2020, 'Intermediate Organic Chemistry', 'Laboratory introduction of standard research techniques; lecture covering synthetic design, functional group transformations, advanced nomenclature, and mechanistic analysis of reactions. One hour lecture and three hours laboratory. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 2032 and CHEM 2033. F (Formerly 405)', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140892, 78448, 'MLSC', '4033', 2020, 'Microbiology III-Practicum', 'Continuation of MLSC 4032. Advanced concepts in the use and interpretation of medical bacteriology, mycology, virology, and parasitology procedures and data. Practical application of clinical bateriology, mycology, virology, and parasitology knowledge and skills in a clinical laboratory setting. MLSC majors only. F, Sp (Formerly CLSC 433)', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140893, 524697, 'CLSC', '322', 2020, 'Immunology', 'A course covering the principles of basic immunology and the application of clinical immunology in the medical laboratory to include: immunoglobulin structures; antigen- antibody reactions, classification, mechanisms, and clinical characteristics of immune disease; transplantation and tumor immunology; and a study of various serological testing procedures and interpretation and correlation of test results with disease states. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 322)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140894, 964940, 'CLSC', '1004', 2020, 'Urinalysis Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 103, involving qualitative and quantitative studies, both chemical and microscopic, of urine. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140895, 369145, 'CHEM', '1005', 2020, 'Chemistry in Society', 'Fundamental concepts of chemistry with an emphasis on its impact on society, industry and the environment. Three hours of lecture per week. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 101. For non- majors. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140896, 97009, 'CHEM', '1006', 2020, 'Chemistry in Society Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany CHEM 105. Three hours of laboratory per week. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 103 and registration or credit in CHEM 105. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140897, 160789, 'CHEM', '306', 2020, 'Organic Chemistry Laboratory II', 'Laboratory to accompany Organic Chemistry II. Application of techniques from Organic Chemistry I to organic reactions. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 2031 and credit or registration in CHEM 2032. F, Sp, Su2 (Formerly 306)<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 2221', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140898, 278608, 'CHEM', '3010', 2020, 'Descriptive Inorganic Chemistry', 'Discussion of elemental properties, elemental combinations into ionic and molecular compounds, and periodic trends. Laboratory synthesis and characterization of inorganic compounds. Three hours lecture; three hours laboratory. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 1008. Sp (Formerly 313/314).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140899, 706038, 'CHEM', '400', 2020, 'Chemistry Capstone', 'A course designed as a culminating experience in the chemistry curriculum incorporating aspects of research methods, literature review, oral presentation, and written reports. Prerequisites: Two hours of CHEM 4099 and junior or senior standing in chemistry. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140900, 329875, 'CHEM', '3037', 2020, 'Biochemistry II', 'Thermodynamics, metabolism, photosynthesis, protein and nucleic acid biosynthesis. Three hours lecture. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 3050. Sp (Formerly 337)\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 4413', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `courses` VALUES (140901, 344414, 'CHEM', '3003', 2020, 'Organic Chemistry I', 'Discussion of structure and bonding theory, acid-base chemistry, reactions of alkanes, alkenes, alkynes, alcohols and alkyl halides. Three hours lecture. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 1008. F, S, Su1 (Formerly 303)<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 2213', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140902, 974979, 'ENGL', '201', 2020, 'British Literature I', 'Texts through the eighteenth century. Content varies.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CENL 2103', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140903, 997924, 'CHEM', '4030', 2020, 'Advanced Organic Chemistry', 'A mechanistic study of prevailing organic reactions via structural and electronic effects. Three hours of lecture per week. Prerequisite: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 2032 and CHEM 3022. Sp, odd', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140904, 278320, 'CHEM', '1000', 2020, 'The World of Chemistry', 'Chemical principles, facts and theories, revealed through practical applications, computer graphic illustrations and experiments. Chemistrys historical foundations, recent developments, and future directions. Prerequisites: Eligibility for MATH 111 or a more advanced mathematics course. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140905, 163762, 'BIOL', '4096', 2020, 'Cooperative Internships', 'Closely supervised practical experience working in agencies/businesses that employ biologists. Only junior and senior majors and graduate students are eligible. Students will receive grades of CR (credit) or NC (no credit). Students may repeat this course for a total of 3 credits; not to exceed 6 credits total in combination with 403. The course may not be used by graduate students to fulfill major requirements.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140906, 479623, 'BIOL', '484', 2020, 'Ornithology', 'Morphology, taxonomy, behavior, and natural history of birds. Two hours lecture and three hours laboratory with field trips required. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 1022, 1023.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140907, 630465, 'ART', '4049', 2020, 'Special Problems: Printing (Formerly ART 441F)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441F)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140908, 630465, 'ART', '441F', 2020, 'Special Problems: Printing (Formerly ART 441F)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441F)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140909, 629986, 'BIOL', '488', 2020, 'Game Mammals and Fur Bearers', 'Recognition, life histories, predators, economics and management practices of game mammals and fur bearers with special emphasis on regional fauna. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory with field trips. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in an introductory course in Biology and permission of the instructor.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140910, 122887, 'BIOL', '486', 2020, 'Game Birds', 'Recognition, life histories, predators, economics and management practices of North American game birds. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory with field trips. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in an introductory course in Biology and permission of the instructor.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140911, 844383, 'BIOL', '466', 2020, 'Advanced Microbiology', 'Advanced microbiological techniques; a study of the morphological, physiological, and genetic characteristics of important groups of microorganisms; introduction to biotechnology. Two hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 2014, 2015; 8 semester hours of chemistry.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140912, 598664, 'BIOL', '476', 2020, 'Freshwater Ecology', 'The biological, chemical, and physical characteristics of freshwater habitats. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory. Field trip fee required. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 1022, 1023.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140913, 598664, 'BIOL', '4076', 2020, 'Freshwater Ecology', 'The biological, chemical, and physical characteristics of freshwater habitats. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory. Field trip fee required. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 1022, 1023.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140914, 637705, 'BIOL', '480', 2020, 'Herpetology', 'Morphology, taxonomy, and life history of amphibians and reptiles with emphasis on the taxonomy of the amphibians and reptiles of Louisiana. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory with field trips required. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 1022, 1023.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140915, 799599, 'BIOL', '442', 2020, 'Agrostology', 'The identification, classification and ecology of grass and grass-like plants. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory with scheduled field trips. Prerequisite: 204. (Formerly Botany 419, 420.)', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140916, 306788, 'BIOL', '446', 2020, 'Economic Botany', 'The study of applied uses of plants as food, fibers, lumber, drugs, and related commodities. Prerequisite: 204. (Formerly Botany 481.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140917, 306788, 'BOTN', '481', 2020, 'Economic Botany', 'The study of applied uses of plants as food, fibers, lumber, drugs, and related commodities. Prerequisite: 204. (Formerly Botany 481.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140918, 649052, 'ZOOL', '435', 2020, 'Estuarine Zoology', 'An introduction to basic estuarine ecology with a focus on the ecology and systematics of major aquatic invertebrates and fishes native to estuaries of the northern Gulf of Mexico. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory. Field trip fee required. Prerequisite: 122, 123. (Formerly Zoology 435.) Sp, odd', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140919, 39162, 'BIOL', '470', 2020, 'Immunology-Concepts and Principles', 'Detailed discussion of the cellular and humoral components of the immune system and their interrelationships in the production and control, at both the genetic and cellular levels, of immune responses. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 2014 or 1015 or 3012; or permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140920, 890967, 'BIOL', '464', 2020, 'Water Management', 'A survey of water distribution and uses, including water purification and sewage treatment, industrial and agricultural, irrigation scheduling.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140921, 553147, 'BIOL', '4069', 2020, 'General VIrology Laboratory', 'A laboratory to accompany 4068. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit with \"C\" or better or registration in 4068.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140922, 442474, 'BIOL', '438', 2020, 'Biology of Nonseed Plants', 'The characteristics, classification, phylogeny, and life cycles of fungi, algae, mosses, hornworts, liverworts, and ferns are emphasized. Two hours lecture and four hours laboratory including frequent field trips. Prerequisite: 122, 123. (Formerly Botany 415, 416.)', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140923, 890967, 'BIOL', '4064', 2020, 'Water Management', 'A survey of water distribution and uses, including water purification and sewage treatment, industrial and agricultural, irrigation scheduling.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140924, 795080, 'MICR', '423', 2020, 'Food and Dairy Microbiology', 'The role of microorganisms in the preservation, spoilage and poisoning in food and dairy products. Also, their role in the manufacture of products of agricultural origin. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2014; credit or registration in 4063.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140925, 795080, 'BIOL', '4062', 2020, 'Food and Dairy Microbiology', 'The role of microorganisms in the preservation, spoilage and poisoning in food and dairy products. Also, their role in the manufacture of products of agricultural origin. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2014; credit or registration in 4063.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140926, 553147, 'MICR', '426', 2020, 'General VIrology Laboratory', 'A laboratory to accompany 4068. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit with \"C\" or better or registration in 4068.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140927, 117820, 'BIOL', '479', 2020, 'Fisheries Biology', 'General principles and methods of freshwater fisheries biology and the management of natural fish populations. Three hours of lecture and three hours of laboratory. Laboratory fee required. Prerequisite: Biology 208, 209; Math 114, 116 or equivalent. Sp, odd.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140930, 132204, 'BIOL', '110', 2020, 'Human Biology', 'A comprehensive study of the structure and function of the human body and of the ecological problems that face mankind today. Non-majors only. Prerequisite: &quot;C&quot; or better in 1001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140931, 23610, 'BIOL', '451', 2020, 'Field Biology', 'Field studies of the flora and fauna native to selected habitats. Field trip fee required. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 2004, 2005, 2010; or \"C\" or better in 2030; or approval of department head.', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140932, 801432, 'COMM', '3030', 2020, 'Persuasion', 'A review of general theoretical approaches to persuasion and influence with focus on principles of persuasive communication and application of persuasive strategies. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3030)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140933, 677984, 'BIOL', '436', 2020, 'Dendrology', 'Classification, identification, and characteristics of important forest trees of the United States, stressing native species common to Louisiana. Two hours lecture and four hours laboratory including frequent field trips. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 1022, 1023.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140935, 649084, 'MATH', '1013', 2020, 'Elementary Functions', 'A pre-calculus course emphasizing functions of algebraic, trigonometric, and transcendental nature . This course is designed for those students who intend to enroll in calculus. Prerequisite: \'A\' in Math 1009 or Math ACT score of 23 or higher.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CMAT 1233', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140936, 169429, 'BIOL', '4026', 2020, 'Neurology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 4025. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 4025.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140937, 806197, 'CMST', '102', 2020, 'Voice and Diction', 'A non-technical approach to developing expressive speech. Emphasis is on phonetics, the mechanics of vocal sound, and oral readings.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140938, 289967, 'BIOL', '432', 2020, 'Aquatic Plants', 'A study of the plants that grow in aquatic and wetland sites. Emphasis placed on identification, distribution, and field characteristics. Two hours lecture and four hours laboratory including frequent field trips. Prerequisite: 122, 123. (Formerly Botany 403, 404.)', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140939, 802763, 'BIOL', '4025', 2020, 'Neurology', 'Study of the anatomy, physiology and pathology of the human nervous system.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140940, 802763, 'BIOL', '425', 2020, 'Neurology', 'Study of the anatomy, physiology and pathology of the human nervous system.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140941, 509361, 'CHEM', '4025', 2020, 'Directed Study: Inorganic', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A directed study for undergraduates and graduates. May include laboratory and/or library work. Four to six hours per week for each credit hour earned. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 422C)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140942, 37231, 'ART', '4050', 2020, 'Special Problems: Sculpture (Formerly ART 441G)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441G)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140943, 560478, 'BIOL', '4009', 2020, 'Cellular Physiology Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 4008. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in 4008.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140944, 560478, 'BIOL', '409', 2020, 'Cellular Physiology Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 4008. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in 4008.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140945, 559503, 'BIOL', '4008', 2020, 'Cellular Physiology', 'Physical and chemical aspects of the living organism including an introduction to molecular biology with emphasis on the cell. Prerequisites: credit or registration in CHEM 2032: credit or registration in BIOL 4009.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140946, 136645, 'BIOL', '417', 2020, 'Developmental Biology', 'An introduction to the mechanisms and evolution of developmental processes of plants and animals. Topics include pattern formation, cell differentiation, and organogenesis. An emphasis is placed on experimental aspects of developmental biology. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in BIOL 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140947, 697749, 'AVIA', '4030', 2020, 'Aviation Law', 'National and international regulatory and civil law as it relates to aviation and the aviation professional.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140948, 815936, 'AVIA', '4071', 2020, 'Airport Planning and Operations', 'Elements of planning and developing an airport.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140949, 91322, 'AVIA', '4072', 2020, 'Air Transportation Logistics', 'Transportation economics and logistics, including systems of goods movement, principles of transportation, logistics, costs and services, rate making, management and coordination.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140950, 277832, 'AVIA', '4003', 2020, 'Aerospace Education', 'Fundamentals of flight. Aeronautical knowledge equivalent to that required by the Federal Aviation Administration private pilot written examination. For Aerospace Education teachers, K-12.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140951, 181168, 'AVIA', '4004', 2020, 'Advanced Aerospace Education', 'Provides Aerospace Education teachers with advanced technological orientation, and foundation in the aerospace career fields.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140952, 132204, 'BIOL', '1010', 2020, 'Human Biology', 'A comprehensive study of the structure and function of the human body and of the ecological problems that face mankind today. Non-majors only. Prerequisite: &quot;C&quot; or better in 1001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140953, 580574, 'BIOL', '1003', 2020, 'Introduction to Scientific Research', 'A hands-on approach to understanding the scientific method with emphasis on project design, and data collection and analysis. Prerequisite: Admission to ULM Summer Collegiate Program and ULM-HHMI Pre-College Research Program.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140954, 596790, 'PHYS', '1050', 2020, 'Integrated Physics for Education Majors', 'Basic concepts and principles of physics, in particular, force and motion, energy, light, heat, electricity, and magnetism. Personal applications of science, process skills, problem-solving, and discovery/inquiry learning are also emphasized. Integrated lecture/lab format. For Elementary Education Majors only. F, Sp\r\n\r\nLCCN: CPHY 1013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140955, 947032, 'CHEM', '308', 2020, 'Quantitative Analysis Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany CHEM 2040. Six hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 1010 and credit or registration in CHEM 2040. F (Formerly 308)\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 2301', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140956, 794383, 'BIOL', '405', 2020, 'Evolutionary Population Genetics', 'A study of genetic variation in populations and its role in the evolutionary process. Prerequisite: 305. Sp, odd', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140957, 583510, 'CODI', '4085', 2020, 'Aural Rehabilitation', 'Professional services and procedures facilitating adequate receptive and expressive communication in persons with hearing impairments.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140958, 518731, 'BIOL', '4011', 2020, 'Genetics and Society', 'A survey of current topics in genetic research and recent advances in biotechnology, including implications of these discoveries. Prerequisite: Biology 120 and either 305 or permission of the instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140959, 722880, 'BIOL', '312', 2020, 'Human Physiology II', 'A continuation of 311. Emphasis on circulatory, respiratory, digestive, excretory, endocrine, and reproductive systems. Prerequisites: 311. (Formerly Zoology 312.) Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140960, 194779, 'BIOL', '332', 2020, 'Vertebrate Zoology', 'The morphology, taxonomy, and life history of representative vertebrates. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory with field trips. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2010 or 2030.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140961, 194779, 'BIOL', '3032', 2020, 'Vertebrate Zoology', 'The morphology, taxonomy, and life history of representative vertebrates. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory with field trips. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2010 or 2030.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140962, 988605, 'BIOL', '4114', 2020, 'Science, Biology, and Evolution', 'A biology capstone course. A broad, topical examination of evolutionary theory and principles and its connection to all disciplines of the biological sciences. Prerequisites: C or better in 1020, 1022, and 3005, or instructor\r\napproval.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140963, 428807, 'AVIA', '4002', 2020, 'Air Traffic Administration', 'The National Aerospace System. The role of Air Traffic Control in aviation safety. For Aviation Majors. Prerequisites: 1010, 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140964, 310810, 'AVIA', '4011', 2020, 'Flight Instructor Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction required for FAA flight instructor certificate. Course completion requires that the certificate be issued. Grades of CR(Credit) or NC(No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisite: 410 or concurrent enrollment. (Formerly 314).', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140965, 778781, 'AVIA', '4001', 2020, 'Air Transportation', 'The development and present status of air transportation, federal legislation, characteristics and classification of air carriers; the organization and function of the Federal Aviation Administration.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140966, 512736, 'AVIA', '3013', 2020, 'Flight Instructor Ground School', 'Instructional knowledge required for FAA flight instructor certificate. Prerequisite: Commercial pilot certificate with instrument rating. (Formerly 313).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140967, 559272, 'CHEM', '323', 2020, 'Physical Chemistry Laboratory II', 'Modern experimental techniques in physical chemistry. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 2041 and credit or registration in CHEM 3020. F.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140968, 634298, 'AVIA', '4017', 2020, 'Advanced Aerial Application', 'Operation of an agricultural aviation service. Economics, flight operations and techniques. Prerequisite: Junior standing in Aviation.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140969, 633459, 'AVIA', '4020', 2020, 'Airline Transport Pilot Ground School', 'Aeronautical knowledge required for FAA airline transport pilot certificate. Prerequisite: Unlimited commercial pilot certificate.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140970, 996016, 'AVIA', '4014', 2020, 'Instrument Flight Instructor Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction for FAA instrument rating on flight instructor certificate. Course completion requires that the rating be issued. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisite: 413 or concurrent enrollment.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140971, 625901, 'AVIA', '3041', 2020, 'Multiengine Pilot Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction required for FAA multiengine pilot rating. Course completion requires that the rating be issued. Grades of CR(Credit) or NC(No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisites: 340 or concurrent enrollment; Commercial pilot certificate with instrument rating. (Formerly 321).', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140972, 615609, 'AVIA', '3012', 2020, 'Agricultural Pilot Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction and practice required for FAA commercial pilot certificate, with emphasis on tailwheel and agricultural-type airplanes, and agricultural aviation operations. Course completion requires that the certificate be issued. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisite: Private pilot certificate with instrument rating.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140973, 566877, 'AVIA', '4015', 2020, 'Aircraft Engines and Systems', 'Advanced aircraft engines and systems of a typical large twin pressurized turboprop, including warning systems, doors, electrical, lighting, fuel, engines, fire protection, hydraulics, flight controls, stall warnings, avionics, TCAS, EGPWS, communications, landing gear, pneumatics, air conditioning, pressurization, oxygen, ice protection, APU, and emergency equipment. Prerequisite: minimum grade of &quot;C&quot; in 1010 and 1011, completion of all 100-level English and Math courses, or instructor approval...', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140974, 480320, 'AVIA', '3018', 2020, 'Aerial Application', 'Concepts of aerial application of agricultural seed and chemicals; safety, history, regulations, equipment, environmental impact. Prerequisite: Private pilot certificate. (Formerly 217).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140975, 495281, 'AVIA', '2022', 2020, 'Instrument Pilot Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction required for FAA instrument pilot rating, given in actual or simulated instrument meteorological conditions. Course completion requires that the rating be issued. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisite: Private pilot certificate. (Formerly 332)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140976, 305127, 'AVIA', '3011', 2020, 'Commercial Pilot Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction and practice required for FAA commercial pilot certificate. Course completion requires that the certificate be issued. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisite: Private pilot certificate with instrument rating. (Formerly 212-213-214)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140977, 114813, 'AVIA', '3010', 2020, 'Commercial Ground Instruction', 'Advanced principles of flight, advanced navigation, aircraft systems, advanced meteorology. Aeronautical knowledge required for Commercial Pilot Certification. Prerequisite: Private Pilot Certification or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140978, 630677, 'INSU', '205', 2020, 'Risk and Insurance', 'A study of pure risk and risk- bearing, including insurance and non-insurance methods of handling risks; introduction to life, disability, property, marine, and liability insurance. F,Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140979, 435110, 'ATMS', '415', 2020, 'Micrometeorology', 'Introduction to the physical processes in the atmospheric surface boundary layer. Influence of low level atmospheric turbulence on the diffusion of heat, water vapor (evaporation), and atmospheric pollutants. Prerequisites: ATMS 3006 and 3015.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140980, 912282, 'ART', '4040', 2020, 'Metalcraft and Jewelrymaking', 'The designing and fabrication of jewelry and small metal products. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1002 or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140981, 879583, 'BIOL', '400D', 2020, 'Directed Study: Cosmos', 'Selected studies in general and biological science. Content varies. A. Oceanus; B. Brain, Mind, and Behavior; C. Through the Genetic Maze; D. Cosmos; E. Race to Save the Planet. May be repeated for a maximum of 12 credit hours. No more than 6 semester hours may be applied toward degree requirements.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140982, 940866, 'NURS', '2005', 2020, 'Health Intervention I', 'Theories and concepts of health intervention and their relationship to the nursing process. Emphasis is on health promotion and health maintenance in the adult with common variations across the life span. Prerequisite: NURS 2000, Registration or credit in NURS 2007 and 2004, 2016, and 2080.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140983, 29457, 'ATMS', '3050', 2020, 'Special Topics in Operational Meterology', 'Provides the students with work experience at a National Weather Service Forecast Office. Grade of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisites: ATMS 3003, and credit or registration in ATMS 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140984, 655607, 'ATMS', '102', 2020, 'Introduction to Severe Weather', 'Introduction to basic meteorology, forecasting, and societal impacts of severe and\r\nhazardous weather. Phenomena studied include hurricanes, thunderstorms, tornadoes,\r\nhail, lighting, winter storms, floods and drought.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140985, 95875, 'ART', '3056', 2020, 'Advanced Color Photography', 'Theory and practice of advanced color photography for the creative photographer. Prerequisites: Art 2046, 2056, or permission of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140986, 351606, 'ART', '3001', 2020, 'Calligraphy', 'A comprehensive study of hand lettering. Variations in styles are complemented with a study of motifs executed in pen and ink. For art majors and non-art majors.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140987, 10917, 'ART', '3081', 2020, 'Intermediate Sculpture', 'Further development of sculptural processes and techniques in a variety of media. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2081. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140988, 135662, 'ART', '4004', 2020, 'Advanced Drawing', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Advanced drawing. Primarily life drawing in a variety of media. Six hours studio. Prerequisite: 1004. (Formerly 303.) Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140989, 809845, 'ART', '4007', 2020, 'Raku Ceramics', 'Lecture and demonstrations on use of Raku ceramics, including kiln construction and firing. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140990, 809845, 'ART', '407', 2020, 'Raku Ceramics', 'Lecture and demonstrations on use of Raku ceramics, including kiln construction and firing. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140991, 145582, 'ART', '425', 2020, 'Renaissance', 'The visual arts in Italy from the early Renaissance through Mannerism. Prerequisite: 2001, 2002. (Formerly 325.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (140992, 771907, 'ART', '4008', 2020, 'Art Applications in Teaching', 'Mixed media; drawing multi-image processes, enlargement techniques, and three- dimensional poster material are utilized in visual aid techniques.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140993, 851789, 'ART', '4009', 2020, 'Techniques in the Fine Arts', 'A study, analysis, and participation in the productions of various media in the fine arts such as drawing, painting, printing, and sculpture. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140994, 562672, 'ART', '4026', 2020, 'Nineteenth Century', 'Nineteenth Century European and American Rococo through Post-Impressionism periods. Prerequisites: 2001, 2002, or approval of the department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140995, 492949, 'ART', '4029', 2020, 'Contemporary', 'Twentieth century European and American Art. A study of the major achievements in painting, sculpture, and architecture since 1900. Prerequisite: 2001, 2002. (Formerly 329.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (140996, 34176, 'ART', '272', 2020, 'Painting', 'Painting in oils. Six hours studio. Prerequisites: 101, 104 or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141000, 657779, 'ART', '206', 2020, 'Graphic Design II', 'Typography, its usage as a design element, the layout and design of publications and introduction to commercial production methods. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2005. (Formerly Advertising Design 206.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141001, 389054, 'ART', '2000', 2020, 'Analytical Perspective', 'The principles of geometry in the development of spatial logic and imagery in one-point, two- point, and isometric perspective will be used. Techniques in rendering support procedures in architecture, illustration, and industrial and environmental design. For art majors and non-art majors. Six hours studio. (Formerly Art 403, Analytical Perspective).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141002, 329875, 'CHEM', '352', 2020, 'Biochemistry II', 'Thermodynamics, metabolism, photosynthesis, protein and nucleic acid biosynthesis. Three hours lecture. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 3050. Sp (Formerly 337)\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 4413', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141003, 332491, 'ART', '2041', 2020, 'General Crafts', 'Exploration of various craft media. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141004, 515424, 'ART', '2042', 2020, 'Arts and Crafts', 'Application of methods and exploration of media for the exceptional child. One hour lecture and ninety minutes studio.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141005, 442391, 'ART', '2057', 2020, 'Lithography', 'Printing process with Bavarian limestone. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1001, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141006, 584620, 'ART', '2058', 2020, 'Block Printing', 'Printing process in wood and linoleum. One hour lecture and 5 hours studio. Prerequisite: 1001, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141007, 43061, 'AGRO', '413', 2020, 'Soil Fertility and Chemical Properties', 'The chemical and mineralogical properties of soils from the theoretical and technical viewpoints. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: AGRO 2001; CHEM 1001, 1005, or 1007. (Formerly AGRO 405, 406).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141008, 43061, 'AGRO', '4013', 2020, 'Soil Fertility and Chemical Properties', 'The chemical and mineralogical properties of soils from the theoretical and technical viewpoints. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: AGRO 2001; CHEM 1001, 1005, or 1007. (Formerly AGRO 405, 406).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141009, 758261, 'AGRO', '4011', 2020, 'Agricultural Chemicals', 'Herbicides, fungicides, insecticides and growth regulators and their uses. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: CHEM 1001 or 1007.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141010, 4273802, 'AVIA', '3080', 2020, 'U A S Design and Systems', 'Basic design and aerodynamic considerations for UAS, including systems common to most UAS with focus on those that differ significantly from their manned counterparts, and emphasis on autopilot systems and their integration with flight controls and airborne\r\ncommunication systems. Prerequisite: Approval of