a working knowledge of IBM compatible microcomputer systems and common software usages of agriculturalist. Topics covered: DOS, word processing, spreadsheet analysis, introduction to SAS, and management software. Prerequisite: CSCI 170.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141032, 150673, 'AGRI', '3044', 2020, 'Agribusiness Practicum', 'Design, plan, and execute an approved agribusiness enterprise. May be used for elective credit only. May be repeated. Prerequisites: AGRI 244 and approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141033, 800397, 'AGRI', '4001', 2020, 'Animal and Plant Improvement', 'Application of the scientific methods, principles, and techniques of mating and selection systems to improve economically important traits in animal and plant populations.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141034, 213697, 'AGRI', '4005', 2020, 'Irrigation Practicum', 'Principles and techniques in irrigation system design.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141035, 716289, 'AGRI', '4092', 2020, 'Soil Science (Formerly AGRI 491A)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Individualized work on special problems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly AGRI 491A)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141036, 716289, 'AGRI', '491A', 2020, 'Soil Science (Formerly AGRI 491A)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Individualized work on special problems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly AGRI 491A)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141039, 3285678, 'TOXI', '2010', 2020, 'Techniques of Food Microbiology and Toxicology', 'Practical guidelines and understanding of analytical methods of food safety and toxicology. Emphasis on micro-organisms and toxins encountered in foods. Prerequisites: TOXI 1010, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141040, 865361, 'AGRO', '309', 2020, 'Forage Crops and Pasture Management', 'Adaptation, production, establishment, utilization and management of forage crops and pastures. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 1001 or 1003. (Formerly AGRO 305, 307).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141041, 865361, 'AGRO', '3009', 2020, 'Forage Crops and Pasture Management', 'Adaptation, production, establishment, utilization and management of forage crops and pastures. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 1001 or 1003. (Formerly AGRO 305, 307).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141042, 240972, 'TOXI', '326', 2020, 'Clinical Chemistry and Toxicology', 'Principles of basic clinical chemistry and toxicology procedures applied to enzymes; endocrine function; electrolytes and blood gases; renal function; gastric, pancreatic and intestine function; biochemistry of pregnancy; therapeutic drug monitoring and analysis of toxic substances. Prerequisite: MLSC 3022, 3023, or approval of the Program Director. (Same as MLSC 3026.) Toxicology majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141043, 290680, 'SOCL', '3025', 2020, 'Contemporary Social Movements', 'An examination of current social movements with an analysis of social and cultural background, forms of expression and organization, and their role and function in modern society.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141046, 542079, 'TOXI', '4014', 2020, 'General Toxicology Laboratory', 'Laboratory exercises to accompany 4012. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 4012. Toxicology majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141047, 199237, 'TOXI', '4044', 2020, 'Industrial Hygiene', 'Introduction to industrial hygiene: general principles, regulatory standards, workplace hazards, exposure control, problem solving strategies. Prerequisites: TOXI 1001, 2001. Toxicology majors only. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141048, 602664, 'PHAR', '4013', 2020, 'Pharmacology III', 'Continuation of 412 with emphasis on the cardiovascular, renal, and respiratory systems. Prerequisites: 407, 412, 436.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141049, 602664, 'PHAR', '413', 2020, 'Pharmacology III', 'Continuation of 412 with emphasis on the cardiovascular, renal, and respiratory systems. Prerequisites: 407, 412, 436.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141050, 913603, 'AVIA', '101', 2020, 'Introduction to Aviation', 'Introduction to the history and development of aviation, with an analysis of its impact on national and international affairs. A non-technical survey.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141052, 773317, 'TOXI', '4091', 2020, 'Seminar', 'Students are required to make oral presentations and discuss special current problems in the field of toxicology. Involves presentation and class participation. A final comprehensive examination will cover all aspects of the discipline of toxicology. Prerequisite: credit or registration in all required Toxicology courses. Toxicology majors only. F,Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141053, 16068, 'TOXI', '4012', 2020, 'General Toxicology', 'Continuation of Toxicology 4011. Physiological basis of chemical toxicity in organ systems. Prerequisites: TOXL 4011; BIOL 3011, 3012; grade of &quot;C&quot; or better in Toxicology 1001 and 2001; credit or registration in 4014. Toxicology majors only. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141054, 16068, 'TOXI', '412', 2020, 'General Toxicology', 'Continuation of Toxicology 4011. Physiological basis of chemical toxicity in organ systems. Prerequisites: TOXL 4011; BIOL 3011, 3012; grade of &quot;C&quot; or better in Toxicology 1001 and 2001; credit or registration in 4014. Toxicology majors only. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141055, 278857, 'TOXI', '4041', 2020, 'Industrial Hygiene I', '3 cr. Introduction into industrial hygiene covering its history, ethics, and general principles. Review of regulatory agencies and occupational safety and health standards included. Detailed discussions regarding specific occupational hazards will begin, and include properties of the hazard, industrial exposure potential, exposure monitoring techniques, relevant regulatory standards, and control methodologies. Prerequisites: TOXI 1001 and 2001. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141056, 378640, 'RADT', '4003', 2020, 'Radiographic Exposure', 'Advanced theories of radiographic exposure including problem solving and the practical application of technic principles. Methods of generator and x-ray equipment quality assurance. Prerequisite: RADT 320, 321. F', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141058, 790337, 'HUMN', '1003', 2020, 'Interdisciplinary Arts Abroad', 'An interdisciplinary study of fine arts and culture with study and travel abroad. Prerequisite: Approval of instructors.', 6.0000, 6.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141059, 703818, 'PHIL', '300B', 2020, 'Study of Religion: Ethics in America', 'Selected studies in Philosophy and Religion. Content varies. A. A Study of Religion. (Same as Religion 300A.); B. Ethics in America. C. The Examined Life.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141063, 418862, 'PHAR', '419', 2020, 'Pharmacobiotech', 'A study of the application of biotechnology to pharmaceuticals including drugs, diagnostics, and vaccines. Emphasis is placed on the techniques of biotechnology, recombinant proteins and peptides, monoclonal antibodies, and physiochemical properties, and metabolism of genetically engineered biopharmaceuticals. Prerequisite: 408, 409; credit or registration in 414; or approval of Department Head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141064, 111561, 'PHAR', '447', 2020, 'Ethics in Pharmacy Practice', '3 cr. This course prepares students to distinquish ethical from other kinds of issues in pharmacy, and to identify the options open to a pharmacist faced with an ethical issue.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141065, 103288, 'ENTR', '250', 2020, 'Entrepreneurship', 'This course will explore the unique aspects of entrepreneurship in modern society. Students will learn how to identify, assess, and develop business ideas and how to locate and evaluate business opportunities. Prerequisites: None. F, S<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CMGM 2413', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141066, 494412, 'POLS', '491C', 2020, 'Directed Study: Political Theory (Formerly 491C)', 'Directed study and/or research in selected areas of government. Prerequisite: Advanced standing, approval of department head, and permission of the instructor. (Formerly 491C)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141067, 539081, 'PHAR', '412', 2020, 'Pharmacology II', 'Continuation of Pharmacy 411 with emphasis on inflammatory and allergic reactions and the central nervous system. Prerequisites: 411; Credit or registration in 436.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141075, 245994, 'PHAR', '493', 2020, 'Case Studies in Pharmacy Administration', 'Case studies in drug marketing, pharmacy law and ethics, professional relations, and managerial accounting. Prerequisite: 451, 454.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141082, 90754, 'PHAR', '4011', 2020, 'Pharmacology I', 'Pharmacological, anatomical, and physiological basis of drug action. Topics include general principles of therapeutics, pharmacodynamics, pharmacokinetics and toxicology, and the action of drugs in the peripheral nervous system. Prerequisite: First Year Pharmacy Standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141092, 78728, 'PHAR', '4081', 2020, 'Introductory Institutional Pharmacy Experience', 'A one-month introduction to the practice of pharmacy in the institutional setting. Minimum of 40 hours per week experiential training. Prerequisite: Second year pharmacy standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141093, 581745, 'RADT', '4030', 2020, 'Vascular / Interventional Procedures', 'Principles and skills involved in vascular/interventional procedures. Prerequisite: RATE standing. F, Sp, S', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141095, 754880, 'SOCL', '4145', 202