ion of hardware and software and software technology to management, accounting, and finance in small businesses. Prerequisite: CINS 2005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141777, 517865, 'ENGL', '3051', 2020, 'Junior Seminar: Poetry / Drama', 'Intensive study of a significant body of poetry and/or drama, with an emphasis on close reading. Prerequisite: one 2000-level literature course in English.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141778, 278164, 'ENGL', '4081', 2020, 'Expository Writing', 'Development of the ability to communicate accurately and effectively in writing, with emphasis on the teaching of writing in all disciplines.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141779, 884692, 'FCSC', '2017', 2020, 'Child Guidance', 'Directing and guiding the behavior of young children in the preschool setting. Sp', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141780, 442624, 'FCSC', '2012', 2020, 'Introduction to Human Development', 'Study of growth and development from birth to age three with special emphasis on observation and participation with the infant, toddler, and preschool child.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141781, 295461, 'CMST', '310', 2020, 'Communication and Conflict', 'A study of the theory and practice of communication strategies and styles in conflict situations; looks at conflict in interpersonal and/or professional settings. Prerequisite: COMM 1018 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3010)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141782, 880760, 'ENGL', '3093', 2020, 'Mythology of the Greeks and Romans', 'Tales of the gods, heroes, and great families that have influenced literature, art, and music. (Same as Latin 3003.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141783, 619033, 'ENGL', '4038', 2020, 'Shakespeare’s Comedies and Histories', 'Representative comedies and histories, with emphasis on Shakespeares development as a dramatic artist.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141784, 728088, 'FCSC', '2006', 2020, 'Residential Design', 'Selection and arrangement of furnishings with emphasis on planning costs and budgets for different income levels. Planning of individual rooms including the study of accessories, color schemes, and suitable fabrics. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141785, 495430, 'ENGL', '4042', 2020, 'Style and Editing in Technical Writing', 'A study of the varieties of technical style and techniques of editing and revision. \r\nPrerequisite: Registration in or completion of any junior-level or above writing course or department head approval.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141786, 736633, 'ENGL', '4036', 2020, 'Chaucer', 'Studies in The Canterbury Tales and selected other works of Geoffrey Chaucer.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141787, 183673, 'ENGL', '4075', 2020, 'Romantic Movement', 'Representative writers and works of the Romantic period.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141788, 848759, 'FCSC', '1001', 2020, 'Professional Etiquette', 'Understanding of basic social concepts in the home, society, business and the professional world.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141789, 708950, 'ENGL', '3015', 2020, 'Creative Writing', 'Writing and criticism of short stories, essays, one-act plays, and poetry.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141791, 59997, 'ENGL', '325', 2020, 'Advanced Grammar', 'Prerequisite: 1002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141792, 263117, 'ENGL', '326', 2020, 'Advanced Composition', 'Factual, narrative, biographical, informal, and critical essays with intensive study of prose techniques. Prerequisite: 1002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141793, 551726, 'ENGL', '4021', 2020, 'The Literature of the Bible', 'Selected books from the Old and New Testaments, with emphasis on their literary value and influence on English and American literature.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141794, 921166, 'ENGL', '4078', 2020, 'American Literary Studies I', 'Works of major writers to 1850.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141799, 120534, 'ENGL', '2020C', 2020, 'Professional Writing and Communication: Arts, Hum., Soc. Sci.', '3 cr. Instruction in technical and professional writing and communication for arts, humanities, and social sciences. Emphasis on written and oral forms. Includes practice in documentation, collaboration, oral presentation, graphics and design, and research. Prerequisites: ENGL 1002; junior standing or permission of English Dept. Head; restricted to Arts and Sciences and Construction majors EXCEPTING biology, chemistry, geosciences, agriculture, and math majors. (Formerly ENGL 220B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141800, 784592, 'ENGL', '4027', 2020, 'Literature of the South', 'Representative writers of the myths and reality of the south.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141801, 156039, 'FRNH', '201', 2020, 'Intermediate French I', 'A continuation on the intermediate level of 1001-1002, with an increased emphasis upon reading and discussion. Work in the computerized Language Learning Center is required. Prerequisite: A \"C\" or better in 1002 or 1005, or permission of Department Head.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CFRN 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141802, 370541, 'ENGL', '2006', 2020, 'American Literature II', 'Texts from the Civil War to the present. Content varies.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CENL 2163', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141803, 60837, 'ENGL', '202', 2020, 'British Literature II', 'Texts from the Romantics to the present. Content varies.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CENL 2113', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141804, 60837, 'ENGL', '2002', 2020, 'British Literature II', 'Texts from the Romantics to the present. Content varies.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CENL 2113', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141805, 484616, 'CMST', '490', 2020, 'Internship', 'One semester of supervised off-campus industry service. Academic requirements include a final paper and presentation. Prerequisites: Completion of 16 hours of COMM courses, including either COMM 2009 or COMM 2090, plus an approved internship proposal. (Formerly CMST 4090 and MCOM 4090)', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141806, 354053, 'MCOM', '454', 2020, 'Advanced Electronic Media Design', 'Theory and principles of electronic media design from conception to completion, for a variety of mass communications applications emphasizing multimedia. Prerequisite: MCOM 354.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141807, 354053, 'MCOM', '4054', 2020, 'Advanced Electronic Media Design', 'Theory and principles of electronic media design from conception to completion, for a variety of mass communications applications emphasizing multimedia. Prerequisite: MCOM 354.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141811, 474217, 'MCOM', '4090', 2020, 'Internship', 'Field experience under the general supervision of a faculty member and the direct supervision of an industry professional, with academic components including a final paper and presentation. Prerequisites: Completion of 15 hours of Mass Communications coursework including MCOM 390 and approval of academic advisor, faculty internship supervisor and site supervisor.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141814, 785554, 'READ', '4022', 2020, 'Literacy Interventions for Adolescents', 'Teaches secondary education majors to integrate reading, writing, speaking, and listening strategies and activities into adolescent reading instruction. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141815, 270566, 'MCOM', '3055', 2020, 'Interactive Media Publishing', 'An integrated approach to interactive media publishing, focusing on the establishment of an effective online presence through the design, development, and management of Internet web sites utilizing text, images, sound and video. Prerequisites: MCOM 354 or permission of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141816, 73184, 'MCOM', '4032', 2020, 'Advanced Reporting for Print Media', 'Depth reporting and critical writing on police, court, political, financial, governmental and other social events and issues. Prerequisite: MCOM 331.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141817, 73184, 'MCOM', '432', 2020, 'Advanced Reporting for Print Media', 'Depth reporting and critical writing on police, court, political, financial, governmental and other social events and issues. Prerequisite: MCOM 331.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141818, 475376, 'COMM', '2002', 2020, 'Media Performance', 'The role of the announcer; principles of communication in the electronic media; voice and diction, including foreign pronunciation; techniques for various program types. Lecture and lab. A fee is charged each student to help defray expenses related to this course.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141819, 751975, 'PHIL', '403', 2020, 'Ethics', 'A study of the theoretical foundations of morality with reference to approaches to ethical thought, character, and action. Concepts include good and evil, right and wrong, obligation and rights, responsibility and freedom. The application of these concepts to the working out of particular ethical problems. (Same as PHIL 403.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141820, 596520, 'PHIL', '405', 2020, 'Philosophy of Religion', 'A study of attempts to bring rational justification and clarification to religious beliefs and practices, focusing primarily on the concepts of Christian theology. Topics will include the existence of nature of God, faith and reason, death and immortality, mysticism, the problem of evil, religious experience, and the impact of existentialism on contemporary religious thought.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141821, 28651, 'SPCH', '4051', 2020, 'American Public Address', 'Provides a study of American public address from colonial times to the present. Prerequisite: COMM 2001, 3030 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 4051)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141822, 766539, 'CJUS', '4019', 2020, 'Internship in Criminal Justice', 'One semester of supervised service in a criminal justice agency. Open only to Criminal Justice majors who have completed at least 60 hours of course work and have no prior experience. Students must make application for the Internship the semester prior to that in which it will be taken.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141824, 4245865, 'COMM', '2010', 2020, 'Writing for Professional Communicators', 'Introduction to writing for professional communicators, emphasizing styles of\r\nwriting for eye vs. ear and for print, broadcast and online contexts. Lecture and\r\nlab. Prerequisite: ENGL 1002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141825, 874501, 'MUSC', '1092', 2020, 'Enjoyment of Jazz', 'Logical musical derivations and developments of American Jazz, both of itself as an art form and its influence on other areas of music. Ethnic influences such as Afro-American Jazz, New Orleans ragtime, and Memphis influences will be explored.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CMUS 1023', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141826, 873481, 'MCOM', '350', 2020, 'Audio Production', 'Introduction to audio production for radio, video, film and music recording, including principles, equipment, pre-production, production, and post-production. A fee is charged each student to help defray expenses related to this course. Prerequisite: Sophomore standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141827, 347224, 'COMM', '4072', 2020, 'Media Analysis and Criticism', 'Critical methodologies and analysis of media content and programming, emphasizing aesthetic, historical, social, cultural, and industrial factors affecting audience response. Prerequisite: Junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141828, 159306, 'MGMT', '308', 2020, 'Compensation and Benefits', 'Provides an In-depth overview of compensation and benefits administration in public and private organizations. Focuses on factors impacting compensation and benefit issues including corporate policy, job analysis and job evaluation, market pricing, and industry comparisons. Prerequisite: 3001 or 3005 or consent of management program coordinator.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141830, 546620, 'SPCH', '4091B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Forensics (Formerly CMST 491B)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisites: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141834, 707267, 'CJUS', '2070', 2020, 'Corrections', 'An in-depth examination of the Corrections component of the criminal justice system. Fundamentals of correctional practices and philosophy, historically and systemically studied, including law, sentencing, and appellate review as each relates to the correctional process. Survey of correctional components: community-based programs, institutions, administration, offender categories, classification, and treatment. Prerequisite: For Criminal Justice majors only--1001 or approval of program director.<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCRJ 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141836, 954173, 'CJUS', '2006', 2020, 'Industrial and Business Security', 'An examination of the basic problems, procedures, and needs in the field of security work. A comparison of private agencies, hotels, retail and industrial enterprises which handle their own security with private and public security organizations. Emphasis is given to the role of private, industrial, and business security systems and their relationship to the criminal justice system.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141837, 529396, 'CJUS', '4099', 2020, 'Senior Seminar in Criminal Justice', 'A capstone course for the integration of knowledge concerning the criminal justice system, criminal law, criminology, juvenile delinquency, law enforcement, corrections, administration, legal aspects, and research methods. Restricted to students receiving the baccalaureate degree in Criminal Justice. Registration is required during the semester in which the degree is to be received.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141838, 549324, 'CJUS', '400', 2020, 'Correctional Treatment', 'An overview and an examination of the basics of classification and counseling approaches, emphasizing interpersonal skills development, data collection, interviewing, assessment techniques, and counseling. Prerequisite: 1001, 2070, and junior standing or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141839, 549324, 'CJUS', '4000', 2020, 'Correctional Treatment', 'An overview and an examination of the basics of classification and counseling approaches, emphasizing interpersonal skills development, data collection, interviewing, assessment techniques, and counseling. Prerequisite: 1001, 2070, and junior standing or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141840, 596482, 'CJUS', '3010', 2020, 'Correctional Institutions', 'Analysis of the structure and function of prison staffing, prison operations, the convict world, prison violence, and jails. Prerequisite: 1001, 2070, or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141841, 596482, 'CJUS', '310', 2020, 'Correctional Institutions', 'Analysis of the structure and function of prison staffing, prison operations, the convict world, prison violence, and jails. Prerequisite: 1001, 2070, or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141842, 382953, 'CJUS', '3001', 2020, 'Criminal Justice Procedure and Evidence', 'Analysis of procedural law related to due process. Evidence and rules of aw related to evidence are examined. Prerequisite: CJUS 2093 or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141843, 359561, 'CJUS', '4016', 2020, 'Contemporary Issues in Criminal Justice', 'Examination of the literature and analysis of current issues relevant to criminal justice. Prerequisite: Junior, Senior, or Graduate standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141845, 352485, 'CJUS', '2033', 2020, 'Forensics', 'An overview of techniques applied in identification of human skeletal remains for the medicolegal professions, including assessment of age, sex, ancestry, trauma, and disease; occupational stress markers; procedures for search/recovery of human remains; and estimations of time since death (same as ANTS and SOCL 2033).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141846, 352485, 'CJUS', '233', 2020, 'Forensics', 'An overview of techniques applied in identification of human skeletal remains for the medicolegal professions, including assessment of age, sex, ancestry, trauma, and disease; occupational stress markers; procedures for search/recovery of human remains; and estimations of time since death (same as ANTS and SOCL 2033).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141847, 612369, 'CJUS', '4091', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Individual examination of relevant literature in students area of interest as approved and directed by the major professor. May not be repeated for more than 3 hours credit. Prerequisite: Prior approval of supervising instructor.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141848, 313306, 'CJUS', '4005', 2020, 'Theories of Crime and Delinquency', 'An analysis of the extent of crime and delinquency; impact of crime and delinquency on society; physical, social, and psychological causation of crime and delinquency; and current issues in criminology. (Same as SOCL 4005.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141849, 313306, 'CJUS', '405', 2020, 'Theories of Crime and Delinquency', 'An analysis of the extent of crime and delinquency; impact of crime and delinquency on society; physical, social, and psychological causation of crime and delinquency; and current issues in criminology. (Same as SOCL 4005.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141850, 165177, 'CJUS', '2099', 2020, 'Overview of the Criminal Justice System', 'A capstone course for the integration of knowledge concerning the criminal justice system and criminal law with some attention to current legal issues in law enforcement and corrections. Restricted to students receiving the Associate of Arts Degree in Criminal Justice. Registration is required during the semester in which the degree is to be received.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141851, 301929, 'CHEM', '103', 2020, 'Introductory Chemistry Laboratory I', 'A laboratory course to accompany CHEM 1001. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in CHEM 1001. For non-majors. F, Sp, Su1\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1101', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141852, 474370, 'SCIE', '104', 2020, 'Integrated Geosciences for Education Majors', 'The goal of this course is to present an integrated approach to essential concepts in introductory geology (physical and historical geology), astronomy (from an earth science perspective), and weather. Personal applications of science, the process skills, problem-solving, and discovery/inquiry learning are emphasized. For Elementary Education majors only. (Formerly SCIE 104)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141853, 399407, 'AVIA', '1012', 2020, 'Private Pilot Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction and solo practice required for FAA private pilot certificate. Course completion requires that the certificate be issued. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141854, 495281, 'AVIA', '3022', 2020, 'Instrument Pilot Flight Instruction', 'Flight instruction required for FAA instrument pilot rating, given in actual or simulated instrument meteorological conditions. Course completion requires that the rating be issued. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisite: Private pilot certificate. (Formerly 332)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141855, 849359, 'CHEM', '231', 2020, 'Organic Chemistry Laboratory I', 'Laboratory to accompany Organic Chemistry I. Introduction to procedures used in the organic laboratory. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: credit or registration in CHEM 2030 and a \'C\" or better in CHEM 1010. F, Sp, Su1 (Formerly 305)<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 2211', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141856, 404242, 'CHEM', '350', 2020, 'Biochemistry I', 'Introduction to structure and function of proteins, nucleic acids, lipids and carbohydrates and enzyme kinetics, mechanisms, regulation, and vitamins. Three hours lecture. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 2032. F, Su1 (Formerly 336)<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 3403', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141858, 135431, 'CHEM', '1002', 2020, 'Introductory Chemistry II', 'The fundamentals of organic and biochemistry. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 1001. Three hours lecture. For non-majors. F, Sp, Su2\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1113', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141859, 64784, 'CHEM', '4013', 2020, 'Advanced Inorganic Chemistry', 'The periodic table, valence theories, inorganic structure and reactivity, and coordination chemistry. Three hours of lecture per week. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in CHEM 2030. F, odd.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141860, 64784, 'CHEM', '413', 2020, 'Advanced Inorganic Chemistry', 'The periodic table, valence theories, inorganic structure and reactivity, and coordination chemistry. Three hours of lecture per week. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in CHEM 2030. F, odd.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141861, 974957, 'CHEM', '499B', 2020, 'Research: Biochemistry (Formerly CHEM 400B)', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 cr. Research problems that can be completed in one semester. Three to six hours laboratory per week per credit hour. Prerequisites: Junior or senior standing in chemistry and approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 400B)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141862, 87341, 'SCIE', '102', 2020, 'Integrated Chemistry for Education Majors', 'Fundamental concepts of chemistry with an emphasis on the interdisciplinary nature of the concepts introduced. Integrated lecture/lab format. For Elementary Education Majors only. F, Sp\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141863, 216924, 'CHEM', '3020', 2020, 'Physical Chemistry I', 'Fundamental interpretations of the physical principles of chemistry with emphasis on equilibrium thermodynamics and chemical kinetics. Three hours lecture and one hour recitation. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in CHEM 1008; PHYS 2008; MATH 1032. F (Formerly 401)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141864, 917306, 'CHEM', '3001', 2020, 'Chemistry Seminar', '1 credit hour per semester, with cumulative maximum of 4 cr. allowed. Presentation of oral reports (with written synopses) on topics of current scientific and societal interest, including discussion of ethical and political implications, with emphasis on resources in the chemical literature. Prerequisite: Junior or senior standing in chemistry. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141866, 951639, 'BIOL', '2040', 2020, 'Human Anatomy', 'Gross structure and physiology of the body with emphasis on the skeletal, muscular, nervous, and circulatory systems. Prerequisites: 1020 and 1021, or 2026; cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher; \"C\" or better in 1020/1021 or 2026; credit or registration in 2041. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141867, 565932, 'BIOL', '308', 2020, 'Introduction to Evolutionary Biology', 'A survey of fundamental concepts of modern evolutionary theory, including natural selection, speciation, and adaptation, followed by an investigation of recent issues and controversies in evolutionary biology. Reading and discussion of primary sources will be emphasized. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141868, 565932, 'BIOL', '3008', 2020, 'Introduction to Evolutionary Biology', 'A survey of fundamental concepts of modern evolutionary theory, including natural selection, speciation, and adaptation, followed by an investigation of recent issues and controversies in evolutionary biology. Reading and discussion of primary sources will be emphasized. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141869, 743302, 'CHEM', '422D', 2020, 'Directed Study: Organic', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A directed study for undergraduates and graduates. May include laboratory and/or library work. Four to six hours per week for each credit hour earned. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 422D)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141872, 904048, 'BIOL', '3020', 2020, 'Conservation Biology', 'A course dealing with biodiversity and its conservation. Topics include biodiversity, habitat loss, the effects of habitat changes on populations, and the design and establishment of reserves. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in 1022, 1023.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141873, 513716, 'CJUS', '2050', 2020, 'Courts and Criminal Justice', 'Examination of the court component of the criminal justice system. Emphasis on structure, roles, and functions of courts and their relationship to other system components and social institutions. Prerequisite: 1001 or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141874, 513716, 'CJUS', '250', 2020, 'Courts and Criminal Justice', 'Examination of the court component of the criminal justice system. Emphasis on structure, roles, and functions of courts and their relationship to other system components and social institutions. Prerequisite: 1001 or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141875, 17424, 'ANTG', '410', 2020, 'Archeology of Louisiana Indians', 'An introduction to the archeology of Louisianas Indian tribes from Paleo-Indian times (10,000 B.C.) through the historic period. Prerequisite: Junior or senior standing or permission of the instructor. (Same as GEOG 4010.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141876, 559503, 'BIOL', '408', 2020, 'Cellular Physiology', 'Physical and chemical aspects of the living organism including an introduction to molecular biology with emphasis on the cell. Prerequisites: credit or registration in CHEM 2032: credit or registration in BIOL 4009.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141877, 919952, 'BIOL', '4097', 2020, 'Undergraduate Research Participation', 'An honors course in which the student performs independent research. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141879, 975905, 'ZOOL', '114', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Anatomy and Physiology II Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 1015. Two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit with C or better or registration in 1015, 1016. Non-majors only.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 2221', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141880, 975905, 'BIOL', '1017', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Anatomy and Physiology II Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 1015. Two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit with C or better or registration in 1015, 1016. Non-majors only.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 2221', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141881, 432690, 'BUSN', '4081', 2020, 'Continuing Studies in Business', 'Various topics in applied business for students not pursuing a degree. May be repeated. Credit may not be applied toward a degree. Grades of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141883, 404886, 'BIOL', '498', 2020, 'Undergraduate Research Participation', 'A continuation of 4097.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141884, 534961, 'BIOL', '499', 2020, 'Senior Biology Seminar', 'May be repeated one time. A seminar course to acquaint students with recent primary literature. Class format will include discussions and written papers. Prerequisite: 40 hours of Biology credit.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141885, 662179, 'BIOL', '330', 2020, 'Invertebrate Zoology', 'The morphology and phylogeny of representative invertebrates. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2010 or 2030.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141886, 662179, 'BIOL', '3030', 2020, 'Invertebrate Zoology', 'The morphology and phylogeny of representative invertebrates. Three hours lecture and three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2010 or 2030.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141887, 591515, 'BIOL', '122', 2020, 'Principles of Biology II', 'A continuation of Biology 1020. Course content provides an introduction to evolution, ecology and biological diversity. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in BIOL 1020.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 1043', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141888, 33304, 'BIOL', '4040', 2020, 'Taxonomy of Vascular Plants', 'Characteristics of plant families are emphasized. This includes classification systems and emphasis on primitive and advanced characteristics. Most of the lab is devoted to identification of plants by using keys from plant identification manuals Two hours lecture and four hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2004 or 2030.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141889, 4926, 'BIOL', '1001', 2020, 'The Living World', 'Basic scientific and biological principles with an emphasis on the structure and processes of organisms. The course also includes a survey of the major types of living organisms. Non-majors only. No prerequisite.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141890, 210279, 'AGRI', '406', 2020, 'Plant Pathology', 'A study of signs, symptoms, and syndromes as they relate to the causal agents and control of plant diseases. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: BIOL 1020, 1021, BIOL 2014. Field trip fee required. (Formerly AGRI 403, 404).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141891, 476176, 'BIOL', '209', 2020, 'Animal Diversity Laboratory', 'A laboratory course in animal diversity to accompany 208. Prerequisites: Credit or registration in 208. (Formerly Zoology 210.)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141892, 965297, 'AGRI', '301', 2020, 'Agricultural Statistics', 'Planning, conducting, and interpreting agricultural experiments, to include central tendency measures and dispersion, hypothesis, hypothesis testing, and statistical inferences as applied to agricultural data. Prerequisite: MATH 1011, 1016.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141893, 621979, 'AGRI', '4011', 2020, 'Internship in Agriculture', 'Supervised work experience with industry in the use of materials and equipment related to the student&#39;s major field of interest. Six hours maximum towards B.S. degree. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141894, 721618, 'ART', '4048', 2020, 'Special Problems: Drawing (Formerly ART 441E)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441E)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141895, 298078, 'AGRB', '2001', 2020, 'Introductory Agricultural Economics', 'Identification of resources used in agriculture. Basic concepts, principles and applications of agricultural economics to the farm operation. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. (Formerly AGEC 201)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141896, 298078, 'AGRB', '201', 2020, 'Introductory Agricultural Economics', 'Identification of resources used in agriculture. Basic concepts, principles and applications of agricultural economics to the farm operation. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. (Formerly AGEC 201)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141897, 387525, 'ART', '441', 2020, 'Special Problems', '3 credits per course. Any area may be repeated. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. A. Graphic Design; B. Ceramics; C. Painting; D. Photography; E. Drawing; F. Printing; G. Sculpture. Additional course fee may apply to certain topics.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141898, 744977, 'CHEM', '101', 2020, 'Introductory Chemistry I', 'The fundamentals of inorganic chemistry. Prerequisite: Grade of \"C\" or better in MATH 1009, or eligibility for MATH 1011 or a more advanced mathematics course. Three hours lecture. For non-majors. F, Sp, Su1\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1103', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141899, 616004, 'AGRI', '4029', 2020, 'Integrated Pest Management', 'Principles of insect pest management, identification, and control/management systems. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 1001 or 1003. (Formerly AGRI 425, 426).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141900, 616004, 'AGRI', '429', 2020, 'Integrated Pest Management', 'Principles of insect pest management, identification, and control/management systems. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: AGRI 1001 or 1003. (Formerly AGRI 425, 426).', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141901, 16716, 'AGRI', '1015', 2020, 'Agricultural Safety', 'Recognition and applied solutions as related to farm machinery, livestock, chemicals, and AGRICULTURE 139 other related agricultural hazards. Emphasis will be placed on both the ethics and liabilities associated with farm safety.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141902, 763072, 'AGRI', '4095', 2020, 'Agriculture Research', 'Student participation in research projects in the areas of A. Agriculture; B. Agriculture Economics; C. Animal Science; D. Equine Science. Two to three hours per week per credit hour. Prerequisites: Junior or senior standing in agriculture and approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141903, 645852, 'ATMS', '4060', 2020, 'Meteorology for Teachers', 'A non-mathematical introduction to meteorology designed for elementary and secondary school science teachers. The courses are a blend of lecture, demonstrations, and hands-on work and are designed to be taken in sequence (4060-4061). The courses cannot be used to satisfy degree requirements in Atmospheric Science. Prerequisite: MATH 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141904, 758261, 'AGRO', '411', 2020, 'Agricultural Chemicals', 'Herbicides, fungicides, insecticides and growth regulators and their uses. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: CHEM 1001 or 1007.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141905, 732533, 'ART', '4047', 2020, 'Special Problems: Photography (Formerly ART 441D)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441D)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141906, 22916, 'SOCL', '2007', 2020, 'Cultural Anthropology', 'A comparative study of the life and organization of human groups throughout the world, with an emphasis on traditional societies. (Formerly ANTS and SOCL 307, SOCL 300E, and GEOS 400B.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141907, 248306, 'MGMT', '3030', 2020, 'Enterprise Management', 'Students will study the application of management concepts to new and growing ventures. Analysis of organizational design, planning, implementation, and control of enterprises; social and ethical considerations in managing enterprises; and production, decision making, and behavioral factors in new and growing venture management. Prerequisite: Junior/senior standing or consent of instructor. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141908, 249342, 'SOCL', '495A', 2020, 'Teaching Children About Aging', 'An evaluation of pre-school, elementary and secondary school literature, class projects, video tapes and feature films that focus on various issues related to aging. The focus is to identify methods and mechanisms that enhance childrens images of older persons and growing older. (Formerly SOCL 495A.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141909, 888938, 'LING', '4051', 2020, 'Language and Culture', 'An overview of linguistic concepts and theories. Attention will be given to the history of language study and to the phenomenon of language acquisition from cultural and social viewpoints.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141910, 121616, 'ZOOL', '205', 2020, 'Human Anatomy and Physiology', 'Structure and function of the principal organ systems of the human body. Cannot be taken for credit if credit has been awarded for 3011 or 30 12. Non- majors only.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141911, 216686, 'CMST', '325A', 2020, 'Rhetoric & Public Address', 'Study of various communication contexts, problems, and issues in Rhetoric and Public Address. Prerequisite: COMM 2001 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3019)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141912, 216686, 'COMM', '3019', 2020, 'Rhetoric & Public Address', 'Study of various communication contexts, problems, and issues in Rhetoric and Public Address. Prerequisite: COMM 2001 or consent of instructor. (Formerly CMST 3019)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141913, 93926, 'POLS', '433', 2020, 'The Judical Process', 'Structure, functions, and operations of the judiciary. Prerequisite: 2001. (Formerly 312.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141914, 68286, 'POLS', '4040', 2020, 'Comparative', 'The structure, theory, organization, and methods of control in the governments of the major European powers; recent political trends. Prerequisite: 2001. (Formerly 305.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141915, 93926, 'GOVM', '4033', 2020, 'The Judical Process', 'Structure, functions, and operations of the judiciary. Prerequisite: 2001. (Formerly 312.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141916, 93926, 'GOVM', '433', 2020, 'The Judical Process', 'Structure, functions, and operations of the judiciary. Prerequisite: 2001. (Formerly 312.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141917, 93926, 'POLS', '4033', 2020, 'The Judical Process', 'Structure, functions, and operations of the judiciary. Prerequisite: 2001. (Formerly 312.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141918, 967005, 'RADT', '2000', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Medical Imaging', 'An overview of the foundations in imaging sciences and the practitioner&#39;s role in the health care delivery system. F, Sp', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141927, 912224, 'RADT', '1001', 2020, 'Introduction', 'An introduction to radiologic technology including historical aspects, orientation to the program and curriculum objectives. F, Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141928, 432631, 'RADT', '3014', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 313. Prerequisite: Registration in RADT 313. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141929, 432631, 'RADT', '314', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 313. Prerequisite: Registration in RADT 313. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141930, 206085, 'RADT', '3019', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures Laboratory II', 'A laboratory course to accompany RADT 3018. Prerequisite: RATE standing. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141931, 91891, 'RADT', '3018', 2020, 'Radiographic Procedures II', 'The principles and skills involved in routine radiographic positioning to demonstrate the vertebral column, cranium, gastrointestinal tract, and urinary system. Prerequisite: RATE standing. Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (141932, 887663, 'RADT', '320', 2020, 'Radiographic Exposure', 'Radiographic exposure principles: prime factors, factors influencing radiographic quality, beam restricting devices and attentuating devices. Prerequisite: RATE standing. Sp', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (141933, 560593, 'RA