als of professional responsibiity. Prerequiste: First year standing, and credit or registration in 4020.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142038, 478735, 'PHRD', '4012', 2020, 'Pathophysiology I', 'Students will be introduced to disease processes at a cellular level. Prerequisite: First year standing, and credit or registration in 4020.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142039, 478735, 'PHRD', '412', 2020, 'Pathophysiology I', 'Students will be introduced to disease processes at a cellular level. Prerequisite: First year standing, and credit or registration in 4020.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142040, 363421, 'PHRD', '458', 2020, 'Neurology and Psychiatry Module', 'Principles of pathophysiology, pharmacology, medicinal chemistry, clinical pharmacokinetics and pharmacotherapy (including both prescription and non-prescription\r\nmedications) as they apply to neurology/psychiatric drug therapy management.\r\nPrerequisites: 4027, 4035', 5.0000, 5.0000, 5.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142041, 171568, 'PHRD', '4052', 2020, 'Research Methods & Literature Evaluation', 'Introduction and application of basic concepts of research methodology and design needed for efficient evaluation, utilization, and clincial application of medication information available in medical literature. Prerequisites: PHRD 4033', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142042, 745263, 'PHRD', '4035', 2020, 'Pathophysiology II', 'The student will continue to build on the knowledge from pathophysiology I as complete organ systems are introduced and the impact of diseases on these systems are studied. Prerequisties: PHRD 4012', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142043, 70889, 'PHRD', '433', 2020, 'Drug Information Retrieval', 'Orientation to current drug information systems, appropriate search strategies utilizing primary, secondary and tertiary resources combined with applications of common statistical tests seen in medical literature. Prerequisite: P1 Status', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142044, 50949, 'PHRD', '456', 2020, 'Biopharmaceutics and Pharmacokinetics', 'The study of the interrelationship between formulation factors and pharmacokinetic aspects of drug absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion. Prerequisites: PHRD 4002, 4008', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142045, 453815, 'PHRD', '4054', 2020, 'Introduction to Communications', 'Orientation to psychosocial and communication principles and techniques with application to professional practice environments and clinical counseling situations. Prerequisites: PHRD 4010, 4031, 4033', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142046, 453815, 'PHRD', '454', 2020, 'Introduction to Communications', 'Orientation to psychosocial and communication principles and techniques with application to professional practice environments and clinical counseling situations. Prerequisites: PHRD 4010, 4031, 4033', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142047, 709843, 'PHRD', '4049', 2020, 'Integrated Lab Sequence II', 'Second in a six-semester longitudinal course sequence reinforcing students&#39; knowledge, skills, and attitudes necessary for current and future pharmacy practice. Focus on immunology, drug action, therapeutics, pharaceutics, law/ethics, informatics, pathophysiology, and parenterals. Prerequsites: 420, and credit or registration in 4025, 4027, 4029, 4031, 4033, 4035, 4047.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142048, 895089, 'PHRD', '481', 2020, 'Infectious Diseases Module', 'Principles of pathophysiology, pharmacology, medicinal chemistry, clinical pharmacokinetics and pharmacotherapy (including both prescription and non-prescription medications) as they apply to infectious diseases drug therapy management. Prerequisites: 4025, 4027, 4035, 4056', 6.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142049, 8869, 'PHRD', '499', 2020, 'Integrated Lab Sequence IV', 'Fourth in a 6 semester Longitudinal course sequence reinforcing students knowledge, skills, and attitudes necessary for current and future pharmacy practice. Focus on health-care systems, self-care; patient assessment, infectious diseases, and\r\nGastrointestinal/nutritional/hepatic disorders. Prerequisites: 4070,\r\ncredit/registration in 4077, 4079, 4081, 4083.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142050, 729866, 'PHRD', '470', 2020, 'Integrated Lab Sequence III', 'Third in a 6-semester Longitudinal course sequence reinforcing students knowledge, skills, and attitudes necessary for current and future pharmacy practice. Focus on drug literature evaluation, communications, biopharmaceutics/pharmacokinetics,\r\nneurologic/psychiatric, and endocrinologic disorders. Prerequisites: 4049, credit/\r\nregistration in 4052, 4054, 4056, 4058, 4074', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142051, 558906, 'PHRD', '479', 2020, 'Self Care / Patient Assessment I', 'Basic patient assessment skills required in the delivery of pharmaceutical care and principles of self care including: determining if self care is appropriate and recommending appropriate self care treatment. Prerequisite: 4010', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142056, 662640, 'PHRD', '4002', 2020, 'Principles of Drug Action I', 'This course focuses on the molecular-level composition of living organisms in relationship to the biochemical and molecular biopharmaceutical bases of therapeutic intervention with medicinal substances, and associated foundational concepts of medicinal and pharmaceutical chemistry, pharmacology, and toxicology. Prerequisites: Credit or registration in 4020.', 5.0000, 5.0000, 5.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142062, 149782, 'CONS', '101', 2020, 'Construction Materials', 'Materials of construction, their properties, manufacture, characteristics and use. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142065, 34513, 'MLSC', '3040', 2020, 'Medical Laboratory Science Capstone', 'Seminar and management course that includes oral and written presentations of research on current topics related to laboratory medicine. Laboratory management topics are analyzed using case studies and group exercises. Regulations and laws that impact the clinical laboratory are discussed. MLSC majors only. (Formerly CLSC 340)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142068, 150717, 'PHYS', '2008', 2020, 'University Physics II', 'This is a calculus-based physics class involving the principles and applications of electricity, magnetism, and light. For students who will pursue science and engineering. Prerequisite: PHYS 2007. Sp<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CPHY 2153', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142069, 150717, 'PHYS', '208', 2020, 'University Physics II', 'This is a calculus-based physics class involving the principles and applications of electricity, magnetism, and light. For students who will pursue science and engineering. Prerequisite: PHYS 2007. Sp<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CPHY 2153', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142079, 877235, 'SOCW', '3017', 2020, 'Group Work', 'Examines various theoretical approaches to social work practice with groups, basic skills involved in leadership and group development, and the fundamentals of the dynamics and processes in social group work. Prerequisite: SOCW 301 or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142080, 877235, 'SOCW', '317', 2020, 'Group Work', 'Examines various theoretical approaches to social work practice with groups, basic skills involved in leadership and group development, and the fundamentals of the dynamics and processes in social group work. Prerequisite: SOCW 301 or approval of program director.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142081, 702510, 'SPCH', '4091A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Rhetoric and Public Address (Formerly CMST 491A)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisites: Approval of department head. (Formerly CMST 491A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142082, 702510, 'CMST', '4092', 2020, 'Directed Study: Rhetoric and Public Address (Formerly CMST 491A)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisites: Approval of department head. (Formerly CMST 491A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142083, 702510, 'CMST', '491A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Rhetoric and Public Address (Formerly CMST 491A)', 'May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisites: Approval of department head. (Formerly CMST 491A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142084, 128440, 'POLS', '4092', 2020, 'Directed Study: National, State, and Local (Formerly 491A)', 'Directed study and/or research in selected areas of government. Prerequisite: Advanced standing, approval of department head, and permission of the instructor. (Formerly 491A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142085, 944485, 'AVIA', '4093', 2020, 'Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Management (Formerly AVIA 491B)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Management. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142086, 944485, 'AVIA', '491B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Management (Formerly AVIA 491B)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Directed Study: Problems of Aviation Management. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491B)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142087, 664052, 'EDFN', '4030C', 2020, 'Special Topics: Comparative Education', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A. Study of International Education on Location; B. Study of United States School Systems on Location; C. Comparative Education; D. Evaluation in Education; E. Educational Technology and Media.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142088, 537239, 'EDFN', '4030D', 2020, 'Special Topics: Evaluation in Education', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A. Study of International Education on Location; B. Study of United States School Systems on Location; C. Comparative Education; D. Evaluation in Education; E. Educational Technology and Media.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142089, 475579, 'EDFN', '4030E', 2020, 'Special Topics: Educational Technology and Media', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A. Study of International Education on Location; B. Study of United States School Systems on Location; C. Comparative Education; D. Evaluation in Education; E. Educational Technology and Media.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142090, 299040, 'EDFN', '4036', 2020, 'Educational Data Processing', 'Principles of electronic data processing in education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142093, 63491, 'FCSC', '104', 2020, 'Clothing Basics', 'Planning, selection, and care of clothing for the family with special emphasis on budgeting and needs of various family members at different life stages.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142095, 902645, 'TOXI', '1001', 2020, 'Toxicology and the Environment', 'This class will provide an introduction to the field of toxicology and illustrate the relationships between chemicals, man and the environment. Historical and contemporary &quot;case studies&quot; of contamination episodes will be used to highlight the various factors involved in evaluating and controlling chemical hazards. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142096, 609480, 'NURS', '2017', 2020, 'Concepts of Nursing and Health Care', 'Introduction to professional nursing, nursing history, theories, therapeutic communication techniques, and health promotion throughout the life span. Prerequisite: Registration or credit in NURS 2016.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142097, 315402, 'GOVM', '4054', 2020, 'Congress and the Presidency', 'A course focused on two of the three major institutional components of American politics. Main topics include the history of the Congress and Presidency (i.e., the two institutions structural, behavioral and institutional adaptation to a changing America), the internal and external dynamics of public policy production (i.e., how demands arising in the electorate and elsewhere are conveyed to and/or produced within the Congress and the translation of these demands into specific laws and policies), and, the complex interaction between the Congress and the Presidency as different and separate institutions sharing power. Prerequisite: POLS 2001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142098, 76430, 'HLST', '4004', 2020, 'Healthcare Emergency Preparedness', 'The student will acquire basic health care emergency preparedness knowledge relevant to the needs of a healhcare professional during natural, technological, and man made disasters, and will identify adequate measures to be taken in the event of acute illness. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142099, 851801, 'PSYC', '2000A', 2020, 'Discovering Psychology', 'An introductory survey of the field of psychology. Students with prior credit in Psychology 201 are not eligible to receive credit in Psychology 200A.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142100, 335728, 'PSYC', '4005', 2020, 'Mental Retardation', 'Recognition, diagnosis, and etiology of mental retardation. Emphasis on psychological theories, procedures, and application. Prerequisites: PSYC 201, 203. (Formerly The Mentally Retarded Child.) F, Su', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142101, 412267, 'AGEC', '3007', 2020, 'Advanced Agricultural Marketing', 'Fundamental concepts of forward pricing. Introduction to forward contracting, the futures market, and options on agricultural futures. Emphasis is placed on forward pricing as a tool to reduce price risk. (Formerly AGEC 207) Prerequisite: Minimum grades of &quot;C&quot; in AGRB 1001, 2001, and 2003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142102, 434333, 'NURS', '4035', 2020, 'Health Assessment & Health Maintenance of the Aging Patient', 'A study to impart concepts of the nursing processes as they relate to health assessment and health maintenance of the aging person. Principles of history-taking and physical examination and assessment skills are emphasized as they pertain to the aging patient. The focus is directed toward the assessment of physiological, environmental, sociological, and psychological needs in the aging patient. Prerequisite: NURS 2004', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142103, 652273, 'AGEC', '203', 2020, 'Agricultural Marketing', 'The principles and methods of marketing agricultural products and the institutions performing the various functions in the marketing of various commodities. Current trends and developments in the agricultural marketing process. (Formerly AGEC 203)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142104, 313387, 'ATMS', '3003', 2020, 'Atmospheric Thermodynamics', 'Introduction to classical and statistical thermodynamics as it applies to dry and moist atmospheric phenomena. Ideal Gas Law, First and Second Laws of Thermodynamics. Thermodynamic potentials and diagrams. Moisture variables. Prerequisites: ATMS 2005, and credit or registration in MATH 1031 and PHYS 2007.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142107, 386700, 'SPLP', '4004', 2020, 'Multicultural Issues in Clinical Service Delivery', 'The nature of deafness and hard of hearing problems. Focus is on professional\r\nprocedures facilitating adequate communication in persons with hearing impairments. (Prereq: SPLP 1013,1052, 2001, 2002) (Formerly SPLP 445)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142108, 75925, 'SPLP', '4026', 2020, 'Diagnosis and Appraisal of Communication Disorders', 'Instruments, procedures, and report writing skills utilized in diagnosing and reporting speech, language, and hearing disorders. Enrollment in 427 is required. Prerequisite: 113 and consent of instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142109, 612712, 'GEOS', '4015', 2020, 'Soils for the Environmental Geoscientist', 'Fundamentals of pedology aimed at environmental geoscientists, including: soil terminology, soil genesis, the 7th Approximation soil classification system, the use of parish and county soil surveys, soil descriptions, soil toxicity, national and worldwide soil type distribution. Prerequisite: GEOL 101 or GEOG 213 or permission of the instructor.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142111, 291010, 'MRKT', '4001', 2020, 'International', 'All phases of marketing as applied in an international operation: research, marketing channels, promotion, financing, pricing, licensing, organization requirements, and methods of coordination. Prerequisite: MRKT 3001. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142112, 291010, 'MRKT', '401', 2020, 'International', 'All phases of marketing as applied in an international operation: research, marketing channels, promotion, financing, pricing, licensing, organization requirements, and methods of coordination. Prerequisite: MRKT 3001. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142113, 268615, 'OCCT', '1006', 2020, 'Pathology', 'Introduction to physical pathological conditions commonly encountered in the practice of occupational therapy. Prerequisite: 2.5 overall GPA (uncorrected). OCTA majors only. Su II', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142114, 268615, 'OCCT', '106', 2020, 'Pathology', 'Introduction to physical pathological conditions commonly encountered in the practice of occupational therapy. Prerequisite: 2.5 overall GPA (uncorrected). OCTA majors only. Su II', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142116, 89049, 'ATMS', '103', 2020, 'Basic Meteorology Laboratory I', 'A laboratory course designed to expose students to basic uses of meteorological data from the surface, upper air, radars, and satellites. Topics include surface and upper-air map analysis, fronts and cyclones, and severe weather.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142117, 635458, 'ENTR', '4035', 2020, 'Family and Closely Held Businesses', 'Practical considerations associated with family businesses. Focus on unique opportunities and problems of managing family business through the business life cycle, such as founder stage, training children, bringing children into the business, and managing for succession. Prerequisite: Junior standing or consent of instructor. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142118, 635458, 'MGMT', '3033', 2020, 'Family and Closely Held Businesses', 'Practical considerations associated with family businesses. Focus on unique opportunities and problems of managing family business through the business life cycle, such as founder stage, training children, bringing children into the business, and managing for succession. Prerequisite: Junior standing or consent of instructor. F', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142120, 907668, 'ANTG', '421', 2020, 'The Archeology of Mexico', 'An in-depth view of the development of pre-Hispanic Mexican and Meso-American cultures and civilizations from Paleo-Indian times to the Spanish Conquest; an overview of the major archeological sites pertinent to these cultures. (Same as GEOG 4021.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142121, 17424, 'ANTG', '4010', 2020, 'Archeology of Louisiana Indians', 'An introduction to the archeology of Louisianas Indian tribes from Paleo-Indian times (10,000 B.C.) through the historic period. Prerequisite: Junior or senior standing or permission of the instructor. (Same as GEOG 4010.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142122, 13956, 'CHEM', '4024', 2020, 'Directed Study: Biochemistry', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A directed study for undergraduates and graduates. May include laboratory and/or library work. Four to six hours per week for each credit hour earned. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Su1, Su2 (Formerly CHEM 422B)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142123, 38077, 'CHEM', '4022', 2020, 'Directed Study', '1-6 credits; maximum, 6 credits. A directed study for undergraduates and graduates. May include laboratory and/or library work in the areas of A. Analytical; B. Biochemistry; C. Inorganic; D. Organic; E. Physica