ailable at this time.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142261, 506316, 'FCSC', '4015C', 2020, 'Problems: Family Relations and Human Devel', '1-6 credits; maximum, 12 credits. Problems in A. Clothing and Textiles; B. Equipment and Home Management; C. Family Relations and Human Development; D. Foods and Nutrition; E. Family and Consumer Sciences Education; and F. Housing and Home Furnishings. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142262, 829509, 'FCSC', '4015B', 2020, 'Problems: Equipment and Home Manageme', '1-6 credits; maximum, 12 credits. Problems in A. Clothing and Textiles; B. Equipment and Home Management; C. Family Relations and Human Development; D. Foods and Nutrition; E. Family and Consumer Sciences Education; and F. Housing and Home Furnishings. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 6.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142272, 854294, 'FINA', '4092', 2020, 'Directed Study: Banking', 'Individual study. May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly FINA 491A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142273, 854294, 'FINA', '491A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Banking', 'Individual study. May be repeated for a total of 6 crs. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly FINA 491A)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142276, 706972, 'GRMN', '1001', 2020, 'Elementary German I', 'An introduction to the basic grammatical structures of German with the objectives of developing an elementary ability to speak, understand, read and write the language. Language laboratory required.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CGRM 1013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142278, 831567, 'GEOG', '1001', 2020, 'Regional Geography', 'A regional approach to the study of human geography, with emphasis on spatial distributions, interactions, and processes on the earth&#39;s surface. The geographical study of the major realms are divided as follows: GEOG 1001 covers Europe (including Russia), North America, and North Africa/Middle East and GEOG 1002 covers Latin America, Sub-Saharan Africa, and Asia.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142281, 381020, 'GERO', '456D', 2020, 'International Studies: Far East (Formerly GERO 456D)', 'Extended gerontology field study outside the United States with guest lectures, visits to gerontological related facilities and programs, and assigned readings related to aging in the designated study region. (Formerly GERO 456D)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142282, 59452, 'GERO', '456', 2020, 'International Studies', 'Extended gerontology field study outside the United States with guest lectures, visits to gerontological related facilities and programs, and assigned readings related to aging in the designated study region. A. Europe, B. England, C. Latin America, D. Far East, E. Middle East. Individual topics may not be repeated for credit.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142283, 59452, 'GERO', '4056', 2020, 'International Studies', 'Extended gerontology field study outside the United States with guest lectures, visits to gerontological related facilities and programs, and assigned readings related to aging in the designated study region. A. Europe, B. England, C. Latin America, D. Far East, E. Middle East. Individual topics may not be repeated for credit.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142296, 680336, 'KINS', '491D', 2020, 'Directed Study: Selected Topics', 'Directed study and/or research of A. Health; B. Kinesiology; C. Athletic Injuries; D. Selected Topics. A maximum of six credit hours may be taken. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142298, 237220, 'KINS', '491', 2020, 'Directed Study', 'Directed study and/or research of A. Health; B. Kinesiology; C. Athletic Injuries; D. Selected Topics. A maximum of six credit hours may be taken. Prerequisite: Approval of department head.', 1.0