 Meso-American cultures and civilizations from Paleo-Indian times to the Spanish Conquest; an overview of the major archeological sites pertinent to these cultures. (Same as GEOG 4021.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142762, 786679, 'ANTG', '4023', 2020, 'Archeological Field Techniques', 'A field course introducing the basic techniques of archeological mapping, excavation, cataloging, specimen preparation and preservation. A study of soils, physical stratigraphy, synecology, and techniques of artifact laboratory analysis. May be repeated once for a maximum of 12 hours credit. (Same as ANTG 4023.)', 6.0000, 6.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142763, 713971, 'ANTS', '2007', 2020, 'Cultural Anthropology', 'A comparative study of the life and organization of human groups throughout the world, with an emphasis on traditional societies. (Formerly ANTS and SOCL 307, SOCL 300E, and GEOS 400B).<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CATR 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142764, 713971, 'ANTS', '207', 2020, 'Cultural Anthropology', 'A comparative study of the life and organization of human groups throughout the world, with an emphasis on traditional societies. (Formerly ANTS and SOCL 307, SOCL 300E, and GEOS 400B).<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CATR 2013', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142765, 828592, 'ANTS', '4022', 2020, 'Latin America: Peoples and Institutions', 'Description of indigenous social organizations prior to conquest. Survey of community ethnographic studies of African, Amerind, Asiatic and European cultures in contemporary rural and urban Latin America. Prerequisite: Sociology 3007 or approval of department head. (Same as SOCL 4022.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142766, 117467, 'ANTS', '4030', 2020, 'Belief Systems', 'The relationship between pre-literate belief systems and social structure; myths of creation, life cycle crisis, rites of passage, purity and pollution, witchcraft and supernatural illness. (Same as SOCL 4030.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142767, 117467, 'ANTS', '430', 2020, 'Belief Systems', 'The relationship between pre-literate belief systems and social structure; myths of creation, life cycle crisis, rites of passage, purity and pollution, witchcraft and supernatural illness. (Same as SOCL 4030.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142768, 800097, 'GEOG', '1011', 2020, 'Human Origins and Evolution', 'The study of the origin of and biogenetic heritage of humans; a survey of modern human radial variation; an introduction to archeological and per-historic techniques of investigation regarding the changing physical form of humans. (Same as ANTG 1011).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142769, 349610, 'ART', '104', 2020, 'Figure Drawing', 'Drawing made from models. Six hours studio. Prerequisite: 1003. Additional Course Fee .\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CART 2213', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142770, 62817, 'ARAB', '401', 2020, 'Practicum in Arabic', 'Application of language skills in a foreign language environment. Students will be involved in a total immersion living situation and will receive a minimum of fifteen clock hours per week in formal language instruction. May be repeated with permission of the department head. Prerequisite: Arabic 2002 or permission of the Department Head.', 3.0000, 12.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142771, 850151, 'SOCL', '233', 2020, 'Forensics', 'An overview of techniques applied in identification of human skeletal remains for the medicolegal professions, including assessment of age, sex, ancestry, trauma, and disease; occupational stress markers; procedures for search/recovery of human remains; and estimations of time since death (same as ANTS and CJUS 2033).', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142772, 245955, 'CHEM', '351', 2020, 'Biochemistry Laboratory I', 'Laboratory to accompany Biochemistry I. Introduction to procedures used in Biochemistry Laboratory. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisites: Credit or registration in CHEM 3050 and \"C\" or better in CHEM 2033. F<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 3401', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142773, 442391, 'ART', '257', 2020, 'Lithography', 'Printing process with Bavarian limestone. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1001, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142774, 584620, 'ART', '258', 2020, 'Block Printing', 'Printing process in wood and linoleum. One hour lecture and 5 hours studio. Prerequisite: 1001, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142775, 182756, 'ART', '259', 2020, 'Etching', 'Printing process with zinc plates. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1001, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142776, 520031, 'ART', '260', 2020, 'Silkscreen', 'Printing process with stencil techniques. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1001, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142777, 34176, 'ART', '2072', 2020, 'Painting', 'Painting in oils. Six hours studio. Prerequisites: 101, 104 or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142778, 39403, 'ART', '4031', 2020, 'Watercolor', 'Painting in watercolor. Prerequisites: 101, 103, or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142779, 213675, 'ART', '281', 2020, 'Sculpture', 'Sculpture problems in a variety of media. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1002, 1004 or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142780, 95875, 'ART', '356', 2020, 'Advanced Color Photography', 'Theory and practice of advanced color photography for the creative photographer. Prerequisites: Art 2046, 2056, or permission of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142781, 10917, 'ART', '381', 2020, 'Intermediate Sculpture', 'Further development of sculptural processes and techniques in a variety of media. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2081. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142782, 741542, 'ART', '401', 2020, 'Advanced Ceramics', '3 credits, maximum, 12 credits. Origin and properties of ceramics raw materials and problems in glaze research. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2003 or 2004. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142783, 716423, 'ART', '402', 2020, 'Creating Paper / Casting and Molding', 'Study and processing of basic skills in creating paper from laminations to cast paper. One hour lecture, 5 hours laboratory per week. Prerequisite: 1001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142784, 135662, 'ART', '404', 2020, 'Advanced Drawing', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Advanced drawing. Primarily life drawing in a variety of media. Six hours studio. Prerequisite: 1004. (Formerly 303.) Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142785, 632895, 'ART', '405', 2020, 'Advanced Graphic Design', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Design problems to develop professional studio skills and practices in graphic design. Develop methods of problem solving with specific production limitations. Methods of presentation. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2006. (Formerly 305; Advanced Advertising Design 405.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142786, 895563, 'ART', '406', 2020, 'Computer Art', 'Decision making with the graphic computer, creation to production. Computer-aided visual design including image origination as well as input, output, selection, editing, alteration, and manipulation. Prerequisites: Art 1001, 1003; Computer Science 1070, or approval of department head. Six hours studio.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142787, 562672, 'ART', '426', 2020, 'Nineteenth Century', 'Nineteenth Century European and American Rococo through Post-Impressionism periods. Prerequisites: 2001, 2002, or approval of the department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142788, 492949, 'ART', '429', 2020, 'Contemporary', 'Twentieth century European and American Art. A study of the major achievements in painting, sculpture, and architecture since 1900. Prerequisite: 2001, 2002. (Formerly 329.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142789, 912282, 'ART', '440', 2020, 'Metalcraft and Jewelrymaking', 'The designing and fabrication of jewelry and small metal products. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 1002 or approval of department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142790, 659884, 'BIOL', '403A', 2020, 'Problems: Anatomy / Physiology (Formerly BIOL 403A)', 'Problems: Anatomy / Physiology. 1-6 credits, maximum 6 cr. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly BIOL 403A)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142791, 408313, 'ART', '443F', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Women Artists (Formerly ART 443F)', 'Seminar in Art History: Women Artists. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443F)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142792, 408313, 'ART', '4065', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Women Artists (Formerly ART 443F)', 'Seminar in Art History: Women Artists. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443F)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142793, 724021, 'ART', '443C', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Far Eastern (Formerly ART 443C)', 'Seminar in Art History: Far Eastern. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443C)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142794, 89033, 'ART', '443G', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Surrealism in Art (Formerly ART 443G)', 'Seminar in Art History: Surrealism in Art. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443G)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142795, 759797, 'ART', '443B', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Baroque (Formerly ART 443B)', 'Seminar in Art History: Baroque. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142796, 897931, 'AGRI', '4097', 2020, 'Equine Science (Formerly AGRI 491E)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Individualized work on special problems. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly AGRI 491E)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142797, 167199, 'ART', '443H', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: History of Photography (Formerly ART 443H)', 'Seminar in Art History: History of Photography. Prequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443H)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142798, 198923, 'AVIA', '491A', 2020, 'Directed Study: Aviation Course Construction (Formerly AVIA 491A)', 'Maximum, 6 cr. Directed Study: Aviation Course Construction. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142799, 574950, 'AVIA', '491D', 2020, 'Directed Study: Aviation / Inter-Modal Transportation (Formerly AVIA 491D)', 'Directed Study: Aviation / Inter-Modal Transportation. Maximum, 6 cr. Prerequisite: Junior or Senior Aviation major. (Formerly AVIA 491D)', 1.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142800, 102415, 'ART', '443D', 2020, 'Seminar in Art History: Theory (Formerly ART 443D)', 'Seminar in Art History: Theory. Prerequisites: Art 2001, 2002, or approval of department head. (Formerly ART 443D)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142801, 388726, 'ART', '455', 2020, 'Advanced Photography', 'Maximum, 12 hrs. Individual instruction in planning and executing a personal response to the visual elements and creative composition. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 2046.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142802, 285153, 'ART', '481', 2020, 'Advanced Sculpture', 'Maximum, 12 cr. Advanced problems in sculptural processes and techniques. Emphasis upon individual creative expression. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 3081. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142803, 58536, 'CLSC', '3038', 2020, 'Directed Study', '1-6 credits each. Individual investigation of selected problems in: A. Urinalysis; B. Hematology; C. Immunology; D. Blood Banking; E. Serology; F. Clinical Chemistry; H. Toxicology; J. Other associated areas of clinical laboratory science; K. Parasitology; and L. Clinical Laboratory Management. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142804, 212542, 'ASCI', '205', 2020, 'Practical Work With Livestock', 'Dehorning, castration, methods of restraint, fitting for show, etc. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: ASCI 101.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142805, 926967, 'ASCI', '307', 2020, 'Animal Physiology', 'An introduction to the study of veterinary science, dealing with the fundamental physiological processes of farm animals. Prerequisites: ASCI 101, BIOL 120, 121, CHEM 101, 103 or 107, 109.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142806, 128316, 'ART', '441C', 2020, 'Special Problems: Painting (Formerly ART 441C)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441C)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142807, 637723, 'ASCI', '323', 2020, 'Livestock Feeding', 'Chemical composition of feeds, requirements of animals, utilization of nutrients, formulating and balancing rations. Prerequisites: ASCI 101, CHEM 101, 103 or 107, 109, MATH 110 or 111.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142808, 77640, 'ASCI', '325', 2020, 'Genetics', 'Fundamental concepts of heredity at the molecular, cellular, organismic, and population levels. Nature of the genetic material and its involvement in the determination of structure and function. Consideration given to both classical and modern genetics. Prerequisites: BIOL 120, 121; CHEM 101, 103.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142809, 655141, 'AGRI', '495A', 2020, 'Agricultural Research: Agriculture (Formerly AGRI 495A)', 'Student participation in research projects in the areas of Agriculture. Two to three hours per week per credit hour. Prerequisites: Junior or senior standing in agriculture and approval of department head. (Formerly AGRI 495A)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142810, 14727, 'ASCI', '407', 2020, 'Meat Processing and Preservation', 'The factors involved in dressing percentage and output values of carcasses, cutting, curing, and handling of meat products. One hour lecture and four hours laboratory. Prerequisite: ASCI 101.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142811, 254971, 'ASCI', '430', 2020, 'Artificial Insemination & Embryo Transfer', 'Development and use of artificial insemination and embryo transfer techniques in modern livestock breeding programs. Two hours lecture and two hours laboratory. Prerequisites: ASCI 101, 341, CHEM 101 or 107, MATH 110 or 111.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142812, 98039, 'ASCI', '405', 2020, 'Practical Livestock Handling', 'Handling of livestock for sale, show, and general management procedures. Three hours laboratory. Prerequisite: ASCI 101.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142813, 435758, 'ATMS', '1010', 2020, 'Microcomputers in Meteorology', 'Two hours of laboratory work learning to operate personal computer systems dealing with meteorological data. Discussions will consider data distribution, reception and archival; IBM operating systems; Weathercapture software; DIFAX; and the PC-McIDAS network.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142814, 228672, 'ATMS', '3005', 2020, 'Dynamic Meteorology', 'Introduction to atmospheric kinematics, dynamics, and coordinate systems. Fundamental forces; equations of motion; scale analysis; mass conservation; geostrophic and thermal winds, idealized flows; circulation and vorticity. Prerequisites: PHYS 2007 and credit or registration in 3003 and MATH 2032.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142815, 957268, 'ATMS', '3007', 2020, 'Meteorology Lab', 'Two hours of laboratory to accompany 3005. The application of techniques, charts and diagrams in the analysis and study of meteorological practices and phenomena. Prerequisites: ATMS 2005 and credit or registration in ATMS 3005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142816, 957268, 'ATMS', '307', 2020, 'Meteorology Lab', 'Two hours of laboratory to accompany 3005. The application of techniques, charts and diagrams in the analysis and study of meteorological practices and phenomena. Prerequisites: ATMS 2005 and credit or registration in ATMS 3005.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142817, 445454, 'ATMS', '306', 2020, 'Dynamic Meteorology II', 'Application in kinematics, dynamics, and thermodynamics in diagnosing synoptic-scale weather systems. Quasi-geostrophic theory; cyclogenesis and frontogenesis; jet dynamics, linear perturbation theory; atmospheric waves, baroclinic instability. Prerequisites: C or better in 3003 and 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142818, 445454, 'ATMS', '3006', 2020, 'Dynamic Meteorology II', 'Application in kinematics, dynamics, and thermodynamics in diagnosing synoptic-scale weather systems. Quasi-geostrophic theory; cyclogenesis and frontogenesis; jet dynamics, linear perturbation theory; atmospheric waves, baroclinic instability. Prerequisites: C or better in 3003 and 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142819, 905696, 'ATMS', '3008', 2020, 'Meteorology Laboratory', 'Two hours of laboratory to accompany 3006. The application of techniques, charts and diagrams in the analysis and study of meteorological practices and phenomena. Prerequisites: ATMS 2005 and credit or registration in ATMS 3006.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142820, 365011, 'ATMS', '360', 2020, 'Human and Atmosphere Interaction', 'An interdisciplinary course that serves as the atmospheric sciences and University Capstone. Projects focus on anthropogenic impacts on and interaction with the atmosphere or impacts of the atmosphere on humans. Prerequisites: All core curriculum courses, ATMS 2005, and junior standing.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142821, 951181, 'ATMS', '315', 2020, 'Physical Meteorology', 'Introduction to physical principles underlying atmospheric radiation, cloud physics and precipitation processes. Prerequisite: ATMS 3003 and PHYS 2008.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142822, 29457, 'ATMS', '350', 2020, 'Special Topics in Operational Meterology', 'Provides the students with work experience at a National Weather Service Forecast Office. Grade of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Prerequisites: ATMS 3003, and credit or registration in ATMS 3005.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142823, 3081879, 'ATMS', '4004', 2020, 'Mesoscale Meteorology', 'Application of dynamics, thermodynamics, and forecasting techniques in diagnosing the organization of mesoscale and convective phenomena. Mesoscale instabilities; air mass boundaries; boundary layer dynamics; low-level jets; severe thunderstorms; tornadoes; mesoscale convective systems; mountain waves. Prerequisites: ATMS 3006 and ATMS 4003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142824, 614077, 'ATMS', '4011', 2020, 'Tropical Meteorology', 'An examination of the structure and dynamics of the tropical atmosphere. Convection in the tropics, tropical cyclones (hurricanes) and an introduction to monsoon circulation. \r\nPrerequisites: PHYS 2007 and credit or registration in ATMS 3003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142825, 614077, 'ATMS', '411', 2020, 'Tropical Meteorology', 'An examination of the structure and dynamics of the tropical atmosphere. Convection in the tropics, tropical cyclones (hurricanes) and an introduction to monsoon circulation. \r\nPrerequisites: PHYS 2007 and credit or registration in ATMS 3003.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142826, 308942, 'ATMS', '4002', 2020, 'Synoptic Meteorology', 'Analysis of synoptic weather charts and thermodynamic diagrams in the Weather Research Center. Enphasis is on understanding the three-dimensional structure of the atmosphere, interpretation of surface, upper air, radar, meteorological satellite weather data, and National Weather Service products received in the Weather Research Center. Prerequisites: 3006, 3008, 4001.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142827, 18562, 'ATMS', '1006', 2020, 'Introduction to Climate Change', 'An introduction to the Earth\'s Climate and components of the climate system. Topics include the Earth system, past climates, natural and anthropogenic climate change.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142828, 3582023, 'ATMS', '2000', 2020, 'Weather Analysis and Forecasting', 'Introduction to short-range weather prediction and scalar analysis practices at the synoptic, regional, and local scale. Weather observing techniques; temperature and precipitation forecasting concepts and practice; weather map analysis and discussions; numerical guidance; soundings and stability. Prerequisite; ATMS 1003, MATH 1013.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142829, 760196, 'GEOS', '3032', 2020, 'Broadcast Meteorology Practicum', 'Systematic research, training, and active participation in meteorological/climatological laboratory 2-6 hours/week at a television weather\r\nstation. Grade of CR (Credit) or NC (No Credit) will be awarded. Can serve as\r\ncredit for an atmospheric sciences elective. \r\nPrerequisites: Credit or registration in ATMS 2005 and sophomore standing.', 1.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142830, 435110, 'ATMS', '4015', 2020, 'Micrometeorology', 'Introduction to the physical processes in the atmospheric surface boundary layer. Influence of low level atmospheric turbulence on the diffusion of heat, water vapor (evaporation), and atmospheric pollutants. Prerequisites: ATMS 3006 and 3015.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142831, 630677, 'RMIN', '2005', 2020, 'Risk and Insurance', 'A study of pure risk and risk- bearing, including insurance and non-insurance methods of handling risks; introduction to life, disability, property, marine, and liability insurance. F,Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142832, 630677, 'INSU', '2005', 2020, 'Risk and Insurance', 'A study of pure risk and risk- bearing, including insurance and non-insurance methods of handling risks; introduction to life, disability, property, marine, and liability insurance. F,Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142833, 365232, 'ATMS', '450', 2020, 'Atmospheric Pollution', 'A study of elements, effects and meteorology of air pollution including the &quot;Greenhouse&quot; effect, acid rain, and ozone depletion problems. Air pollution modeling and prediction is also covered. Prerequisites: Completion of freshman mathematics requirements and CHEM 1007.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142834, 586405, 'ZOOL', '209', 2020, 'Animal Diversity', 'The anatomy, physiology, and classification of animals with an emphasis on animal diversity. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in 120, 121.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142835, 586405, 'BIOL', '2008', 2020, 'Animal Diversity', 'The anatomy, physiology, and classification of animals with an emphasis on animal diversity. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in 120, 121.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142836, 586405, 'BIOL', '208', 2020, 'Animal Diversity', 'The anatomy, physiology, and classification of animals with an emphasis on animal diversity. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in 120, 121.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142837, 444603, 'ATMS', '461', 2020, 'Meteorology for Teachers', 'A non-mathematical introduction to meteorology designed for elementary and secondary school science teachers. The courses are a blend of lecture, demonstrations, and hands-on work and are designed to be taken in sequence (4060-4061). The courses cannot be used to satisfy degree requirements in Atmospheric Science. Prerequisite: ATMS 4060.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142838, 981897, 'AVIA', '223', 2020, 'Instrument Pilot Ground School', 'Advanced instrument procedures, departure, en-route and approach procedures, precision and non-precision approaches; GPS en-route approach procedures, review and preparation for taking the FAA Instrument Written Exam. Prerequisite: 2020 or permission of program coordinator.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142839, 428807, 'AVIA', '402', 2020, 'Air Traffic Administration', 'The National Aerospace System. The role of Air Traffic Control in aviation safety. For Aviation Majors. Prerequisites: 1010, 1011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142840, 320911, 'AVIA', '413', 2020, 'Instrument Flight Instructor Ground School', 'Instructional knowledge required for FAA instrument rating on flight instructor certificate. Prerequisite: 4011.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142841, 566877, 'AVIA', '4016', 2020, 'Aircraft Engines and Systems', 'Advanced aircraft engines and systems of a typical large twin pressurized turboprop, including warning systems, doors, electrical, lighting, fuel, engines, fire protection, hydraulics, flight controls, stall warnings, avionics, TCAS, EGPWS, communications, landing gear, pneumatics, air conditioning, pressurization, oxygen, ice protection, APU, and emergency equipment. Prerequisite: minimum grade of &quot;C&quot; in 1010 and 1011, completion of all 100-level English and Math courses, or instructor approval...', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142842, 566877, 'AVIA', '415', 2020, 'Aircraft Engines and Systems', 'Advanced aircraft engines and systems of a typical large twin pressurized turboprop, including warning systems, doors, electrical, lighting, fuel, engines, fire protection, hydraulics, flight controls, stall warnings, avionics, TCAS, EGPWS, communications, landing gear, pneumatics, air conditioning, pressurization, oxygen, ice protection, APU, and emergency equipment. Prerequisite: minimum grade of &quot;C&quot; in 1010 and 1011, completion of all 100-level English and Math courses, or instructor approval...', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142843, 566877, 'AVIA', '416', 2020, 'Aircraft Engines and Systems', 'Advanced aircraft engines and systems of a typical large twin pressurized turboprop, including warning systems, doors, electrical, lighting, fuel, engines, fire protection, hydraulics, flight controls, stall warnings, avionics, TCAS, EGPWS, communications, landing gear, pneumatics, air conditioning, pressurization, oxygen, ice protection, APU, and emergency equipment. Prerequisite: minimum grade of &quot;C&quot; in 1010 and 1011, completion of all 100-level English and Math courses, or instructor approval...', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142844, 963675, 'ZOOL', '113', 2020, 'Fundamentals of Anatomy and Physiology I Lab', 'A laboratory course to accompany 1014. Two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit with C or better or registration in 1014. Non-majors only. <br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 2211', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142845, 929698, 'BIOL', '241', 2020, 'Human Anatomy Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 2040. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisites: Cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher; \"C\" or better in 1020/1021 or 2026; credit or registration in 2040. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142846, 929698, 'BIOL', '2041', 2020, 'Human Anatomy Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 2040. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisites: Cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher; \"C\" or better in 1020/1021 or 2026; credit or registration in 2040. F', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142847, 186522, 'BIOL', '2010', 2020, 'Animal Diversity', 'The study of the biology, ecology, and evolutionary relationships of the major animal phyla. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory per week. Prerequisites: &quot;C: or better in BIOL 122, 123. (Formerly BIOL 208, 209)', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142848, 58291, 'ASCI', '201', 2020, 'Breeds of Livestock', 'The origin, history, and characteristics of leading breeds of livestock. Prerequisite: ASCI 101.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142849, 364725, 'BIOL', '1011', 2020, 'Human Biology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 110. Two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 110, or approval.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142850, 917099, 'BIOL', '2050', 2020, 'Economic Plants', 'The history and applied uses of plants as food, fibers, lumber, drugs, and related commodities. Prerequisites: C or better in 1001 or 1020, or instructor approval.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142851, 277469, 'BIOL', '220', 2020, 'Cell Biology', 'A survey of the structural and functional relationships operative at the cellular and molecular levels of organization. Prerequisites: \"c\" or better in BIOL 1020, 1021; CHEM 1008.<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 2133', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142852, 33304, 'BIOL', '440', 2020, 'Taxonomy of Vascular Plants', 'Characteristics of plant families are emphasized. This includes classification systems and emphasis on primitive and advanced characteristics. Most of the lab is devoted to identification of plants by using keys from plant identification manuals Two hours lecture and four hours laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 2004 or 2030.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142853, 810805, 'MICR', '201', 2020, 'Introductory Microbiology', 'The distribution and importance of microorganisms in nature. Methods of studying and controlling microorganisms. Their role in agriculture, industry and medicine. Prereq