iven to both classical and modern genetics. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in 1020, 1021; junior standing.\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CBIO 3523', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142864, 8990761, 'BIOL', '2030', 2020, 'Plant and Animal Form and Function', 'A detailed and systematic study of plant structure, growth, nutrition, transport, development, reproduction, animal nutrition, circulation, gas exchange, homeostatic mechanisms, chemical signaling, reproduction and development. Three hours lecture and two hours laboratory per week. Prerequisite: C or better in 1022, 1023.', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142866, 459356, 'CSCI', '373', 2020, 'Numerical Methods', 'Numerical algorithms fundamental to scientific work including discussion of error. Prerequisite: CSCI 2003 and MATH 2002 and 1032. (Dual listed as MATH 3073.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142867, 459356, 'CSCI', '3073', 2020, 'Numerical Methods', 'Numerical algorithms fundamental to scientific work including discussion of error. Prerequisite: CSCI 2003 and MATH 2002 and 1032. (Dual listed as MATH 3073.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142868, 4913754, 'TOXI', '4046', 2020, 'Industrial Hygiene for Safety Professionals', 'Industrial Hygiene for Safety Professionals is an introduction to industrial hygiene. Terminology, general principles, regulatory standards, workplace hazards, exposure evaluation methods, and control strategies will be discussed during the course.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 0.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142869, 484623, 'BIOL', '4004', 2020, 'Ecological Methods', 'Contemporary methods employed in plant and animal ecology. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 3002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142870, 484623, 'BIOL', '404', 2020, 'Ecological Methods', 'Contemporary methods employed in plant and animal ecology. Prerequisites: \"C\" or better in 3002.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142871, 395968, 'ART', '4045', 2020, 'Special Problems: Ceramics (Formerly ART 441B)', '3 credits per course. A maximum of 12 hours allowed toward the degree. Additional course fee may apply. (Formerly ART 441B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 12.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (142872, 364725, 'BIOL', '111', 2020, 'Human Biology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 110. Two hours laboratory. Prerequisite: Credit or registration in 110, or approval.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142873, 518731, 'BIOL', '411', 2020, 'Genetics and Society', 'A survey of current topics in genetic research and recent advances in biotechnology, including implications of these discoveries. Prerequisite: Biology 120 and either 305 or permission of the instructor.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142874, 395662, 'MCOM', '312', 2020, 'Broadcast Copywriting', 'Preparation of short-form copy for radio and television, including public service, advertising and promotional material, with emphasis on the relationship between writers and users of electronic media. Prerequisite: MCOM 210.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142875, 904048, 'BIOL', '320', 2020, 'Conservation Biology', 'A course dealing with biodiversity and its conservation. Topics include biodiversity, habitat loss, the effects of habitat changes on populations, and the design and establishment of reserves. Prerequisites: &quot;C&quot; or better in 1022, 1023.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142876, 635877, 'ANTG', '3008', 2020, 'Old World Archeology', 'A survey of the major archeological sequences of prehistoric Eurasia, Africa, and Oceania. (Same as GEOG 3008.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142877, 635877, 'ANTG', '308', 2020, 'Old World Archeology', 'A survey of the major archeological sequences of prehistoric Eurasia, Africa, and Oceania. (Same as GEOG 3008.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (142878, 941460, 'BIOL', '416', 2020, 'Physiology of Reproduction', 'Study of the physiological and environmental processes involved in mammalian reproduc