 problem solving. One hour lecture and five hours studio. Prerequisite: 273, or approval of department head. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144215, 70071, 'ENGL', '3004', 2020, 'Film Analysis and Criticism', 'Theories and practices in the analysis and criticism of film as an art form and an entertainment medium; evaluation of trends in film presentations. A fee is charged each student to defray expenses related to this course. Prerequisite: Junior standing. (Same as ENGL 304.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144216, 70071, 'MCOM', '473', 2020, 'Film Analysis and Criticism', 'Theories and practices in the analysis and criticism of film as an art form and an entertainment medium; evaluation of trends in film presentations. A fee is charged each student to defray expenses related to this course. Prerequisite: Junior standing. (Same as ENGL 304.)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144217, 686621, 'CLSC', '1000', 2020, 'Medical Application of Science for Health', 'This course is designed to facilitate academic enrichment in health care science and improve basic awareness of health care careers. This course is open to regular University students and to students who make application to and are accepted into the M*A*S*H program sponsored by the North Louisiana Area Health Education Center. F, Sp, Sum', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144218, 78448, 'CLSC', '433', 2020, 'Microbiology III-Practicum', 'Continuation of MLSC 4032. Advanced concepts in the use and interpretation of medical bacteriology, mycology, virology, and parasitology procedures and data. Practical application of clinical bateriology, mycology, virology, and parasitology knowledge and skills in a clinical laboratory setting. MLSC majors only. F, Sp (Formerly CLSC 433)', 4.0000, 4.0000, 4.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144219, 517491, 'CLSC', '450', 2020, 'Cooperative Education Experience', 'Planned and supervised work experience in students major field to include phlebotomy, patient relations, laboratory operations, and laboratory computers. Grades of A, B, C, and NC (No Credit) will be awarded. May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Students must work a minimum of 20 hrs./week and must be compensated by employer. F, Sp, Sum', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144220, 123427, 'ELED', '4041', 2020, 'Elementary Science Methodology', 'Techniques for organizing and teaching science at the lower and upper elementary school levels. Must be admitted to Teacher Education. Take during professional semester 3. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144221, 123427, 'ELED', '441', 2020, 'Elementary Science Methodology', 'Techniques for organizing and teaching science at the lower and upper elementary school levels. Must be admitted to Teacher Education. Take during professional semester 3. F, Sp', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144222, 536780, 'CLSC', '401', 2020, 'Advanced Laboratory Methods', 'Practical instruction and laboratory practice in the performance of laboratory techniques used in automation, quality control, flow cytometry, and molecular methods. MLSC majors only. Sp (Formerly CLSC 401)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144223, 536780, 'CLSC', '4001', 2020, 'Advanced Laboratory Methods', 'Practical instruction and laboratory practice in the performance of laboratory techniques used in automation, quality control, flow cytometry, and molecular methods. MLSC majors only. Sp (Formerly CLSC 401)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `courses` VALUES (144224, 474370, 'SCIE', '1004', 2020, 'Integrated Geosciences for Education Majors', 'The goal of this course is to present an integrated approach to essential concepts in introductory geology (physical and historical geology), astronomy (from an earth science perspective), and weather. Personal applications of science, the process skills, problem-solving, and discovery/inquiry learning are emphasized. For Elementary Education majors only. (Formerly SCIE 104)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144225, 637443, 'ATMS', '3004', 2020, 'Introduction to Atmospheric Kinematics and Dynamic', 'Vector operations in meterology, horizontal flow patterns, fundamental forces in the atmosphere, basic laws of conservation of momentum, mass and energy applied to the atmosphere. Prerequisites: 205, MATH 131.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144226, 637443, 'ATMS', '304', 2020, 'Introduction to Atmospheric Kinematics and Dynamic', 'Vector operations in meterology, horizontal flow patterns, fundamental forces in the atmosphere, basic laws of conservation of momentum, mass and energy applied to the atmosphere. Prerequisites: 205, MATH 131.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144227, 403904, 'MUSC', '2001', 2020, 'Basketball Pep Band', 'Entertainment ensemble for home basketball games. Group travels to conference tournament and postseason games. Prerequisite: Approval of the director. May be repeated.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144228, 403904, 'MUSC', '201', 2020, 'Basketball Pep Band', 'Entertainment ensemble for home basketball games. Group travels to conference tournament and postseason games. Prerequisite: Approval of the director. May be repeated.', 0.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144229, 837457, 'ENGL', '440', 2020, 'Graphic Presentation in Technical Communication', 'The theory, use, and creation of graphics and visuals in professional communication and documentation. Prerequisite: Registration in or completion of any upper-level writing course or permission of the department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144230, 837457, 'ENGL', '4040', 2020, 'Graphic Presentation in Technical Communication', 'The theory, use, and creation of graphics and visuals in professional communication and documentation. Prerequisite: Registration in or completion of any upper-level writing course or permission of the department head.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144231, 732563, 'COMM', '2009', 2020, 'Evidentiary Speaking', 'Engages students in Speech & Debate Forum public communication events as preparers, presenters and audience. May be repeated up to three credit hours. (Formerly CMST 1009)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144232, 732563, 'CMST', '1009', 2020, 'Evidentiary Speaking', 'Engages students in Speech & Debate Forum public communication events as preparers, presenters and audience. May be repeated up to three credit hours. (Formerly CMST 1009)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144233, 176860, 'THEA', '4093', 2020, 'Directed Study: Directing (Formerly 491B)', 'Directed study in Directing. May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144234, 176860, 'THEA', '4091B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Directing (Formerly 491B)', 'Directed study in Directing. May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144235, 176860, 'THEA', '491B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Directing (Formerly 491B)', 'Directed study in Directing. May be repeated for a total of 6 credits. Prerequisite: Approval of department head. (Formerly THEA 491B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144236, 474217, 'MCOM', '490', 2020, 'Internship', 'Field experience under the general supervision of a faculty member and the direct supervision of an industry professional, with academic components including a final paper and presentation. Prerequisites: Completion of 15 hours of Mass Communications coursework including MCOM 390 and approval of academic advisor, faculty internship supervisor and site supervisor.', 2.0000, 2.0000, 2.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144237, 120534, 'ENGL', '3023', 2020, 'Professional Writing and Communication: Arts, Hum., Soc. Sci.', '3 cr. Instruction in technical and professional writing and communication for arts, humanities, and social sciences. Emphasis on written and oral forms. Includes practice in documentation, collaboration, oral presentation, graphics and design, and research. Prerequisites: ENGL 1002; junior standing or permission of English Dept. Head; restricted to Arts and Sciences and Construction majors EXCEPTING biology, chemistry, geosciences, agriculture, and math majors. (Formerly ENGL 220B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144238, 120534, 'ENGL', '220C', 2020, 'Professional Writing and Communication: Arts, Hum., Soc. Sci.', '3 cr. Instruction in technical and professional writing and communication for arts, humanities, and social sciences. Emphasis on written and oral forms. Includes practice in documentation, collaboration, oral presentation, graphics and design, and research. Prerequisites: ENGL 1002; junior standing or permission of English Dept. Head; restricted to Arts and Sciences and Construction majors EXCEPTING biology, chemistry, geosciences, agriculture, and math majors. (Formerly ENGL 220B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144242, 120534, 'ENGL', '323', 2020, 'Professional Writing and Communication: Arts, Hum., Soc. Sci.', '3 cr. Instruction in technical and professional writing and communication for arts, humanities, and social sciences. Emphasis on written and oral forms. Includes practice in documentation, collaboration, oral presentation, graphics and design, and research. Prerequisites: ENGL 1002; junior standing or permission of English Dept. Head; restricted to Arts and Sciences and Construction majors EXCEPTING biology, chemistry, geosciences, agriculture, and math majors. (Formerly ENGL 220B)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144243, 255532, 'ENGL', '491', 2020, 'Advanced Fiction Writing', 'The writing of fiction, with emphasis on voice, style, and fictive worlds. Prerequisite: ENGL 3015 or approval of department head. Course may be taken twice for a maximum of 6 credit hours.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144244, 255532, 'ENGL', '4091', 2020, 'Advanced Fiction Writing', 'The writing of fiction, with emphasis on voice, style, and fictive worlds. Prerequisite: ENGL 3015 or approval of department head. Course may be taken twice for a maximum of 6 credit hours.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 6.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144245, 969255, 'ART', '418', 2020, 'Inclusive Art Instruction', 'A lecture/discussion/experience course designed to present art and education students with theories, strategies, and experiences in designing and teaching art activities. For juniors, seniors and graduate students only. Additional course fee .', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144246, 895323, 'CHEM', '107', 2020, 'General Chemistry I', 'A course in modern chemistry theories and principles; quantitative approach and problem solving; descriptive chemistry of selected elements and compounds. Three hours of lecture and one hour of recitation. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in MATH 1011 or 1013, or equivalent, or eligibility for MATH 1013 and completion of a Chemistry Placement Exam. F, Sp, Su1<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1123', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144247, 260112, 'CHEM', '1008', 2020, 'General Chemistry II', 'A continuation of CHEM 1007; continuation of theory with emphasis on chemical equilibria; a quantitative approach to solution chemistry; descriptive chemistry of selected elements and compounds from the main groups and the first transition series. Three hours of lecture and one hour of recitation. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 1007. F, Sp, Su2<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1133', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144248, 958710, 'CHEM', '104', 2020, 'Introductory Chemistry Laboratory II', 'A laboratory course to accompany CHEM 1002. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 1003 and registration or credit in CHEM 1002. For non-majors. Sp\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1111', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144249, 958710, 'CHEM', '1004', 2020, 'Introductory Chemistry Laboratory II', 'A laboratory course to accompany CHEM 1002. Three hours of laboratory. Prerequisite: \"C\" or better in CHEM 1003 and registration or credit in CHEM 1002. For non-majors. Sp\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\nLCCN: CCEM 1111', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144250, 30739, 'SPED', '3010', 2020, 'Behavior Support and Interventions', 'Methods and techniques for effective behavior management and classroom organization to meet the unique needs of diverse students with exceptionalities. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144252, 341302, 'SPED', '4020', 2020, 'Assessment and Evaluation for Special Learners', 'Develops assessment skills for instructional planning to meet the educational needs of diverse learners with mild/moderate disabilities. Addresses formal and informal assessments. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144253, 994364, 'SPED', '4025', 2020, 'Collaborative Teaming and Transition', 'Teaches secondary education majors to integrate reading, writing, speaking, and listening strategies and activities into adolescent reading instruction. Must be admitted to Teacher Education.', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144256, 524697, 'CLSC', '3022', 2020, 'Immunology', 'A course covering the principles of basic immunology and the application of clinical immunology in the medical laboratory to include: immunoglobulin structures; antigen- antibody reactions, classification, mechanisms, and clinical characteristics of immune disease; transplantation and tumor immunology; and a study of various serological testing procedures and interpretation and correlation of test results with disease states. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 322)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144257, 268460, 'CLSC', '201', 2020, 'Medical Laboratory Principles and Methods', 'A laboratory course to instruct students in the principles of medical laboratory science and basic laboratory techniques including proper use of the medical microscope, pipetting techniques, blood and microscopic slide preparation, use of the spectrophotometer, safety and infection control techniques, proper use of personal protective equipment, venipuncture, hematocrit, and proper identification and cells and microorganism with the microscope. MLSC majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144258, 268460, 'CLSC', '2001', 2020, 'Medical Laboratory Principles and Methods', 'A laboratory course to instruct students in the principles of medical laboratory science and basic laboratory techniques including proper use of the medical microscope, pipetting techniques, blood and microscopic slide preparation, use of the spectrophotometer, safety and infection control techniques, proper use of personal protective equipment, venipuncture, hematocrit, and proper identification and cells and microorganism with the microscope. MLSC majors only.', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144260, 139736, 'CLSC', '3020', 2020, 'Hematology', 'A study of hematopoiesis, classification, mechanisms and clinical characteristics of the anemias, leukemias, lymphomas, and other related diseases; the mechanism and specific disorders of hemostasis and a study of the principles of various hematological testing procedures and interpretations and correlation of test results with disease states. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 320 and CLSC 100)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144261, 853023, 'MLSC', '3021', 2020, 'Hematology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 320 to include procedures for a complete blood count, sedimentation rate, L.E. prep, osmotic fragility, sickle cell testing, coagulation testing, various miscellaneous tests and quality control procedures. Three hours laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 321)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144262, 853023, 'CLSC', '3021', 2020, 'Hematology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 320 to include procedures for a complete blood count, sedimentation rate, L.E. prep, osmotic fragility, sickle cell testing, coagulation testing, various miscellaneous tests and quality control procedures. Three hours laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 321)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144263, 853023, 'CLSC', '321', 2020, 'Hematology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 320 to include procedures for a complete blood count, sedimentation rate, L.E. prep, osmotic fragility, sickle cell testing, coagulation testing, various miscellaneous tests and quality control procedures. Three hours laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 321)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144264, 677165, 'CLSC', '338B', 2020, 'Directed Study: Hematology (Formerly CLSC 338B)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems in Hematology. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338B)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144265, 677165, 'CLSC', '3042', 2020, 'Directed Study: Hematology (Formerly CLSC 338B)', '1-6 credits. Individual investigation of selected problems in Hematology. MLSC majors only. Prerequisites: Approval of the Program Director. F, Sp, Sum (Formerly CLSC 338B)', 1.0000, 6.0000, 6.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144266, 712461, 'CLSC', '3023', 2020, 'Serology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 3022 to include representative tests of all types of serological testing performed in the clinical laboratory. Three hour laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. (Formerly CLSC 323)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144267, 712461, 'CLSC', '323', 2020, 'Serology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 3022 to include representative tests of all types of serological testing performed in the clinical laboratory. Three hour laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. (Formerly CLSC 323)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144268, 926814, 'CLSC', '3024', 2020, 'Clinical Chemistry and Toxicology', 'Study of physiologic limits and composition of various body fluids and their methods of analysis. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. F (Formerly CLSC 324)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144269, 249183, 'CLSC', '3025', 2020, 'Clinical Chemistry and Toxicology Laboratory', 'A laboratory course to accompany 3024 including qualitative and quantitative analysis of physiologic components and composition of the various components of blood and other body fluids and methods of analysis for toxic substances. Three hours laboratory. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp (Formerly CLSC 325)', 1.0000, 1.0000, 1.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144270, 273131, 'CLSC', '326', 2020, 'Clinical Chemistry and Toxicology', 'Principles of basic clinical chemistry and toxicology procedures applied to enzymes; endocrine function; electrolytes and blood gases; renal function; gastric, pancreatic and intestine function; biochemistry of pregnancy; therapeutic drug monitoring and analysis of toxic substances. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. (Same as Toxicology 3026.) Sp (Formerly CLSC 326)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144271, 273131, 'CLSC', '3026', 2020, 'Clinical Chemistry and Toxicology', 'Principles of basic clinical chemistry and toxicology procedures applied to enzymes; endocrine function; electrolytes and blood gases; renal function; gastric, pancreatic and intestine function; biochemistry of pregnancy; therapeutic drug monitoring and analysis of toxic substances. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. (Same as Toxicology 3026.) Sp (Formerly CLSC 326)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144272, 14211, 'MLSC', '3027', 2020, 'Immunohematology and Blood Banking', 'A course in the genetic theory of the human blood groups and the administrative and technical operation of blood banks. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp (Formerly CLSC 327)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 0, NULL, 0, 0), (144273, 14211, 'CLSC', '3027', 2020, 'Immunohematology and Blood Banking', 'A course in the genetic theory of the human blood groups and the administrative and technical operation of blood banks. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp (Formerly CLSC 327)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144274, 14211, 'CLSC', '327', 2020, 'Immunohematology and Blood Banking', 'A course in the genetic theory of the human blood groups and the administrative and technical operation of blood banks. Three hours lecture. MLSC majors only. Prerequisite: Approval of the Program Director. Sp (Formerly CLSC 327)', 3.0000, 3.0000, 3.0000, 1, NULL, 0, 0), (144275, 237810, 'CLSC', '328', 2020, 'Technical Procedures in Blood Banking', 'A laboratory course to accompany 3027, giving practical experience in pretransfusion compatibility testing and basic antibody identification and an introduction to donor screening and component 